{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist","id":338242,"title":"Lunar Wishlist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-12T12:21:47-08:00","id":338242,"title":"Lunar Wishlist","content":"Starting with a number of things I'd like Lunars to be able to do with familiars:<ul><li>Automatically gain a familiar's Hearts Blood, just by having the familiar bond with the animal in question. The Heart's Blood is kept constantly fresh by the bond, you don't need to keep making &quot;back up&quot; save files every time you think your familiar might die soon.<ul><li>Treat a familiar's shape as one of your true forms, for as long as the familiar lives.<ul><li>Gain a second war form based on a familiar's shape, for as long the familiar lives.</li> <li>Gain a false Tell based on the familiar's shape, to mask your true Tell?</li> <li>Possibly one of multiple routes to Chimerahood?</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Gain Heart's Blood through a familiar's actions.</li> <li>Give a familiar human intelligence.<ul><li>Give familiar a war form and true human form of their own.</li> <li>Give familiar access to your True Forms.<ul><li>Give familiar access to your Heart's Blood library.</li> <li>Give familiar Lunar Charms?</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>See through familiar's eyes<ul><li>Act through the familiar, using your Abilities (and Attributes, where appropriate)<ul><li>Using your own or the familiar's Attributes as you please, with shapeshifting <i>making </i>anything appropriate.<ul><li>Exchange locations with your familiar by the two of you shapeshifting into each other, with necessary range and difficulty restrictions.</li> </ul></li> <li>Use your Charms through familiar.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Make your familiar a Chimera.</li> <li>Share health, Willpower and mote pools with your familiar and vice-versa</li> <li>Split off your Spirit Shape to act as a familiar, locking out your Spirit Shape and DBT for the duration; the subdivision is only as smart as a natural beast of that species would be, or only as smart as you could make a familar with the intelligence-increasing Charm. The death of this creature would be crippling if not fatal.</li> <li>Split off your birth form to act as a familiar, locking out your human form and DBT for the duration. Prerequires the ability to give a familiar human intelligence, with the subdivision of you being only as intelligent as the &quot;familiar intelligence&quot; Charm would allow. Same death penalty.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-25-2015, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:23:24-08:00","id":338264,"title":"","content":"I want a power that lets you automatically count as performing a Sacred Hunt on anyone presently hunting <i>you</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:24:54-08:00","id":338266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338264#post338264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a power that lets you automatically count as performing a Sacred Hunt on anyone presently hunting <i>you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wiggling with joy at the thought. Good idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:39:26-08:00","id":338274,"title":"","content":"Quick question as to the original post: what's the advantage of a True Form aside from something like Formlock, which we hope/assume is thoroughly buried alive after being tortured at this point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:48:18-08:00","id":338276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338274#post338274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question as to the original post: what's the advantage of a True Form aside from something like Formlock, which we hope/assume is thoroughly buried alive after being tortured at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Form lock should surely die in a fire as is foretold, but that's not the only disadvantage to false forms.<br /> <br /> The mote cost of assuming it, for sure. Probably how easily or poorly it hides your Tell. As well as other features we can't know about until we see how much Lunar Heart's Blood shapeshifting has or hasn't changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and your Spirit Shape's Attribute ratings probably should count against your dice-adding limit, but again, we don't know what they're going to do to balance out Totems, so we don't know if that would even matter as an advantage of true forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:50:14-08:00","id":338278,"title":"","content":"An ability that lets you gift other people a portion of your bestial strength by feeding them some of your blood would be kinda cool. Lunars don't feel like the type who would train followers, but bestowing them with strength like that does feel appropriate. This could be applied to familiars too.<br /> <br /> Also, and this one might be a stretch, but an actual, proper shapeshifting mechanic would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:57:17-08:00","id":338282,"title":"","content":"- Madness associated powers (associated with the moon in many cultures)<br /> - Social &amp; Teaching Charms that work off of wielding riddles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:00:07-08:00","id":338283,"title":"","content":"For starters, Heart's Blood needs to be reworked entirely. Depending on the ST, it might be pointlessly easy to &quot;find a superlative example of the animal he wishes to hunt, chase the animal to the ground and slay it at the climax of the hunt,&quot; or downright impossible if you're not playing a Lunar with hunting skills. Also, I don't see why Luna should have the power to arbitrarily veto your hunts.<br /> <br /> I believe there should be more ways to acquire the shape of a creature besides personally hunting it down and eating it - in particular, I think it would be great if a Lunar could take on the shapes of other creatures by wearing their skins, and that there might be some benefit to carrying around the hides of everything you kill.<br /> <br /> Luna should have more consistent relationships her chosen. The writers seem to waffle on how much influence she has - apparently she directly appears to every new chosen, and she slept with at least one, and she can validate or invalidate Sacred Hunts, but she doesn't offer them any other kind of help, advice, or direction. I think she should either be more fully involved with the Lunars' lives, or not involved at all.<br /> <br /> Other combat options for Lunars should be equal in stature to the Warform Monsters stand we have now.<br /> <br /> Lunars should not be wyld-tainted by default.<br /> <br /> The Tell should not come with a mind-control compulsion to ignore it, and the rules should be clearer about whether the Tell is something obvious or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-12-2014, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:00:12-08:00","id":338284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338278#post338278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ability that lets you gift other people a portion of your bestial strength by feeding them some of your blood would be kinda cool. Lunars don't feel like the type who would train followers, but bestowing them with strength like that does feel appropriate. This could be applied to familiars too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding others your blood to change their forms into shapes from your Heart's Blood library would certainly be an appropriate extension of Lunar Heart's Blood shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> It's too early to say whether or not Lunar Charms are incapable of supplementing training methods that Lunars might employ. We still really don't have a good idea of how the more cerebral Lunar Charm Charms are supposed to look or work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, and this one might be a stretch, but an actual, proper shapeshifting mechanic would be nice. </div> </div> </div>We're getting actual, proper mechanics and stats for beasts this time, because this time animals are being designed with the idea that Exalted will wear their forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:01:38-08:00","id":338286,"title":"","content":"I'd sure like to be able to make a Tanuki themed Lunar, complete with turning into inanimate objects, and transforming leaves into fake money. Remote transformation would also be cool, swapping places by into an object (&quot;poof, it was just a log you cut&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:03:12-08:00","id":338288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338278#post338278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ability that lets you gift other people a portion of your bestial strength by feeding them some of your blood would be kinda cool. Lunars don't feel like the type who would train followers, but bestowing them with strength like that does feel appropriate. This could be applied to familiars too.<br /> <br /> Also, and this one might be a stretch, but an actual, proper shapeshifting mechanic would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Take this, all of you, and drink from it: this is the cup of my blood, the blood of the new and everlasting covenant. It will be shed for you and for all so that you can all be <i>hella strong.</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:12:33-08:00","id":338312,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338283#post338283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars should not be wyld-tainted by default.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Corollary: lose the Fair Folk Charm acquisition. This isn't pre-1st edition, the two aren't intertwined anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:14:08-08:00","id":338313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338282#post338282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Madness associated powers (associated with the moon in many cultures)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure we're going to get &quot;I go insane&quot; Charms, but I'd also love to get &quot;I drive <i>others </i>insane&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Social &amp; Teaching Charms that work off of wielding riddles </div> </div> </div>Social Charms that work off Blood Oaths would also be cool.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338286#post338286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd sure like to be able to make a Tanuki themed Lunar, complete with turning into inanimate objects, and transforming leaves into fake money. Remote transformation would also be cool, swapping places by into an object (&quot;poof, it was just a log you cut&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you can carve a symbol into a rock or log, fill the symbol with your blood,,, and by drawing the same bloody symbol onto another object later, cause the two objects to exchange locations by shapeshifting. Lunar theft!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:15:25-08:00","id":338316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338283#post338283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna should have more consistent relationships her chosen. The writers seem to waffle on how much influence she has - apparently she directly appears to every new chosen, and she slept with at least one, and she can validate or invalidate Sacred Hunts, but she doesn't offer them and other kind of help, advice, or direction. I think she should either be more fully involved with the Lunars' lives, or not involved at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Luna. Consistency.<br /> <br /> Luna.<br /> Consistency.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no matter how hard I try, those two words don't look right together.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:19:38-08:00","id":338346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338316#post338316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna. Consistency.<br /> <br /> Luna.<br /> Consistency.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no matter how hard I try, those two words don't look right together.</div> </div> </div> </div> She doesn't have to behave the same way around every Chosen, but you also shouldn't have to do a d% roll to determine how the Lunar's patron god acts in any given situation.<br /> <br /> Being a mercurial shapeshifter shouldn't mean you have to be Chaotic Stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:26:05-08:00","id":338350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338283#post338283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there should be more ways to acquire the shape of a creature besides personally hunting it down and eating it</div> </div> </div> </div>Hatewheel intends to cater to you and others who feel the same. There was a thread where he asked people to share their ideas for alternative methods.<br /> <br /> Sex is almost definitely returning. I dearly hope &quot;beating someone in a contest or game, even when they don't know the privacy of their face is at stake&quot; makes an appearance. Letting someone <i>gift </i>you their Heart's Blood through a Blood Oath would also be cool.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's my idea for gaining Heart's Blood through the actions of your familiars. So you can send your pet wolf to hunt something or someone down for you... or you can pimp your woman-formed wolf out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in particular, I think it would be great if a Lunar could take on the shapes of other creatures by wearing their skins, and that there might be some benefit to carrying around the hides of everything you kill. </div> </div> </div>Hatewheel believes that either a form exists in your Library for real, or not at all.<br /> <br /> But wearing something's hide <i>to treat it as a true form</i> would be pretty cool! Thanks for that inspiration!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Luna should have more consistent relationships her chosen </div> </div> </div>This would require Luna to be <i>consistent</i>. Luna the Many-Faced, Goddess or God of Madness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other combat options for Lunars should be equal in stature to the Warform Monsters stand we have now. </div> </div> </div>That's what Evocations are for. Lunar Deadly Beastman Transformation is being balanced against Evocations, so that they are mutually appealing paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars should not be wyld-tainted by default. </div> </div> </div>No fear of that. Lunars aren't going to be tied to the edges of the world, this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tell should not come with a mind-control compulsion to ignore it, and the rules should be clearer about whether the Tell is something obvious or not. </div> </div> </div>The I believe the devs have spoken specifically about how hiding the Tell from Integrity didn't work as well as hiding it from Awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:31:01-08:00","id":338353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338288#post338288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Take this, all of you, and drink from it: this is the cup of my blood, the blood of the new and everlasting covenant. It will be shed for you and for all so that you can all be <i>hella strong.</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With this and Vance's &quot;Hella Snake Prana&quot;, I do believe that the Lunars have a lot of strongholds in northern California.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're getting actual, proper mechanics and stats for beasts this time, because this time animals are being designed with the idea that Exalted will wear their forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am well aware, I was just kidding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:33:16-08:00","id":338354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338350#post338350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would require Luna to be <i>consistent</i>. Luna the Many-Faced, Goddess or God of Madness.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are numerous gods of madness in real mythology and in fiction. Many of them behave in ways that are actually pretty understandable and even predictable, once you understand their idiosyncrasies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:37:55-08:00","id":338357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338312#post338312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corollary: lose the Fair Folk Charm acquisition. This isn't pre-1st edition, the two aren't intertwined anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that should also die in a fire.<br /> <br /> I mean, I would still like Lunars swear magical oaths, but their own Charms can do that. Likewise, they can make their own magical tools without Ring Graces, cast their own spells without Cup Graces or raksha Fantasies, and command terrible beasts without Sword Graces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:42:22-08:00","id":338361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338354#post338354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are numerous gods of madness in real mythology and in fiction. Many of them behave in ways that are actually pretty understandable and even predictable, once you understand their idiosyncrasies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, some Storytellers and players want more Luna in their stories, and others want less.<br /> <br /> Luna consistently does interact with her Chosen at their Second Breath, but she's a very flexible deity who spends as much time with a particular Lunar as she feels that individual Lunar merits.<br /> <br /> She is not a &quot;one-size-fits-all standard&quot; kind of Lady.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:44:01-08:00","id":338363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338316#post338316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna. Consistency.<br /> <br /> Luna.<br /> Consistency.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no matter how hard I try, those two words don't look right together.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between &quot;Luna is predictable&quot; and &quot;Luna can arbitrarily dick over your Sacred Hunt for the lulz.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338350#post338350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The I believe the devs have spoken specifically about how hiding the Tell from Integrity didn't work as well as hiding it from Awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I mean this was clear during 2e. The Tell tried to get real cutesy with the new (terrible) social mechanics and the result was an overcomplicated mess that didn't work well, let alone as-intended. It <i>always</i> should have been based off of an extremely-difficult-even-for-Solars Perception + Awareness test.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:52:21-08:00","id":338369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338361#post338361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, some Storytellers and players want more Luna in their stories, and others want less.<br /> <br /> Luna consistently does interact with her Chosen at their Second Breath, but she's a very flexible deity who spends as much time with a particular Lunar as she feels that individual Lunar merits.<br /> <br /> She is not a &quot;one-size-fits-all standard&quot; kind of Lady.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's so, then let the book spell it out. Right now, Luna's role seems to be to make cameos in people's backstories and then justify some of the Lunar mechanics by standing in for ST fiat (&quot;Luna says you can't Sacred Hunt a mosquito, because that would break the game and/or you don't have the knacks to transform into one of those&quot;). That's kind of an awkward position for any character to be in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:56:04-08:00","id":338371,"title":"","content":"Anyone familiar with the <i>Monster Hunter</i> franchise?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.techdollogic.com/rf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However Lunar crafting Charms compare to those of other Exalted, I want Lunars to have <i>superhuman facility</i> with turning the trophies of their hunts into functioning, durable weapons and armor. Trophies from slain demons, elementals and gods should also be valid targets, especially for crafting artifact gear.<br /> <br /> This works hand-in-hand with the desire for a Charm that lets you wearing an animal's hide so that you can treat the creature as a True Form, like your Spirit Shape. Perhaps even to assume a war form based on that creature, to the extent that the creature resembled an animal or had an alternative, bestial form.<br /> <br /> Like, I could turn a Solar's skull into a helmet, and if he had a Lion Icon for his anima banner, I could assume a Lion war form. (And now you have a special reason to hunt down the First and Forsaken Lion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-12-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:56:58-08:00","id":338373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338346#post338346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She doesn't have to behave the same way around every Chosen, but you also shouldn't have to do a d% roll to determine how the Lunar's patron god acts in any given situation.<br /> <br /> Being a mercurial shapeshifter shouldn't mean you have to be Chaotic Stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it means she'll behave as the Storyteller requires for that specific story - not in some predetermined way set by canon. If she has a very helpful with a Lunar PC, great that's consistent with canon. If she completely ignores a Lunar PC, great that's consistent with canon. If she has an almost antagonist role because she's forcing the given character to adapt-or-die, great that's consistent with canon. If she only communicates through strange enigmas only the wisest can decipher, great that's consistent with canon. She does whatever serves the given story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:03:58-08:00","id":338396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338373#post338373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She does whatever serves the given story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what all characters are supposed to do?<br /> <br /> In Luna's case, deliberately leaving canon vague so you can fill in whatever you like in the blank would be best accomplished by saying <i>nothing</i> about how she relates to her chosen. Otherwise, I see no reason not to give her a motivation, goals, and means of pursuing those goals like everyone else.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I am not saying that Luna should be the same thing to everyone. I'm saying that I don't like the way she is presented now, and that making her either a more active character or a less active character would be preferable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:04:04-08:00","id":338398,"title":"","content":"I want to be able to make a fucking awesome lair, especially with Lunar dominions becoming more widespread. <br /> <br /> Actually, I'm going to go ponder that for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:09:45-08:00","id":338401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338396#post338396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what all characters are supposed to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters who are less mercurial than her would be breaking from canon with certain portrayals (not that breaking from canon is inherently a bad thing of course), with Luna canon is that she is an ever-shifting mesh of diverse aspects, so she can be suddenly very active, or very distant and it be consistent with her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:10:17-08:00","id":338402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338398#post338398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be able to make a fucking awesome lair, especially with Lunar dominions becoming more widespread.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm going to go ponder that for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Elswhere Dens probably won't return in the same form, I can easily imagine Lunar Charms letting you create a TARDIS effect whereby your lair is bigger on the inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:17:25-08:00","id":338407,"title":"","content":"Going back to crafting and lair Charms, I want Lunars to have the power to create stuff that inspires pants-wetting terror or tunnel-vision desire in anyone who beholds them.<br /> <br /> Piss in the woods? The smell terrifies people into fleeing my territory.<br /> <br /> Gouge my claw marks into someone's door? They decide to leave their land.<br /> <br /> Carve an effigy borderstone? No one passes through that way.<br /> <br /> Create a den? Only the bravest of warriors will dare to enter.<br /> <br /> Scar my emissary? No dude is man enough to fuck with him, at least or especially when he is on my business.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the same token, I can bait traps with objects people see and must have, cook meals that draw man for miles around as the smell carries on the wind, prepare lairs that seem welcoming and homey, or simply leave a careless trail of clothes leading to the bedroom which even the most principle Dragon-Blooded officer can't resist.<br /> <br /> Or for giggles, I make a golden ring that people murder each other to own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:38:02-08:00","id":338444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338283#post338283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars should not be wyld-tainted by default.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well define wyld-tainted. I recall a major element to Lunars is change. They were one thing during the Primordial War, another in the First Age, and something different in the Age of Sorrows. A part of this major change is having their exaltation altered and by Wyld essence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:43:33-08:00","id":338446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338371#post338371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone familiar with the <i>Monster Hunter</i> franchise?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.techdollogic.com/rf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However Lunar crafting Charms compare to those of other Exalted, I want Lunars to have <i>superhuman facility</i> with turning the trophies of their hunts into functioning, durable weapons and armor. Trophies from slain demons, elementals and gods should also be valid targets, especially for crafting artifact gear.<br /> <br /> This works hand-in-hand with the desire for a Charm that lets you wearing an animal's hide so that you can treat the creature as a True Form, like your Spirit Shape. Perhaps even to assume a war form based on that creature, to the extent that the creature resembled an animal or had an alternative, bestial form.<br /> <br /> Like, I could turn a Solar's skull into a helmet, and if he had a Lion Icon for his anima banner, I could assume a Lion war form. (And now you have a special reason to hunt down the First and Forsaken Lion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a post a while ago that one of a Lunar's major strengths is using the shapes and powers of their enemies against them. Your post follows this idea in a less shapeshifting way which is interesting. Literally ripping and making crap from your enemies to fight your enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:44:24-08:00","id":338447,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like DBT to be more of a purpose-built warform that you use specifically to kill stuff. I never liked how many auxiliary benefits got attached to it, because it felt like it diluted it to be used for things other than Ultimate Fighting Mode. I'd rather just see the sorts of non-killy DBT effects Lunars have had in the past be available through other means, if they're going to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:52:35-08:00","id":338455,"title":"","content":"I'd like Lunar Wits to be exciting and dynamic and really embody fast thinking, cleverness, trickery...not just a mismatch of kitchen-sink utility effects and Dex copypasta. <br /> <br /> Of course this requires Wits to have a strong definition and occupy a distinct thematic space...the overlap with Intelligence (fast thinking) and Manipulation (trickery) is definitely problematic.<br /> <br /> I think looking at what Scion's Epic Wits could do would be instructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:03:29-08:00","id":338486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338447#post338447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like DBT to be more of a purpose-built warform that you use specifically to kill stuff. I never liked how many auxiliary benefits got attached to it, because it felt like it diluted it to be used for things other than Ultimate Fighting Mode. I'd rather just see the sorts of non-killy DBT effects Lunars have had in the past be available through other means, if they're going to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've contemplated Deadly Beastman Transformation gaining the effects of Solar Battle Fury Focus, so that you HAVE to fight if you're wearing the form... which means you can't use the form unless you want to start a fight.<br /> <br /> Is that something like what you're thinking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:05:18-08:00","id":338488,"title":"","content":"I'd just really like to have an edition where people don't bitch incessantly about them. Anything else is incidental.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately even <i>not having</i> them wouldn't guarantee that, as then people would complain about there not being Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:48:36-08:00","id":338520,"title":"","content":"I want an official word on what happens when I sire or bear a child in the form of a demon, elemental, Dragon-Blood, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Do I get a Demon-Blooded, a mortal, a Lunar half-caste, what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:02:26-08:00","id":338526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338353#post338353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this and Vance's &quot;Hella Snake Prana&quot;, I do believe that the Lunars have a lot of strongholds in northern California.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also considered using 'wicked strong' instead, in case you prefer your lunars on a different coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:04:52-08:00","id":338528,"title":"","content":"OH MAN, I just remembered perhaps the biggest bugbear I had with Second Edition Lunars.<br /> <br /> I want to properly take Heart's Blood from something I kill, even if I don't yet have the Knacks or Charms or whatever for actually using that Heart's Blood to assume its form.<br /> <br /> I do NOT want to kill something right now and miss out on its Heart's Blood FOREVER because I won't have the appropriate knack for at least a few more sessions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Think about how lame it would be if Ligier the Green Sun was permanently slain for all time by a Lunar Exalted with Spirit-Maiming Essence Attack, but because he spent his XP on combat Charms like that one, he didn't have Green Sun Child, and now NO ONE has or ever can have Ligier's form.<br /> <br /> <br /> This problem is especially annoying given that assuming a creature's shape with a particular Knack isn't the only reason to take that creature's Heart's Blood! Towering Beast Shape is meant to make Lunars pay for the advantage of assuming giant shapes, but sometimes I just really want to know what someone else knows, and for that I can use Charms like Lessons in the Blood.<br /> <br /> I should be able to use Charms like Lessons in the Blood on anything whose heart I've eaten, even if I can't physically assume that creature's form. Let No Moons have some fun, dammit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:20:51-08:00","id":338553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338528#post338528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about how lame it would be if Ligier the Green Sun was permanently slain for all time by a Lunar Exalted with Spirit-Maiming Essence Attack, but because he spent his XP on combat Charms like that one, he didn't have Green Sun Child, and now NO ONE has or ever can have Ligier's form.</div> </div> </div> </div>About as lame as the fact that he'll never be able to forge anything from his unique talents ever again.<br /> <br /> That killing something means there's a certain degree of diminishment seems not only perfectly in keeping with the general themes of the game, as well as basically logical.<br /> <br /> Hell, considering what Lunars are doing to the Realm and the Sidereals, it would seem that they're all over the idea that sometimes you break something so that nobody can ever use it again. If a given Lunar has a problem with that, maybe hold off on breaking something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:26:38-08:00","id":338554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338283#post338283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna should have more consistent relationships her chosen. The writers seem to waffle on how much influence she has - apparently she directly appears to every new chosen, and she slept with at least one, and she can validate or invalidate Sacred Hunts, but she doesn't offer them any other kind of help, advice, or direction. I think she should either be more fully involved with the Lunars' lives, or not involved at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a matter of consistency, just degree. I mean, if one wants to argue on the basis that she should step forward or back, then fine, but make that argument rather than the implicitly more hostile one of &quot;the writers can't maintain a party line&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is also the first I'm hearing of Luna having anything to do with Sacred Hunts, beyond being an in-character explanation of the process to the same degree as, say, the Sidereal Charm to see the future that includes the idea of certain gods who go around gathering evidence of disasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:39:50-08:00","id":338558,"title":"","content":"Apart from the usual statements of &quot;no formlock&quot;, &quot;get rid of the tattoo-hiding tax&quot; and &quot;make their history something other than 750 years of failure and irrelevance&quot;, there is a small one--I'd like to see tattoo artifacts stay. Always liked that concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:50:49-08:00","id":338611,"title":"","content":"I am ambivalent about Lunars at best, but...<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to be the &quot;Moon Chosen&quot; Exalt, instead of the &quot;Animal fucking, shitting in the woods and marking my territory via piss&quot; Exalted.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to to be able to stand on their own merits, instead of everyone trying to bring them in to parity with Solars, making them just Silver Solars.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to have Meerkat Steals the Spotlight Prana as an actual Charm.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars as presented to us in 3E to be accepted by fans of Lunars (hahahaha yeah right, wishful thinking)<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to have a coherent theme and strong pace in the world of Exalted, instead of just &quot;those guys who sat over there while everything important happened&quot;<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to compare and contrast well with Solars and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to have Attribute powers, filtered through the lens of the moon, not animal powers filtered through the lens of &quot;fuck civilization! rawr!&quot;.<br /> <br /> I want Lunar Exaltation shards to change over time in response to external pressures by way of pulp evolution/adaptation, rather than &quot;Fuck you, Wyld corruption is a go!&quot;<br /> <br /> I want a Solar Lunar bond that's high risk, high reward for both parties involved.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars who don't feel pressured in to investing in Shapeshifting, can can go their whole lives without taking a different form even once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:56:01-08:00","id":338613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338558#post338558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from the usual statements of &quot;no formlock&quot;, &quot;get rid of the tattoo-hiding tax&quot; and &quot;make their history something other than 750 years of failure and irrelevance&quot;, there is a small one--I'd like to see tattoo artifacts stay. Always liked that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corollary: allow Tattoo Artifact stuff to be added after chargen as desired. Needing to buy it all up-front really sucked. <br /> <br /> And Tattoo Artifact Evocations.......mmmmm........<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:13:10-08:00","id":338623,"title":"","content":"I want a Charm that turns my immediate personal space into an environmental hazard zone for enemies.<br /> <br /> When they get close enough, my hair becomes snakes, my tail becomes an independently moving scorpion's barb, my cloak becomes the beating, bone-breaking wings of a swan, crows fly out of my sleeves, rats boil up from my shadow... Whatever manifestation best fits my character, that pestilence befalls my foes when they approach me.<br /> <br /> A bit more creatively flexible than the old Snake Head Defense... and mechanically simpler.<br /> <br /> An upgrade would allow me to sic this plague of beasts upon distance enemies, a la Thousandfold Wasp Dance, at the cost of denying me the protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:14:53-08:00","id":338625,"title":"","content":"One thing that I find interesting is that there's quite a lot of things that people say they want from Lunars which I think &quot;uh, no, definitely not, that ruins the whole point of them.&quot; And other people do seem to argue about it too.<br /> I think people can't agree what they want from Lunars, and that's possibly why it's difficult to come up with strong themes for them. I mean, they have two strong themes: shapeshifting, and animals. And some people seem to dislike that? If you take that away, they have very little left.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll try and keep this list from getting too long:<br /> <br /> I absolutely do not want Lunars to lose their animal theme. Reskin it, move it around, change how it works, whatever, but I absolutely should still be able to take an animal, think about it's mythic tropes and physical abilities, and build a Lunar off it, because in my experience more than half of the most iconic, memorable characters I've seen played in Celestial games are built this way.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I want them to have at least the option of having a true form/totem. Some people say they don't want it. I wouldn't be massively upset if it's not compulsory, but it absolutely must be there as an option.<br /> <br /> I want to be able to gain the forms of powerful creatures I defeat in combat and eat the hearts of, but didn't actually hunt for hours and hours beforehand. For example, if I run into a behemoth or a second-circle demon and get into a really difficult fight but win.<br /> Honestly, the whole Sacred Hunt needs rethinking. I don't mean the concept of getting shapes by eating hearts, I mean what happens before it. The issue is that it seems mostly written for hunting down a kind of animal, ie &quot;I want a dog shape&quot; rather than &quot;I want that dog right there&quot;. Which gets very awkward with the shapes of demons, elementals, behemoths, etc. I mean, you're not going to hunt down a superlative example of a behemoth because there's only one.<br /> <br /> I want there to be a lot more Int and Wits charms, and the Wits charm not to be a copy of Dex charms.<br /> <br /> I want something similar to Chimerism to be there, as in the horrific mutated monster kind of Lunar. It could be like 1st ed with having multiple true forms that mix together, or something new. I don't want all Lunars to be hideous body-horror abominations, but I'd like some to be able to (what I mean is, I want the mutated Lunar I'm playing to be able to go down this route, while the hot fox girl that's also in the party to not have to).<br /> <br /> <i>'</i>I'd like the theme of savage bestial horror (insanity, eating people's hearts, fucking animals) to still be there with some Lunars, but it doesn't have to be there for all Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'd like for there to be very, very few Lunar charms that are just Solar charms that have been nerfed a bit. I mean, excellencies is okay, but not much more beyond that.<br /> <br /> I'd like for not every Lunar to have to get silver tats. I mean, silver magic tattoos is cool (though I wish they didn't always have to look the same) but it's not so cool when 99% of Lunars have them, it becomes rather bland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:24:09-08:00","id":338630,"title":"","content":"I want Lunars to curse their enemies by transforming them into animals.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to curse Dynasts with lycanthropy. We're told that Lunars aren't going to be built around the werewolf story of fearing the full moon and involuntarily losing control of the inner beast, but I want Lunars to be able to inflict that fate on their enemies. Teach them to fear the sight of the moon in the sky, and wrack them with the taste for the flesh and blood of their fellows. Punish their hedonism by blurring the lines between sexual lust and literal hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-12-2014, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:35:07-08:00","id":338633,"title":"","content":"Oh, something I've considered before, about shapeshifting:<br /> For some concepts, having a ton of animal shapes doesn't make sense. For others, it does. But the thing is, those shapes are free, xp-wise. So, if, for example, you're playing a vegeterian Monk (as one of my players did) you're stuck with just your true form. Now, that player loved turning into an elephant (his totem) but didn't seem that bothered by not being able to turn into a ton of other things, because they'd fit his character concept less anyway. But he was essentially depowering his character just for fluff.<br /> Consider if, say, you play a vampire-themed Lunar. Your totem is vampire bat, you come from a Carpathia-esque region, you can turn into this bat, a wolf, a big black dog maybe... it doesn't really fit the concept that you turn into, say, a parrot. Or a monkey. Or an old woman.<br /> One poster earlier said he didn't want Lunars to be &quot;pressured into shapeshifting&quot;.<br /> Another thing is that if you start with a bunch of forms, you have to buy the Heart's Blood Library background, but if you get them in game you don't have to pay (unless you have an ST that makes you pay XP for all backgrounds, which is an optional rule that most people don't use).<br /> At the same time, the sacred hunt itself can be awkward, in terms of the time, which can end up with you, say, spending 6 hours hunting the dog that lives next door because that's the dog you want.<br /> <br /> My answer: scrap the sacred hunt. You still have to eat your target (or sleep with them with the upgrade charm, and I imagine the new book will add some new options: I kind of like the idea one poster had about wearing the skins). But you don't have to hunt them for hours an hours, unless that is actually required to find your target (which it generally, in practice, actually isn't).<br /> But! To get the form you have to pay 1xp.<br /> After all, more forms is really useful. But it doesn't fit every character. As I said, this would also mean that the rules for getting the forms could be relaxed without the worry that Lunars would just go into a pet shop and grab 30 new forms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:41:33-08:00","id":338635,"title":"","content":"What do I want from Lunars... I know this way seem weird and counter to what they've said? But I kind of want martial arts, or charms in general that come from mimicking animals. Y'know, the idea of emulating animals to learn martial arts is a dang classic idea. I mean sure they don't want, 'Everything is based on animals with lunar charms' but at the same time? I had this idea for a Lunars rewrite before I heard that 3e was nigh (See: After New Year's, before winter ends estimation). Basically, two facets to Lunars for learning tricks. 'The Gaian Dance' for learning anything shapeshifting/animal related (Walking among, learning from the mystic qualities people attributed to animals like an owl's status as a harbinger of doom and a symbol of wisdom both, maybe like omen reading from owls) and, 'The Lunar Dance' for anything self-related like most traditional charms. The basic idea was to have aspects you could equip, but learning too many would trigger their brand of the Great Curse: Losing themselves in all the forms and qualities they collected, and chimerism being the ultimate and final form of the Curse itself. Not to say that Moonsilver tattoos stopped the Great Curse, just that it prevented it from accelerating crazy fast. Also helped solve the weirdness that was, 'Limit, despite being a function of the Great Curse, defined chimerism' in the Lunars book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":". 12-12-2014, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:04:07-08:00","id":338643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338630#post338630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Lunars to curse their enemies by transforming them into animals.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to curse Dynasts with lycanthropy. We're told that Lunars aren't going to be built around the werewolf story of fearing the full moon and involuntarily losing control of the inner beast, but I want Lunars to be able to inflict that fate on their enemies. Teach them to fear the sight of the moon in the sky, and wrack them with the taste for the flesh and blood of their fellows. Punish their hedonism by blurring the lines between sexual lust and literal hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a Punishment Rite in Werewolf: the Dark Ages, incidentally. The Garou stopped using it on account of how it was a blatant veil breach as more and more potential witnesses started crowding the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:26:24-08:00","id":338655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338288#post338288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Take this, all of you, and drink from it: this is the cup of my blood, the blood of the new and everlasting covenant. It will be shed for you and for all so that you can all be <i>hella strong.</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but visualize this being said by Wonderella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:47:21-08:00","id":338682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338633#post338633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some concepts, having a ton of animal shapes doesn't make sense. For others, it does. But the thing is, those shapes are free, xp-wise. So, if, for example, you're playing a vegeterian Monk (as one of my players did) you're stuck with just your true form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a Knack that allow you to only beat your target into unconsciousness so you can gain their form without eating anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T21:05:58-08:00","id":338685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338407#post338407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or for giggles, I make a golden ring that people murder each other to own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a silver apple that makes the closest of boon companions fall out!<br /> <br /> How about smearing your blood on the doorway of your allies, having the effect of Warding their homes from Creatures of the Wyld/Darkness?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T21:30:02-08:00","id":338694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338682#post338682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a Knack that allow you to only beat your target into unconsciousness so you can gain their form without eating anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have trouble fully embracing that Knack.<br /> <br /> The default method for gaining Heart's Blood is violence. The advanced options are completely different: Sex, and games of skill or chance.<br /> <br /> I don't think I can really accept a method which is just &quot;violence, but less violent&quot;. I rather think that if you resort to violence at all, you should need to go the whole way and kill the victim.<br /> <br /> Because if you could ever resort to violence without killing, why should you ever kill again? The killing becomes wasteful rather than meaningful, and I don't want the killing of the violent method to become pointless.<br /> <br /> At the very least, a violent but non-lethal method should be much, much harder than killing the victim. Harder than battering someone into unconsciousness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338685#post338685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a silver apple that makes the closest of boon companions fall out!</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the apple of discord was also golden?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about smearing your blood on the doorway of your allies, having the effect of Warding their homes from Creatures of the Wyld/Darkness? </div> </div> </div>Just the same basic application of the &quot;fear&quot; effect I mentioned in the same post, though upgraded to exclude your allies, and perhaps to exert greater influence upon Creation's enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T22:28:19-08:00","id":338726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338407#post338407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scar my emissary? No dude is man enough to fuck with him, at least or especially when he is on my business.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*thinks of Lion King*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T22:34:18-08:00","id":338729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there is a Knack that allow you to only beat your target into unconsciousness so you can gain their form without eating anything. </div> </div> </div>There is now, though not at the time this was an issue (as it's in one of the 2.5 things, much later). But beating the shit out of a man to get his form is still not very monk-like (and honestly, I don't think it fits. The point of both eating people's hearts, or the upgrade for getting it through sex, is that you've taken part of them inside yourself and thus internalised their form. Beating them up doesn't do that.<br /> But anyway, that's off the point. My point was, my Lunar has about 50 forms, but that's not thematically appropriate for many Lunars. Think of mythic shapeshifters. Most switch between 1 human and 1 animal form. They might sometimes have 3 or 4. They generally do not have 50. Unless they can literally turn into animal at all, or something.<br /> Now, of course, if you play a Lunar based on, say, a werewolf (which is the most stereotypical example I can think of, and I doubt many would play it because it's so incredibly stereotypical, but it serves to illustrate this point), you can turn into a human, a wolf, and perhaps a half-wolf monster man (or lady). You could just not learn any other forms. But, since those forms are free, you are clearly limiting your power for your backstory. Now, normally (assuming charms are balanced, which honestly they're not always) you don't lose much from not buying stuff that doesn't fit your character, because you can spend xp on other things. But because learning new forms costs no xp whatsoever, you have literally gained nothing at all by not picking up a ton of different animal forms.<br /> <br /> Also, since apparently many of the animal forms are going to come with unique skills that make them even more mechanically useful for Lunars (which is of course a good thing, because in the old rules it was rather odd the way that, RAW, turning into a horse didn't actually make you any faster), it would be even more appropriate for Lunars to pay a small amount of xp for each form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-13-2014, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T23:19:16-08:00","id":338768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338655#post338655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't help but visualize this being said by Wonderella.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that Dragon King in the illustration for the Coagulated Eucharist Dark Path...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T23:28:34-08:00","id":338769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338729#post338729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because learning new forms costs no xp whatsoever, you have literally gained nothing at all by not picking up a ton of different animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part concerns me as well, but we will have to wait and see.<br /> <br /> It's possible that &quot;growth through experiences as well as XP&quot; may become the general model for Lunar Exalted, especially if the devs draw inspiration from how the Garou and Uratha of the Worlds of Darkness must learn their powers from spirits.<br /> <br /> That is, perhaps a Lunar buys a Charm, and the Charm gains additional effects (or any effect at all only) when a Lunar has formed some kind of bond with a spirit. Like a Stamina Charm that grants additional soak with the blessing of an Earth elemental or related god, and heat resistance with the blessing of a fiery spirit.<br /> <br /> Even aside from that, the Scorpion and Toad Charms only worked with substances and sicknesses the Lunar had previously suffered, allowing the Lunar to gain immunities and produce ailments without paying for each malady.<br /> <br /> <br /> For a peak into the possible relationship between spirits and Lunars, an excerpt from <i>Masters of Jade</i>:<br /> <br /> More recently, the Southeastern Tea and Mercantile<br /> Company, a Guild trading interest, began the complete<br /> massacre of indigenous peoples in the Blackwater region<br /> of the Maruto River. The people cried out in pain and<br /> misery to their ancestors, whose ghosts in turn called out<br /> to the wind, the trees and the wild, crying for the end of<br /> their tribe, and praying for a champion who would stand<br /> against the monsters who had come to their land. Their<br /> prayer was answered by a Lunar called Ghost Wolf, who<br /> drove back the agents and the soldiers of Southeastern<br /> Tea and Mercantile, breaking their dams, flooding their<br /> camps and dragging their men down into the murky<br /> waters of the swamps to be eaten by things which dwell<br /> in the dark. Empowered by the prayers of the river tribes,<br /> Ghost Wolf was able to transform himself into a variety<br /> of horrific guardian totems in order to terrorize the Guild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T02:25:45-08:00","id":338908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338371#post338371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone familiar with the <i>Monster Hunter</i> franchise?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.techdollogic.com/rf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However Lunar crafting Charms compare to those of other Exalted, I want Lunars to have <i>superhuman facility</i> with turning the trophies of their hunts into functioning, durable weapons and armor. Trophies from slain demons, elementals and gods should also be valid targets, especially for crafting artifact gear.<br /> <br /> This works hand-in-hand with the desire for a Charm that lets you wearing an animal's hide so that you can treat the creature as a True Form, like your Spirit Shape. Perhaps even to assume a war form based on that creature, to the extent that the creature resembled an animal or had an alternative, bestial form.<br /> <br /> Like, I could turn a Solar's skull into a helmet, and if he had a Lion Icon for his anima banner, I could assume a Lion war form. (And now you have a special reason to hunt down the First and Forsaken Lion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted in general, not just Lunars, should have a lot more &quot;Cloak sewn from the skins of the mighty beast I've felled&quot; and a lot less &quot;shiny Saint Seiya spike pauldrons&quot;, far as I'm concerned :P.<br /> <br /> Granted, I already do Monster Hunter stuff as craftable stuff as is. A sword crafted from the tooth of a mighty elemental dragon is way more memorable than a sword crafted out of a chunk of soulsteel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 12-13-2014, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T04:56:37-08:00","id":338959,"title":"","content":"...Hot dang man. That is AWESOME armor. That having been said, Reminiscent Oasis brewed up a Mardukth charmset with a trick that used something similar. +(Essence) successes on making armor out of beasts you've killed, and +(Essence) soak from said armor, be it mundane or artifact. They also get a secondary trick to shunt damage onto it, using HLs as though the armor piece was still retaining its living HLs. But it manifests as clothing damage which is a tad weird in my mind. I'd sooner say, &quot;This turns it increasingly dead looking, from leather to a half-rotting, vaguely fossilized plate&quot; or something. The charm basically said, &quot;Any wound penalties the armor takes manifest as mobility penalties.&quot; which makes sense, personally. They do roughly the same thing, anyway.<br /> <br /> (Also the mass of snakes effect I -think- Morke or TDO mentioned sounds awesome as all get-out. More of that, please!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":". 12-13-2014, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T09:38:18-08:00","id":339150,"title":"","content":"I want crazy HypnoToad eyes as a social Charm superior to the mutation of the same inspiration.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the mutation, I also want the hypnotic voice version as a Charm.<br /> <br /> We should already be assured of a Charm for producing mental-influence smells/pheromones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T09:46:54-08:00","id":339159,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely not the best person to add to this list. I've never played as a Lunar, and never had one in a game I ran (as a player or NPC). I've only ever seen my brother use one in a game that a friend ran, and he definitely didn't use his character in any way that could be construed as &quot;creative&quot;. He mostly just beat people senseless... when he wasn't mauling them! Needless to say, my knowledge of Lunars and their charms is very limited.<br /> I always thought it'd be cool if Lunars could harness nature for themselves. Exert influence over large groups of animals. Perhaps turn a group of animals related to your totem all into familiars. Someone mentioned providing blood to people to empower them. What about doing something similar with that familiar pack of animals. Imagine a Lion-totem Lunar with a group of supernaturally bolstered Lions as his bodyguards/familiars. Perhaps they don't need to be tied to a totem, and you can just claim a &quot;group/pack&quot; as your familiars. I'm thinking of something akin to the Beastmaster movies, where all animals can be made your allies. Some can even be bolstered via other charms giving you several familiars. Not sure if something like this exists, if it does, I'd have more inclination to play a Lunar in 3E. While shapechanging is cooling, being able to command the beasts of the wild is something I find very appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T09:50:47-08:00","id":339164,"title":"","content":"Weird glitch in posting to this thread...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338694#post338694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the apple of discord was also golden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick research shows that, yes, that's right! Damn, why did I think it was silver...?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really, the things I liked best about the Lunar charmset, that stood out to me as being the most original to them, are things that the devs say are going away, like the Illusion/Delusion effects. Outside of &quot;Silver Solar&quot; basic powers and shapeshifting, there's not much left, besides using bodily fluids/parts as foci for magical effects and animal control powers. <br /> <br /> I do want to see Lunars able to gain multiple Familiars. Why should Sidereals get all that fun? But should Lunars be able to evolve theirs into spirits as well, or is that too out-of-theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:17:35-08:00","id":339194,"title":"","content":"I want Lunars to have the option of using their Spirit Shape as a war form, rather than a hybrid shape.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to be able to extend that power-up to their familiars as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:35:59-08:00","id":339216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338486#post338486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've contemplated Deadly Beastman Transformation gaining the effects of Solar Battle Fury Focus, so that you HAVE to fight if you're wearing the form... which means you can't use the form unless you want to start a fight.<br /> <br /> Is that something like what you're thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this would be cool. Of course, it entails offloading some of the things currently associate with DBT to other powers, but I think it would help make DBT feel more hype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:38:30-08:00","id":339217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339194#post339194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Lunars to have the option of using their Spirit Shape as a war form, rather than a hybrid shape.<br /> <br /> I want Lunars to be able to extend that power-up to their familiars as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>By analogy, do you mean...if their spirit shape is Lupus, you want them to have Hispo as a war form, instead of Crinos?<br /> <br /> I'm down with that. Dire elephants ahoy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:46:56-08:00","id":339222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339217#post339217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By analogy, do you mean...if their spirit shape is Lupus, you want them to have Hispo as a war form, instead of Crinos?</div> </div> </div> </div>As an alternative to Crinos, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Particularly for someone who chooses a primate for a Totem. A gorilla is already so humanoid, why bother with a war form? Just make the gorilla form nastier when you need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:07:47-08:00","id":339364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338959#post338959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Hot dang man. That is AWESOME armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monster Hunter armor is generally very cool, silly, or both. <br /> <br /> I was going to start posting images but it'd flood the page too much, so instead, here, take a look yourself: <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/uYJ59\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/a/uYJ59</a>. Some Monster Hunter armor artwork. And I won't even get into the weapons. <br /> <br /> A personal favorite: this little number weaved from the skin of an Air Elemental Dragon.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/3hKdfLa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T14:49:51-08:00","id":339469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339217#post339217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By analogy, do you mean...if their spirit shape is Lupus, you want them to have Hispo as a war form, instead of Crinos?<br /> <br /> I'm down with that. <b>Dire</b> elephants ahoy!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dire&quot;, monster! Your term doesn't belong in this setting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T15:19:13-08:00","id":339476,"title":"","content":"Well, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_wolf\" target=\"_blank\">depending on how you use it.</a>. Although I'm pretty sure we already have what are functionally dire elephants up North. Which... does lead itself back into a point about how one of the Garou/Uratha forms is more than just a wolf with extra scary attachments, and doesn't entirely work in a setting where some prehistoric fauna continues to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:13:57-08:00","id":339526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339476#post339476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_wolf\" target=\"_blank\">depending on how you use it.</a>. Although I'm pretty sure we already have what are functionally dire elephants up North. Which... does lead itself back into a point about how one of the Garou/Uratha forms is more than just a wolf with extra scary attachments, and doesn't entirely work in a setting where some prehistoric fauna continues to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will note that in the article you cited, there is a description of a critter not at all like what D&amp;D uses to describe something under the same name. Much like D&amp;D's take on the &quot;sea lion&quot;, only not quite as insane*. Dire is not a synonym for giant unless you are playing D&amp;D or its derivatives. I've been taking W20 to task about this for describing Hispo in this manner for some time now. Seriously, only the Pure Tribes would have had even the slightest inkling that dire wolves ever existed, thanks to geography and timing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*And the Gorgons are called Medusas, while the Catoblepas is called a Gorgon!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:20:13-08:00","id":339531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339526#post339526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Gorgons are called Medusas, while the Catoblepas is called a Gorgon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do people always say that? Pliny referred to them as &quot;gorgons,&quot; also, even if he was most likely just evoking it to mean &quot;a thing which turns other things to stone.&quot; It's a valid transliteration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T17:37:27-08:00","id":339587,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D's catoblepas is called a catoblepas. It's in either Fiend Folio or Monster Manual II.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:16:56-08:00","id":339621,"title":"","content":"I kind of hope that the Changing Moon full-flare anima effect won't be the same &quot;hide my identity&quot; effect as the Solar Night Caste gets. I realize that Lunar essence is sneakier on the whole than Solar essence, but it's the sort of effect that could be a Charm for any Lunars to learn (indeed, we got such a Charm last edition) and the Changing Moon Caste are the persuasive speakers of the Host. It would be nice if their full-bore anima effect would help with that.<br /> <br /> Especially if they retain the already-identity-concealing power of looking like someone not already in their Heart's Blood library. Though perhaps that effect is the better half to ditch in terms of a persuasion-enhancing power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:45:24-08:00","id":339637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338908#post338908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted in general, not just Lunars, should have a lot more &quot;Cloak sewn from the skins of the mighty beast I've felled&quot; and a lot less &quot;shiny Saint Seiya spike pauldrons&quot;, far as I'm concerned :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the game should have rewards especially for Lunars when they play to the visual archetype of the tattooed, fur-clad barbarian, just as Sidereals have incentives to avoid armor and carry around fancy strips of paper signed with beautiful calligraphy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:58:09-08:00","id":339644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339637#post339637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the game should have rewards especially for Lunars when they play to the visual archetype of the tattooed, fur-clad barbarian,</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what? I guess I tend to view DBT as the reward for that visual archetype you mentioned. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339637#post339637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just as Sidereals have incentives to avoid armor and carry around fancy strips of paper signed with beautiful calligraphy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I would very much like for Sidereals to have incentives to wear armor without totally screwing themselves over power-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:18:34-08:00","id":339657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339637#post339637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the game should have rewards especially for Lunars when they play to the visual archetype of the tattooed, fur-clad barbarian, just as Sidereals have incentives to avoid armor and carry around fancy strips of paper signed with beautiful calligraphy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing with Sidereals is they're bureaucratic secret agent fate ninjas. Stylistically they don't have incentives to wear armor for the same reason James Bond doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:23:55-08:00","id":339662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339657#post339657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the thing with Sidereals is they're bureaucratic secret agent fate ninjas. Stylistically they don't have incentives to wear armor for the same reason James Bond doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals always being worse off by wearing armor is too thematically constraining for me. A Chosen of Battles wearing superheavy plate should either be provided with some armored MAs to choose from or have a good native combat tree, because pigeonholing everyone as a ninja in combat is boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T20:47:07-08:00","id":339710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339662#post339662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals always being worse off by wearing armor is too thematically constraining for me. A Chosen of Battles wearing superheavy plate should either be provided with some armored MAs to choose from or have a good native combat tree, because pigeonholing everyone as a ninja in combat is boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, and if we gonna do that to Sid then it's only fair that every other splat should get the same stupid restriction too, I hope Solar enjoy having to spend BP on superheavy armor at chargen huh duh :'P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T00:09:10-08:00","id":339805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339662#post339662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals always being worse off by wearing armor is too thematically constraining for me. A Chosen of Battles wearing superheavy plate should either be provided with some armored MAs to choose from or have a good native combat tree, because pigeonholing everyone as a ninja in combat is boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note to self, Sidereal Martial Art involving armor. Silver Fortess of Unassailability Style or something along those lines...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T00:47:15-08:00","id":339816,"title":"","content":"Thing is, I'm inclined to agree with Godjaw on this one. Styles are important, like turning into a hellbeast (Devil-Tyrant Avatar Shintai) with ALL the mutations vs. a badass killing beast with +1, or even +2 to your physical attributes (Deadly Beastman Transformation). One speaks to something WRONG but powerful and more than a bit twisted, the other to a primal powerhouse. Give a siddie superheavy plate and something has gone FUBAR. Not saying it's NOT possible, but it's like Iron Man in hulkbuster armor. It's not what you'll be seeing 90% of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:17:22-08:00","id":339829,"title":"","content":"I wish to be able to create a character with a spirit shape of 'Very Large Whale', and to use soak charms and bird transformations to make 'Dropping myself on people/ships/small neighborhoods' a valid tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:22:02-08:00","id":339832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339637#post339637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the game should have rewards especially for Lunars when they play to the visual archetype of the tattooed, fur-clad barbarian, just as Sidereals have incentives to avoid armor and carry around fancy strips of paper signed with beautiful calligraphy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, indeed. Personally, what I did was give Lunars a Craft enhancer for stuff built out of beast parts that was better the bigger and badder the beast in question was. The idea was to make it plain easier for a Lunar to go around clad in the scales of a Rathian than a solid chunk of magical metal. That way I felt I was giving a subtle nudge towards the monster hunter paradigm through making it the path of least resistance, without penalizing the people who <i>wanted </i>to go around looking like a Silver Saint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339805#post339805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self, Sidereal Martial Art involving armor. Silver Fortess of Unassailability Style or something along those lines...</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time ago I was working on a Super Robot-inspired COURAGE (in Exalted, Valor) SMA, which obviously allowed for heavy armors and warstriders. But making good SMAs that are thematic, nonboring, and nonbroken is <i>hard </i>x_x","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 12-14-2014, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:30:40-08:00","id":339837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339832#post339832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some time ago I was working on a Super Robot-inspired COURAGE (in Exalted, Valor) SMA, which obviously allowed for heavy armors and warstriders. But making good SMAs that are thematic, nonboring, and nonbroken is <i>hard </i>x_x</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, assuming that 3e is as good as the devs claim it is, that should hopefully change.<br /> Now how does one make 'being an unconquerable fortress of silver' into something evocative...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:43:48-08:00","id":340061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339816#post339816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give a siddie superheavy plate and something has gone FUBAR. Not saying it's NOT possible, but it's like Iron Man in hulkbuster armor. It's not what you'll be seeing 90% of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not advocating all Sids suddenly wearing superheavy plate as the ideal situation. However it's important that Sids belonging to that 10% (versus your 90% ninja) are not hugely gimped from the get-go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:57:47-08:00","id":340077,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't even peg it at 10% honestly - especially if it's artifact armor; then again, I would say that most <i>Exalts</i> in Ex3 won't have artifact armor, considering how much more rare artifacts in general are being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:51:21-08:00","id":340129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340077#post340077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't even peg it at 10% honestly - especially if it's artifact armor; then again, I would say that most <i>Exalts</i> in Ex3 won't have artifact armor, considering how much more rare artifacts in general are being made.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you agree that if someone has that as their concept for whatever reason, they shouldn't be punished for it in the rules, Y/N?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:56:36-08:00","id":340165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340129#post340129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you agree that if someone has that as their concept for whatever reason, they shouldn't be punished for it in the rules, Y/N?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are being specifically designed so that &quot;weapons rather than war forms&quot; is a competitive and appealing development path for them. Like Drascin, I don't want to prevent Lunars from wearing moonsilver plate armor so much as give them another viable option (and one that can actually be combined with moonsilver armor, like in the picture I posted.)<br /> <br /> But just as war forms and Evocations can't be used together, traditionally SMA and lots of lesser Styles have been incompatible with plate armor. That's not likely to change. Yet at the same time, there are Styles which allow full armor, and Sidereal Melee, Brawl, Archery and Thrown don't care about armor at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T12:07:38-08:00","id":340169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340165#post340165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just as war forms and Evocations can't be used together, traditionally SMA and lots of lesser Styles have been incompatible with plate armor. That's not likely to change. Yet at the same time, there are Styles which allow full armor, and Sidereal Melee, Brawl, Archery and Thrown don't care about armor at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm fine with SMA being mostly out of reach barring custom armor Evocations on stratal that might skirt that restriction. The main thing is for Sidereal native combat Charms to feel competitive with CMA. Which, last ed...some did, some did not (Thrown I recall being full of truly redundant effects that didn't combine well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T12:53:39-08:00","id":340180,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be interesting to have a kind of especially enraged warform or beast form which was difficult to control, but unimaginably dangerous. Kind of like if you're a gigantic burly dude who's also a werewolf. You can fight off ten other guys in your human form, but when an army of fey goblins come swarming towards the town you can transform into a monster from the primordial wild of the world, the kind of fanged, clawed, furred beast that spawns legends around campfires and keeps people awake at night. The kind of predator that stalks you even in your dreams and makes you wake in a cold sweat, desperately hoping that low growl was just in your head and not prowling outside your door.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be all war forms or all transformations, but I definitely think there should be an option to become an unfettered hunter of all things. I'm not sure how you'd do it properly, obviously just putting in a clause to kill everything friend or foe is bad in a million ways, but it could maybe have some danger to it. Like if you had a peony blossom alike you couldn't exclude people from it, and you couldn't pull your blows at all, If you choose to unleash that thing inside you the only way the scene is going to end is you drenched in blood while kneeling on a giant pile of bodies, screaming your victory to the sky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340165#post340165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just as war forms and Evocations can't be used together, traditionally SMA and lots of lesser Styles have been incompatible with plate armor. That's not likely to change. Yet at the same time, there are Styles which allow full armor, and Sidereal Melee, Brawl, Archery and Thrown don't care about armor at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There should definitely be an option to wear armor, but Sidereals more than anyone should be given pathways that allow them to get away with not wearing it. Kind of like how Dragonblooded don't have any resistance charms that are incompatible with armor or that have enough boosted soak to replace armor. DBs, in general, need armor. They don't always always have it, but it's a damn good idea and it helps give them a certain look, if somebody mentions a DB you can expect that if they're smart they'll be running around in some kind of armor, and if somebody mentions a Sidereal you can expect them to be wearing anything but...and still kick your ass harder for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T18:14:34-08:00","id":340305,"title":"","content":"new thought:<br /> <br /> I think it would be appropriate if Heart's Blood Library is re-christened Heart's Blood <i>Veins</i>.<br /> <br /> Think about it. Which sounds more natural for a Lunar to say, &quot;I've taken its blood into my Library&quot;, or &quot;I've taken its blood into my veins.&quot;?<br /> <br /> Are libraries of dusty books more evocative of Barbarian Werewolf Demigods than veins of hot, coursing blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T18:23:28-08:00","id":340311,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Library&quot; is purely an OOC construct used as a point of reference, not something that would remotely be mentioned IC.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've taken its blood into my veins&quot; sounds extremely appropriate as an IC statement though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-14-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T19:43:25-08:00","id":340372,"title":"","content":"I imagine they probably refer to it by a variety of names.<br /> Lunars are only semi-organised, so there's probably a lot of variation in the terms they use.<br /> It might be &quot;Library&quot; in claw-speak though, because &quot;Library&quot; probably made more sense back when they decadent aristocrats in a more advanced society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:23:25-08:00","id":340525,"title":"","content":"&quot;Storage&quot; or &quot;Collection&quot; might be valid terms. What/where do hunters keep the trophies of their kills?<br /> <br /> Also: Should Claw-Speak be kept? Is it too &quot;Werewolf&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:34:47-08:00","id":340531,"title":"","content":"As a language that Lunars can write when in a variety of animal forms, it does make a lot of sense. I have a Lunar that was never properly trained by the Silver Pact, so he doesn't know clawspeak, and honestly it'd be really useful if I could so I didn't have to activate Dog-Tongue Method all the time (which costs a WP).<br /> <br /> I would say though, about the tattoos: IIRC, they're Clawspeak of the Lunar's name and achievements. But that's like President Obama having tattoos that say &quot;I became Mayor of Chicago&quot;. Lunars get their tats pretty early in their careers. I'd much rather, as runes of mystic power, they were incantations to Luna and other Gods, mudras of stability, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-15-2014, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:43:35-08:00","id":340539,"title":"","content":"That being said, I like the Ogham-like appearance of clawspeak in the First Edition book. Kind of sad they sorta just stopped using it randomly in the 2e stuff, even if there were other design elements I thought were neat in the Lunars book aesthetically.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:50:30-08:00","id":340545,"title":"","content":"Should we return to how, in early 1E, Lunars from each Direction had their own style of moonsilver tats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T01:00:11-08:00","id":340659,"title":"","content":"I think that would be good. I think it'd be pretty cool, for example, to have a viking Lunar covered in futhark rune-esque tattoos for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T01:18:29-08:00","id":340664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340659#post340659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that would be good. I think it'd be pretty cool, for example, to have a viking Lunar covered in futhark rune-esque tattoos for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Lunars from the west go around with Maori-style shoulder/arm (or face) tattoos? Because I could really dig that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 12-15-2014, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T02:40:00-08:00","id":340676,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me.<br /> Honestly though, I'd be happy for it to be even more specific than direction-wide. I mean, it might not be culturally appropriate for all westerners to have Maori-esque tats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T02:56:42-08:00","id":340680,"title":"","content":"...Hm. Interesting idea, but I'm kind of questioning the idea of a unified lunar culture vs lunars with the cultural disparity of solars. I've understood it as, 'Moonsilver tattoos look the way they do because they're a product of the lunar collaboration' and that the mystic power intrinsic in them is a function of a degree of homogeneous design. I mean if it were as simple as, 'Tattoo some moonsilver on, BAM! You're good to go.' then I think the chimera problem would be somewhat less prevalent.<br /> <br /> Let me be a bit more clear though. I'm not against the idea of personal decorations, even as they apply to tattoos. Not every bit has to have mystic significance, and there IS some leeway as demonstrated by tattoo artifacts. It's just that when you get down to it, it seems like it vaguely (But only vaguely, not that substantially) cheapens the idea of moonsilver tattoos as a big accomplishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T03:07:03-08:00","id":340683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340305#post340305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are libraries of dusty books more evocative of Barbarian Werewolf Demigods than veins of hot, coursing blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idiomatically referring to acquisition of a new form like that might work, but the idea of people using the term &quot;veins&quot; to refer to a storage of their own blood just strikes me as silly, as well as clunky language.<br /> <br /> It gives me an image of a circulatory system that has been removed from a dissected subject and is spread out on a table in some kind of medical museum.<br /> <br /> I think Library serves as a term for an abstract storage of alternative forms, at least for out of character terms. In character, I don't think anybody is referring to having a Library of forms or a vein of forms or anything like that; they just <i>have</i> those forms. &quot;Person of ten thousand faces&quot;, not &quot;Person with library/veins of ten thousand faces&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:18:38-08:00","id":340786,"title":"","content":"Indeed, most of them probably just say &quot;I know 33 different forms&quot;. Except maybe the Crossroads Society, because those guys are pretentious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:26:35-08:00","id":340787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340786#post340786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, most of them probably just say &quot;I know 33 different forms&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking it's more natural to their image to say that they <u>have</u> multiple forms rather than <u>know</u> multiple forms.<br /> <br /> Even if it's implicit to the Lunar condition that the forms you have, outside the one you were born with and the one that is iconic of you, were &quot;stolen&quot; for some value of that term.<br /> <br /> On a related note, even if they'll go for some novelties in possibilities of rearrangement of Charm cascades to reference the spirit shape, my main attachment to that idea is in the feeling that Lunars are based around a cultural and literary milieu that is more focused on the idea of turning into/having a dual nature with a particular thing, rather than the somewhat more modern idea of being a more amorphous shapeshifter. Lunars are more than werewolves, but they capture some of what is supposed to be evocative about such figures in how they turn into a wolf, rather than turn into a variety of things that happens to include a wolf. Such non-specific shapeshifters aren't necessarily inferior, but they wouldn't feel so &quot;Lunar&quot; to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:47:45-08:00","id":340797,"title":"","content":"Or alternatively &quot;I've <i>taken</i> three-and-thirty forms.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T09:14:53-08:00","id":340858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still trying to figure out why &quot;Prototype&quot; is considered poor inspiration for a lunar, just because Alex/James are &quot;Shoggoth&quot; like shapeshifters or &quot;Rubbermen&quot;... which they're not.<br /> <br /> [Various reasons]</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong on any of this, but it's less that it's a bad inspiration in terms of theme, but terms of aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Lunar powers aren't really about turning your arm into a giant fleshy swordthing, or turning people into bombs by infecting them, or create an explosion of impaling tentacles.<br /> They draw from more mythological themes, and less biological ones, as the devs say, Alex and James have kind of shoggoth-y powers, which is not what they intend the Lunars to be.<br /> <br /> That does raise the question, would an Exalted splat with that particular aesthetic work, and if so, what would they be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T09:45:12-08:00","id":340894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340858#post340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong on any of this, but it's less that it's a bad inspiration in terms of theme, but terms of aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Lunar powers aren't really about turning your arm into a giant fleshy swordthing, or turning people into bombs by infecting them, or create an explosion of impaling tentacles.<br /> They draw from more mythological themes, and less biological ones, as the devs say, Alex and James have kind of shoggoth-y powers, which is not what they intend the Lunars to be.<br /> <br /> That does raise the question, would an Exalted splat with that particular aesthetic work, and if so, what would they be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Infernal has Kimbery and Metagaos, both of them has flesh-manipulation and assimilation as their theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:11:51-08:00","id":340915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340894#post340894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Infernal has Kimbery and Metagaos, both of them have flesh-manipulation and assimilation as their theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of them. That said, neither of them really have 'turn your hand into a giant fleshy swordthing' yet, cool as that would be.<br /> Actually, it sounds kind of like a Liminal thing. Altough, I don't really know much about what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:33:58-08:00","id":340926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340915#post340915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't thought of them. That said, neither of them really have 'turn your hand into a giant fleshy swordthing' yet, cool as that would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Revlid's Metagaos can let you do exactly just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:15:56-08:00","id":341004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340858#post340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong on any of this, but it's less that it's a bad inspiration in terms of theme, but terms of aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Lunar powers aren't really about turning your arm into a giant fleshy swordthing, or turning people into bombs by infecting them, or create an explosion of impaling tentacles.<br /> They draw from more mythological themes, and less biological ones, as the devs say, Alex and James have kind of shoggoth-y powers, which is not what they intend the Lunars to be.<br /> <br /> That does raise the question, would an Exalted splat with that particular aesthetic work, and if so, what would they be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see some Infernals working like that? I mean, if they're keeping the idea of power which makes you more inhuman (Basphomy in Verdigris* has those horns, for instance), but getting rid of the idea that Infernal Charms are statements about the Yozis, and not the Infernal themself, then Alex's abilities could be some subset of Infernal Melee, Resistance, and Stealth. And he certainly fits the idea that Infernals are all about &quot;casual power&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, I dunno that the line between mythic shapeshifters and &quot;shoggoths&quot; is as bright as the devs seem to think. Hindu demons and Journet to the West characters use their shapeshifting powers for all kinds of insane heavy metal album cover tricks which would seem outright <i>silly</i> beside even the most outrageous rubber man. Growing into an X00-foot-tall monstrosity with X heads and X^2 arms or having your blood turn into monsters is just the beginning! For example, Sun Wukong can use either his blood or his hair to change an object, allowing to take any one of his 72 forms, and then proceed to take any action he wills. Is there any reason that a PC with the power couldn't trick someone into swallowing said blood hair first, then have a Yeddim rip out of that person's stomach? That only differs from Alex Mercer turning you into a bomb in visual aesthetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Am I the only one who suspects that her name was chosen solely to screw with people by always making them want to read/type/say &quot;blasphemy&quot; instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:24:06-08:00","id":341012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340915#post340915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't thought of them. That said, neither of them really have 'turn your hand into a giant fleshy swordthing' yet, cool as that would be..</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a charm, but the fact that Infernals have easy access to an Infernal Artifact to do exactly that may indicate that it IS considered well within their themes...<br /> <br /> Oh, there's also the Malfeas Shintai that allows you to assume any physical Mutations at will, which can easily include that sort of thing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T12:53:29-08:00","id":341079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341004#post341004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see some Infernals working like that? I mean, if they're keeping the idea of power which makes you more inhuman (Basphomy in Verdigris* has those horns, for instance), but getting rid of the idea that Infernal Charms are statements about the Yozis, and not the Infernal themself, then Alex's abilities could be some subset of Infernal Melee, Resistance, and Stealth. And he certainly fits the idea that Infernals are all about &quot;casual power&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, I dunno that the line between mythic shapeshifters and &quot;shoggoths&quot; is as bright as the devs seem to think. Hindu demons and Journet to the West characters use their shapeshifting powers for all kinds of insane heavy metal album cover tricks which would seem outright <i>silly</i> beside even the most outrageous rubber man. Growing into an X00-foot-tall monstrosity with X heads and X^2 arms or having your blood turn into monsters is just the beginning! For example, Sun Wukong can use either his blood or his hair to change an object, allowing to take any one of his 72 forms, and then proceed to take any action he wills. Is there any reason that a PC with the power couldn't trick someone into swallowing said blood hair first, then have a Yeddim rip out of that person's stomach? That only differs from Alex Mercer turning you into a bomb in visual aesthetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't &quot;mythic shapeshifter&quot;, but &quot;shapeshifter with the capacity to turn into animals, which have strange attributions of capability in myth&quot;. The hoop snake rolling into victims in order to impale them with itself as if it were a venomous spear, for example, or the exaggeration of spitting cobras into spitting fire. If the Lunar flies, it's on the wings of a beast, not by expelling blood out as reaction mass. If the Lunar has powerful natural weapons, it is in claws or fangs, quills, thagomizers and horns, with nary a sword in sight. Growing extra arms gets you arms like a many-armed beast, not just generically-formed tendrils of stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Am I the only one who suspects that her name was chosen solely to screw with people by always making them want to read/type/say &quot;blasphemy&quot; instead? </div> </div> </div>Or they could just be fans of Sluggy Freelance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:31:41-08:00","id":341235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Sun Wukong can use either his blood or his hair to change an object, allowing to take any one of his 72 forms, and then proceed to take any action he wills.</div> </div> </div> </div> People like to cite Sun Wukong as an inspiration for Lunars, but his animal form is incidental to the origins of those powers (and is kind of weird in connection to his own birth, for that matter), and the aesthetic of them really trends more towards Martial Arts, Sorcery, Sidereals and probably Getimians. If we used everybody with a furry face as an inspiration for Lunars, we'd wind up with something as non-specific as... well, the sum total of everything people have wanted of Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:33:29-08:00","id":341237,"title":"","content":"Hanuman I always thought, when it came to magical monkey-themed individuals, fit Lunars more.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:18:29-08:00","id":341263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340680#post340680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Hm. Interesting idea, but I'm kind of questioning the idea of a unified lunar culture vs lunars with the cultural disparity of solars. I've understood it as, 'Moonsilver tattoos look the way they do because they're a product of the lunar collaboration' and that the mystic power intrinsic in them is a function of a degree of homogeneous design. I mean if it were as simple as, 'Tattoo some moonsilver on, BAM! You're good to go.' then I think the chimera problem would be somewhat less prevalent.<br /> <br /> Let me be a bit more clear though. I'm not against the idea of personal decorations, even as they apply to tattoos. Not every bit has to have mystic significance, and there IS some leeway as demonstrated by tattoo artifacts. It's just that when you get down to it, it seems like it vaguely (But only vaguely, not that substantially) cheapens the idea of moonsilver tattoos as a big accomplishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be perfectly happy with tattoos being minimized to a narrative &quot;adult in society&quot; role if nothing else.<br /> <br /> The whole thing about the tattoos is they're supposed to tell that particular Lunar's story, on her flesh forever, to anchor it and give it just enough form to not fall apart. Leaving aside how shitty it is for a Celestial Exaltation to be warped to high levels of functionality loss by the Wyld, there's no reason why each individual story writ on each Lunar's skin should appear the same. If anything, that makes no sense at all to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340858#post340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or create an explosion of impaling tentacles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no clue how people can say with a straight face that this isn't a Lunar aesthetic. <br /> <br /> Then again I loved the 1e Charm that turned your arm into a biting serpent, so.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this isn't one of the major drawbacks to Infernals being a Thing: that Infernals and Lunars both involve body-shaping, and the presumed need to take shoggoth and related Lovecraftian stuff from Lunars just to give Infernals something that seems otherworldly and awful. If so, that's a shit excuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-15-2014, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:37:35-08:00","id":341271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341263#post341263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no clue how people can say with a straight face that this isn't a Lunar aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Then again I loved the 1e Charm that turned your arm into a biting serpent, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hair. It turned your hair into a snake or bunch of snakes (like Medusa, not a shoggoth), which were all incredibly vulnerable and would likely soon all be slain, costing you your defense against surprise and several lethal health levels due to obvious causes. For whatever reason, it capped off the biting venom tree and was also based off of Charisma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if this isn't one of the major drawbacks to Infernals being a Thing: that Infernals and Lunars both involve body-shaping, and the presumed need to take shoggoth and related Lovecraftian stuff from Lunars just to give Infernals something that seems otherworldly and awful. If so, that's a shit excuse. </div> </div> </div>Lunars should never have been saddled with being shoggoths or having shoggoth-related powers is a very good reason for them to not be saddled with 2e chimera or their powers and themes. Chimera means something, and it isn't &quot;formless blob of flesh&quot;..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:41:46-08:00","id":341273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341271#post341271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hair. It turned your hair into a snake or bunch of snakes (like Medusa, not a shoggoth), which were all incredibly vulnerable and would likely soon all be slain, costing you your defense against surprise and several lethal health levels due to obvious causes. For whatever reason, it capped off the biting venom tree and was also based off of Charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div>lmao 1e Lunar mechanics. <br /> <br /> I like the aesthetic though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341271#post341271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars should never have been saddled with being shoggoths or having shoggoth-related powers is a very good reason for them to not be saddled with 2e chimera or their powers and themes. Chimera means something, and it isn't &quot;formless blob of flesh&quot;..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I follow what you mean? And yeah, the mythical chimerae much more interesting than what we got for 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:46:33-08:00","id":341468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar has Hybrid Body Reara\\ngement.<br /> <br /> Lunar with aprpriate knack eats a demon with a sword arm.<br /> <br /> Lunar can now give himself a sword arm.<br /> <br /> I honstly don't see how the Protptype Protagonists aren't just reskinned Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but that's an extension of shapeshifting after consuming a target, not an example of, like, a native Lunar Attribute Charm.<br /> <br /> Apparently? <br /> <br /> I mean the concept of Knacks are going away, so who knows where shapeshifting expansiona are going to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:47:22-08:00","id":341469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340858#post340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does raise the question, would an Exalted splat with that particular aesthetic work, and if so, what would they be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alex Mercer is a Flesh Aspect Chernozem.<br /> <br /> He fits to a T. He is a completely different person than the man from whose flesh he was born, despite having the same face and some memories. He was created as an act of vengeance, with the original Mercer injecting himself with Blacklight to make a monster that would kill the men trying to murder him. Flesh-aspected Charms are about physical power, violence, and efficiently incorporating the bodies of others into yourself to gain new strength.<br /> <br /> The Liminals are easily the most appropriate splat for bio-punk science fiction flavor. Anything straight out of Prototype, Resident Evil, and Parasite Eve (at least, the first one, before Aya got classical-elemental powers).<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars are more like Mortal Kombat's T-Wolf, with his combat-shamanism and Wolf Totem &quot;Animality&quot;, or Brave-Star invoking the spirits of beasts to become stronger, faster and farther-seeing. They belong to a more spiritual, animistic world, where Heart's Blood has nothing to do with DNA and everything to do with the essential spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-15-2014, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:57:57-08:00","id":341473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar has Hybrid Body Reara\\ngement.<br /> <br /> Lunar with aprpriate knack eats a demon with a sword arm.<br /> <br /> Lunar can now give himself a sword arm.<br /> <br /> I honstly don't see how the Protptype Protagonists aren't just reskinned Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they fit in even better as Liminals. Sunder broke down the first game's situation that way once - the &quot;Mercer&quot; is a body given a new, odd form of life, with all of Mercer's memories but none of his personality. It's a completely new person born entirely at the moment the game's story starts, and which then goes about assimilating and using biomass in ways that an undead monster that can mix and match limbs, organs, tissues and what have you might. In contrast, a Lunar would have been the same person from beginning to end, switching facets on occasion, and with power effects that were closer in appearance to Altered Beast than the ones in the game of Prototype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:00:41-08:00","id":341477,"title":"","content":"Yeah with all of the discussion of what kinds of weird shapeshifting/mutagenic shit everyone but Lunars is getting, it's no surprise that no small amount of people see Lunars as the Boring Animal Exalted and I really hope it doesn't play out this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:38:24-08:00","id":341537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341263#post341263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving aside how shitty it is for a Celestial Exaltation to be warped to high levels of functionality loss by the Wyld, there's no reason why each individual story writ on each Lunar's skin should appear the same. If anything, that makes no sense at all to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that in 3rd Edition, the Lunars themselves broke their Castes deliberately, for the specific purpose of creating new Castes better suited to their unenviable position in the Second Age. This might not have even been the first time they did this -- I think the devs have hinted or outright stated the the Lunars of the First Age eventually abandoned the Castes they needed for the Primordial War and adopted Castes suited to the relative peace and growing indolence of the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> Which is a much more awesome way to &quot;build heat&quot; and sell &quot;we are amazing survivors!&quot; than &quot;we were chased into a metaphorical pool of acid, didn't realize what the acid would do to us, just barely managed to figure out a way to survive the acid, and now live permanently crippled by the acid.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:39:15-08:00","id":341538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340858#post340858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar powers aren't really about turning your arm into a giant fleshy swordthing, or turning people into bombs by infecting them, or create an explosion of impaling tentacles.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341263#post341263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no clue how people can say with a straight face that this isn't a Lunar aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Then again I loved the 1e Charm that turned your arm into a biting serpent, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Saur Ops points out, you <i>could </i>be thinking of Snake Head Defense.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you're thinking of Startling Tentacle Attack, Tentacle Spear Strike and Grasping Pseudopod Method. Which are easily shoggothic attacks, but don't need to be.<br /> <br /> Just as I showed with Snake Head Defense, you could take Charms like those and give various &quot;mystic animal powers&quot; skins to them. Maybe you transform your arm into a cluster of attacking tentacles. Or maybe you shoot a mass of sticky webbing that knocks someone down and holds them. Or maybe you manifest a pouncing tiger that tackles your victim to the ground and savages them for a time before vanishing.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead of retrieving your fallen sword with an extending arm, you spit out an eagle to fetch it back for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:44:00-08:00","id":341544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341468#post341468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the concept of Knacks are going away, so who knows where shapeshifting expansiona are going to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with Knacks staying. Not all of them seem to fit as Attribute Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:21:32-08:00","id":341587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341235#post341235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> People like to cite Sun Wukong as an inspiration for Lunars, but his animal form is incidental to the origins of those powers (and is kind of weird in connection to his own birth, for that matter), and the aesthetic of them really trends more towards Martial Arts, Sorcery, Sidereals and probably Getimians. If we used everybody with a furry face as an inspiration for Lunars, we'd wind up with something as non-specific as... well, the sum total of everything people have wanted of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>We kinda have to find something to inspire Lunars on, though - and a lot of us want werewolves to be the standard inspiration of the shapeshifter splat about as much as we want a root canal. Sun Wukong is a shapeshifter that is also an animal man and who is <i>actually cool</i> instead of a mindless RAR BEAST thing - no duh people want to see him as a possible inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:36:51-08:00","id":341598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341587#post341587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We kinda have to find something to inspire Lunars on, though - and a lot of us want werewolves to be the standard inspiration of the shapeshifter splat about as much as we want a root canal. Sun Wukong is a shapeshifter that is also an animal man and who is <i>actually cool</i> instead of a mindless RAR BEAST thing - no duh people want to see him as a possible inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The werewolves that Lunars are likely to reference the most are not mindless in their other forms. Just much easier to piss off, one even more so than the others. Exalted being Exalted, you're unlikely to have to deal with the social consequences of Rage to anywhere near the same extent.<br /> <br /> By the way, Lunars aren't <i>the</i> shapeshifter splat. They are <i>a</i> shapeshifter splat. Not all shapeshifting concepts are meant to fit within Lunar concept space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T02:20:21-08:00","id":341660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a lot of us want werewolves to be the standard inspiration of the shapeshifter splat about as much as we want a root canal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting comparison; something that people write off as painful and unwanted, but is generally necessary to avoid a certain unpleasant rot from taking hold so deeply that it kills you. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Wukong is a shapeshifter that is also an animal man and who is actually cool instead of a mindless RAR BEAST thing</div> </div> </div> </div> Darn it, I hate comments like this; there's no real way to respond to them that doesn't amount to petulent whinging (at least not with my current mindset), and yet I can't stop focusing on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T05:31:22-08:00","id":341792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341598#post341598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The werewolves that Lunars are likely to reference the most are not mindless in their other forms. Just much easier to piss off, one even more so than the others. Exalted being Exalted, you're unlikely to have to deal with the social consequences of Rage to anywhere near the same extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe social consequences are not really my concern here - social consequences change per campaign, after all, and I've played things running the gamut from total impunity to living in constant worry. My concern is that werewolves are not a good place to base a splat about shapeshifting being awesome on, because lycanthropy is not awesome almost by definition because it's a curse that brings with itself bestiality and the loss of humanity - this bestiality focus having already informed entirely too much of Lunar themes in the previous two editions makes my fears and preference to keep lycanthropy a bit at arm's length to avoid a repeat scenario all the more acute. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341598#post341598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, Lunars aren't <i>the</i> shapeshifter splat. They are <i>a</i> shapeshifter splat. Not all shapeshifting concepts are meant to fit within Lunar concept space.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may not be the sole users of shapeshifting, but I'm pretty sure that they're the only splat that is in large part <i>defined</i> by it. Even the devs in their little poetic waxings call them things like &quot;Moon-mad shapeshifters&quot; while any shifting powers in other splats are caused by their own themes, not themes in themselves. We need to be able to have a decently broad range of shapeshifter concepts caught under the Lunar umbrella because &quot;shapeshifter&quot; seems to be as much of the Lunars' splat power identity as &quot;folk hero&quot; is of Solars, which means it's a nearly inescapable feature of the splat that is going to inform a pile of what they are. So we will try to find cool shapeshifters who actually shift their shape as more than a footnote to try to find inspirations for other ways to Lunar. This is where things like Wukong and Anansi come in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341660#post341660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Interesting comparison; something that people write off as painful and unwanted, but is generally necessary to avoid a certain unpleasant rot from taking hold so deeply that it kills you.<br /> <br /> Darn it, I hate comments like this; there's no real way to respond to them that doesn't amount to petulent whinging (at least not with my current mindset), and yet I can't stop focusing on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, after that first comment you might as well go whole hog. <br /> <br /> I can change the comparison to something different, if you prefer, by the way. I almost posted a kick in the balls, in fact, but I went with the root canal because the ball kick pain may be sharp, but half an hour later you're okay, while the root canal pain is going to be continuously painful for a pretty long time :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:49:33-08:00","id":341879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341792#post341792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In-universe social consequences are not really my concern here - social consequences change per campaign, after all, and I've played things running the gamut from total impunity to living in constant worry. My concern is that werewolves are not a good place to base a splat about shapeshifting being awesome on, because lycanthropy is not awesome almost by definition because it's a curse that brings with itself bestiality and the loss of humanity - this bestiality focus having already informed entirely too much of Lunar themes in the previous two editions makes my fears and preference to keep lycanthropy a bit at arm's length to avoid a repeat scenario all the more acute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the ones we're talking about, again. W:TA turns these assumptions on their head, and it's what the splat was based on, as passed through a pulp swords and sorcery revival filter. Avoiding its influence is not likely to be possible, and even if you could, you'd just end up with another round of 2e Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They may not be the sole users of shapeshifting, but I'm pretty sure that they're the only splat that is in large part <i>defined</i> by it. Even the devs in their little poetic waxings call them things like &quot;Moon-mad shapeshifters&quot; while any shifting powers in other splats are caused by their own themes, not themes in themselves. We need to be able to have a decently broad range of shapeshifter concepts caught under the Lunar umbrella because &quot;shapeshifter&quot; seems to be as much of the Lunars' splat power identity as &quot;folk hero&quot; is of Solars, which means it's a nearly inescapable feature of the splat that is going to inform a pile of what they are. So we will try to find cool shapeshifters who actually shift their shape as more than a footnote to try to find inspirations for other ways to Lunar. This is where things like Wukong and Anansi come in. </div> </div> </div>Probably because it should be cool to do werewolf stuff without being burdened by the &quot;slide into the shitter&quot; parts of the curse-type werewolf narrative. Lo and behold, guess what the developers have assured us? We won't have to deal with the shit parts of the curse-type werewolf narrative! And also, there are a bunch of other Exalted who can pick up the slack on other shapeshifting concepts, most likely numbering among the as-yet-unrevealed complementary Exalted types to be added in this edition. With the focus on elements built up to support them (presumably the animal special abilities are at least one part of this structure), Lunars can be decently broad without having to encompass excess concept baggage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:05:02-08:00","id":342060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=340531#post340531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a language that Lunars can write when in a variety of animal forms, it does make a lot of sense. I have a Lunar that was never properly trained by the Silver Pact, so he doesn't know clawspeak, and honestly it'd be really useful if I could so I didn't have to activate Dog-Tongue Method all the time (which costs a WP).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that a shared language Lunars from any corner of the world can use to communicate with each other in almost any form without Charms can be handy. Especially since Lunars are the Exalt who find it easiest in general to travel to a new Direction and interact with new languages than any other Exalted Host.<br /> <br /> As a secret language, however, it holds less water. Sidereals should have cracked the code fairly early in the dawn of the Second Age. Unless the Lunars did a sorcerous working to keep anyone but Lunars from understanding the language? I think that might exist outside of the scope of sorcerous workings, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. And if you'd pay attention...</div> </div> </div> </div>...you'd notice that we're talking about aesthetics rather than end-result effects, yes. Paying attention <i>would </i>reveal that.<br /> <br /> Summation: Prototype is science-fiction, not fantasy. Yes, even then, there is overlap. So you could base a Lunar on Mercer after giving him an Animal Totem, and changing his backstory and character, and other things. Or you could play a Chernozem, who fits Mercer better in every way.<br /> <br /> Please do not derail a thread about what we want for the Lunars we've been promised with an argument about the Lunars you think we should get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:24:43-08:00","id":342071,"title":"","content":"TL;DR Thread, but here's some things I'd like to see...<br /> <br /> A deep running Interaction with the Wyld. I get that this isn't something that's meant for Lunars to do in the new edition, but I can still dream...<br /> <br /> Speaking of dreams, a deeper connection between dreams and Lunars. Shamanisim, the deep-level instinctual or animal mind. Cool powers that do more interesting things than simple dice adders.<br /> <br /> Powers of epic scope that none-the-less express the Lunar as masters of &quot;physicality&quot;. To be honest I'm suspicious of how exactly Lunars are going to give that -Wow!- factor while expressing &quot;physicality&quot; but I'm very interested to see what the Dev's come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:08:42-08:00","id":342088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341544#post341544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with Knacks staying. Not all of them seem to fit as Attribute Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the whole reason Knacks as a concept exist is to circumvent an author's belief of &quot;if it's a Charm, Eclipsoids HAVE A RIGHT to learn it via their anima but at the same time they shouldn't be able to learn how to shape shift like Lunars...so here are things that are basically Charms but not called that.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=341598#post341598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, Lunars aren't <i>the</i> shapeshifter splat. They are <i>a</i> shapeshifter splat. Not all shapeshifting concepts are meant to fit within Lunar concept space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my concern is that what's left amounts to (what other people have described) as Boring Animal Themes.<br /> <br /> Which...I don't see animal themes as inherently boring, but precedent has made it very hard to get excited about them. Lunars have never been done well so it's hard to really conceive of what doing them well should look like,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:33:40-08:00","id":342108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342088#post342088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the whole reason Knacks as a concept exist is to circumvent an author's belief of &quot;if it's a Charm, Eclipsoids HAVE A RIGHT to learn it via their anima but at the same time they shouldn't be able to learn how to shape shift like Lunars...so here are things that are basically Charms but not called that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Knack will return just as a Keyword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess my concern is that what's left amounts to (what other people have described) as Boring Animal Themes.<br /> <br /> Which...I don't see animal themes as inherently boring, but precedent has made it very hard to get excited about them. Lunars have never been done well so it's hard to really conceive of what doing them well should look like, </div> </div> </div>Well, a number of first edition Charms would probably pump people up a lot more if the mechanical execution hadn't been terrible. Hulking out for a massive Strength bonus? Most people would be all over that. Not so much if it requires about 15 turns of standing around grunting like on padded shonen anime powerup sequences. That kind of kills the buzz, as does giving it a name almost the same as a counterattack Charm for no discernible reason. Growing a bunch of cephalopod limbs to attack would probably also be much more exciting if you didn't have to wade through a mire of speedbumps to get there and then have to take another Charm in order to deal lethal damage with your octopus arms and squid tentacles.<br /> <br /> Then you get to the Silver Solar Charms of 1e, and you ask yourself, &quot;Why are these Solar Melee knockoffs here instead of exhaling fire or toxic gas? Why generic sword tricks instead of shocking people and shooting off lightning like those giant eels* from Savage Seas?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it goes on and on. I can think of so many things related to legendary critters that appear in Shadowrun's old Paranormal Animals of North America/Europe that the concept of &quot;what do Lunar Charms?&quot; look like can be answered with &quot;All the things I wish adepts could take in SR to duplicate critter abilities, but they were never allowed to develop.&quot; There's literally an entire chapter full of them, and then some, because electric rays are cool, too, but for some reason people keep forgetting that the namesake of the torpedo can lay a person out flat with electric shocks. Lambton Wyrm touch, the projectile feathers of the birds of Stymphalos, the petrifying gaze of the Gorgons or Basilisk... all things that Lunars should have, but never appeared in their bag of tricks.<br /> <br /> *Technically knifefish rather than true eels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:40:38-08:00","id":342111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342108#post342108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Knack will return just as a Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mean the problem that the term &quot;Knack&quot; was created to solve is not going to be a problem in 3e, so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342108#post342108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a number of first edition Charms would probably pump people up a lot more if the mechanical execution hadn't been terrible. Hulking out for a massive Strength bonus? Most people would be all over that. Not so much if it requires about 15 turns of standing around grunting like on padded shonen anime powerup sequences. That kind of kills the buzz, as does giving it a name almost the same as a counterattack Charm for no discernible reason. Growing a bunch of cephalopod limbs to attack would probably also be much more exciting if you didn't have to wade through a mire of speedbumps to get there and then have to take another Charm in order to deal lethal damage with your octopus arms and squid tentacles.<br /> <br /> Then you get to the Silver Solar Charms of 1e, and you ask yourself, &quot;Why are these Solar Melee knockoffs here instead of exhaling fire or toxic gas? Why generic sword tricks instead of shocking people and shooting off lightning like those giant eels* from Savage Seas?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it goes on and on. I can think of so many things related to legendary critters that appear in Shadowrun's old Paranormal Animals of North America/Europe that the concept of &quot;what do Lunar Charms?&quot; look like can be answered with &quot;All the things I wish adepts could take in SR to duplicate critter abilities, but they were never allowed to develop.&quot; There's literally an entire chapter full of them, and then some, because electric rays are cool, too, but for some reason people keep forgetting that the namesake of the torpedo can lay a person out flat with electric shocks. Lambton Wyrm touch, the projectile feathers of the birds of Stymphalos, the petrifying gaze of the Gorgons or Basilisk... all things that Lunars should have, but never appeared in their bag of tricks.<br /> <br /> *Technically knifefish rather than true eels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got me excited just from this. Kudos, man, you're spot on! I hadn't really thought of mythical beasts, honestly, but the powers or capabilities of the cockatrice, sphinx, hydra, qiling, uktena, wendigo, catoblepas, a bao a qu, etc...that seems like perfect thematic space.<br /> <br /> And the more I think about it the more and more I am fine with Lunars basically turning into terrain features. Because a Lunar seems the most appropriate to be both Scylla AND Charybdis. <br /> <br /> Yeah the 1e stuff...upthread I mentioned how I loved some of the aesthetics of those &quot;turn your hair into serpents powers&quot; and the like. Found them very evocative, but of course the mechanics were trash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-16-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:55:56-08:00","id":342119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342111#post342111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I mean the problem that the term &quot;Knack&quot; was created to solve is not going to be a problem in 3e, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is indeed true, and I'm not personally expecting to see it again. At least looking anything like it was. However, the particulars of what they're thinking for shapeshifting are still a mystery. It could conceivably be that they look at it and say, &quot;Yeah, the reason they made Knacks separate in 2e was dumb and unnecessary. However, 2e didn't have [REDACTED] and [REDACTED] like this edition will. In light of that new context, the division/distinction starts looking like it's not a terrible idea after all. Especially as we're not seeing it as cause to suck virtually all flavor out of the Lunar Charmset.&quot; (see Saur Ops's fine post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:03:20-08:00","id":342127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stymphalian Bird Lunars, where you can turn your hairs/scales/feathers into lethal projectiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with the Totemist class from D&amp;D 3.5? They're one of the soulmeld classes and...pretty much every magical beast that the Totemist can invoke through a meld should be something that inspires Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342119#post342119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is indeed true, and I'm not personally expecting to see it again. At least looking anything like it was. However, the particulars of what they're thinking for shapeshifting are still a mystery. It could conceivably be that they look at it and say, &quot;Yeah, the reason they made Knacks separate in 2e was dumb and unnecessary. However, 2e didn't have [REDACTED] and [REDACTED] like this edition will. In light of that new context, the division/distinction starts looking like it's not a terrible idea after all. Especially as we're not seeing it as cause to suck virtually all flavor out of the Lunar Charmset.&quot; (see Saur Ops's fine post)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one of the other problems with Knacks is they were CharmCloud 2.0 - you'd have a tree with really variable Attribute prerequisites for each rung, which created huge Multiple Attribute Dependency even worse than Lunars already suffered. Like if your goal is to be able to eat gods and that is based on Stamina, but the prereq Knacks are all in Manipulation and Intelligence, it can make it impossible to build the character you really intend because of those other-Attribute prereqs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:13:04-08:00","id":342132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342127#post342127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you familiar with the Totemist class from D&amp;D 3.5? They're one of the soulmeld classes and...pretty much every magical beast that the Totemist can invoke through a meld should be something that inspires Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not, not much of a D&amp;D fan (I played too many computer RPGs before I got into the tabletop stuff, and by then, I thought D&amp;D was cliche.) But I might have to check it out.<br /> <br /> Still, if the Lunars are being inspired by Mythological monsters (which I am all for), what about Ogres, Giants and Cyclopses? Holden did say that he thinks the Hulk would be a Lunar, so... thoughts? Is Polyphemus a legit Lunar concept now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:32:14-08:00","id":342140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342132#post342132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not, not much of a D&amp;D fan (I played too many computer RPGs before I got into the tabletop stuff, and by then, I thought D&amp;D was cliche.) But I might have to check it out.<br /> <br /> Still, if the Lunars are being inspired by Mythological monsters (which I am all for), what about Ogres, Giants and Cyclopses? Holden did say that he thinks the Hulk would be a Lunar, so... thoughts? Is Polyphemus a legit Lunar concept now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact quote isn't from who you think it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">We're not trying to model the Hulk with Lunars, though there are some things about the Hulk that I admire.</div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ogres, giants and cyclopes are probably a bit too human for a totem, but I can think of ways to arrive at a general appearance with them. Zodd the Immortal from Berserk has a human form that is very ogreish, and he in turn looks like a horned tiger with wings, which is oni-like; a cyclops eye is a listed potential Tell in 1e; and a giant is, well, just a human with a size-increasing mutation, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:33:20-08:00","id":342141,"title":"","content":"As a totem maybe not but as inspiration for Charms? I'd say hell yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:18:59-08:00","id":342168,"title":"","content":"I'd say ogres and stuff could readily inform the qualities of Lunars as they live and act (or are perceived as such) in their human guises. Like, regardless of the diversity of personalities and origins, the typical image of them is likely to be wild, haggard looking barely human things living in caves and such, and it's not entirely inaccurate (not least when they deliberately play into it). So ogres and things aren't always connected to the shapeshifting (even if there are certain mythologies and folklore which ascribe shapeshifting among their powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:37:15-08:00","id":342186,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that when most people say they want Alex Mercer as a Lunar, they mean as he is, with no modifications whatsoever. Really, even insofar as he has a thing of imitating stuff he eats, it still doesn't quite fit Lunars, who should have something more character and image revealing even when they're branching off of the Sacred Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:53:47-08:00","id":342354,"title":"","content":"I wish for Heart's Blood to be one of the evocative terms to explain the heart of the matter, that the Lunar consumes or takes in part of the Essence of the subject. The easiest way of course to do this is hunt it, learn it, kill it, and consume it, but there are many other ways to take in the essence of others. I recall in one of the Aspect books a tantric experiment involved combining the essence of partners went awry, but the essences still bonded briefly. Of course, the Lunar still need to learn the subject, they just do this through &quot;exploration&quot; of the subject, rather than stalking them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-16-2014, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:14:15-08:00","id":342431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342060#post342060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that a shared language Lunars from any corner of the world can use to communicate with each other in almost any form without Charms can be handy. Especially since Lunars are the Exalt who find it easiest in general to travel to a new Direction and interact with new languages than any other Exalted Host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wavecrest! Pass through Yu-Shan gate, take dragon boat, pass through second Yu-Shan gate\u2026 Nexus!<br /> <br /> It sure is convenient being a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-16-2014, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T19:18:04-08:00","id":342491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not traveling through creation, that's traveling through Yu Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say &quot;traveling through Creation,&quot; he said &quot;travel[ing] to a new Direction.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also there's Old Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:01:30-08:00","id":342538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything's easy when you can take a short cut through an alternate plane of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>said</i> it's convenient. Almost like going to different corners of Creation was their job or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Theoretically any exalt could do that. </div> </div> </div>Yet it's not likely outside of a Sidereal game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T22:31:40-08:00","id":342637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342431#post342431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wavecrest! Pass through Yu-Shan gate, take dragon boat, pass through second Yu-Shan gate\u2026 Nexus!</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342491#post342491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there's Old Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also true.<br /> <br /> Though Old Realm would be a BITCH to write with your claws on stone or wood. That's what Clawspeak is for -- it's probably just an alternative, much simpler way to write out the words of the Old Realm language.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T23:09:39-08:00","id":342670,"title":"","content":"Elder Lunars should represent more than just old crazy Lunars. They are living,breathing, connections to the First Age. They have seen with their own eyes the works and madness of the Solars. They should both be a very human view and element to the mystery and wonder of the legends and accounts of the First Age, and be someone anachronistic, but not to the degree of the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> The ideas of Lunar wisdom and songlines(?) from 1e is an interesting concept and could fit into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-17-2014, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T23:12:46-08:00","id":342671,"title":"","content":"Shogunate-era Lunar elders should far outnumber the First Age survivors. This age-bracket of political power and thought deserves some fleshing out the third time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T23:59:38-08:00","id":342693,"title":"","content":"I wish that there is no charms from other splats that straight up shut down and make the neat toys and powers of Lunars useless. Frankly that shouldn't be happening in any splat to any other splat, that just makes for a shitty time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T11:04:35-08:00","id":343116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=342671#post342671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shogunate-era Lunar elders should far outnumber the First Age survivors. This age-bracket of political power and thought deserves some fleshing out the third time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Although the dearth of info on the Shogunate in general hurts this a lot. Hell, a joke in my group about a commonly used First Age Lunar Elder was that she slept through the Shogunate era because &quot;Nothing was going on&quot; as a tongue in cheek jab at how that period seems to do little more than placeholder leading up to the sixteen apocalypse pileup that is the Contagion/Crusade period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:59:03-08:00","id":343314,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has already been brought up, but how about Lunar charms that &quot;cure&quot; chimerism by domesticating chimera as familiars until they return to sanity as a training effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T15:00:54-08:00","id":343316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343314#post343314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has already been brought up, but how about Lunar charms that &quot;cure&quot; chimerism by domesticating chimera as familiars until they return to sanity as a training effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>My only comment is Chimerism in 3e should not look anything like Chimerism in 2e. And even with different aesthetics it probably shouldn't be that big of a Terrible Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:11:26-08:00","id":343431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343316#post343316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only comment is Chimerism in 3e should not look anything like Chimerism in 2e. And even with different aesthetics it probably shouldn't be that big of a Terrible Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I'd like to see it more similar to the Solar's Limit Break mechanic where it poses narrative challenges rather than potentially making your character unplayable. Like spending too much time in one form causes you to gain new tells temporarily, or to adopt your form's mannerisms or even rewrite your memories. But regardless I'd like a canonical cure for chimerism so it's at least possible to reverse it. I imagine ancient Luners returning from centuries of battle in the Deep Wyld requiring a nurturing hand from their fellow Lunars before they can be made sane by Creation's standards again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:14:41-08:00","id":343433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343431#post343431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I'd like to see it more similar to the Solar's Limit Break mechanic where it poses narrative challenges rather than potentially making your character unplayable. Like spending too much time in one form causes you to gain new tells temporarily, or to adopt your form's mannerisms or even rewrite your memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hate the notion that the preeminent shapeshifters among the Exalted keeping a form too long basically gives you an Animorphs curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:19:59-08:00","id":343439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the dearth of info on the Shogunate in general hurts this a lot. Hell, a joke in my group about a commonly used First Age Lunar Elder was that she slept through the Shogunate era because &quot;Nothing was going on&quot; as a tongue in cheek jab at how that period seems to do little more than placeholder leading up to the sixteen apocalypse pileup that is the Contagion/Crusade period.</div> </div> </div> </div> More people should read the Aspect books. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hate the notion that the preeminent shapeshifters among the Exalted keeping a form too long basically gives you an Animorphs curse.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't go with a risk of going full animal, or even tie it much to shapeshifting, but I do like the image of being a Lunar including having a raging storm of personality inside of you that, if left unanchored for too long, can leave you in a permanent state of lunacy. A microcosm of the effect that the Othermoons have on Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:33:06-08:00","id":343443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343439#post343439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More people should read the Aspect books. I wouldn't go with a risk of going full animal, or even tie it much to shapeshifting, but I do like the image of being a Lunar including having a raging storm of personality inside of you that, if left unanchored for too long, can leave you in a permanent state of lunacy. A microcosm of the effect that the Othermoons have on Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying their Curse to the Othermoons is probably the best idea I've head so far. Only concern is the expression of that sounds too much like 2e Solar/Lunar Limit Break. Which is not appealing.<br /> <br /> I like it better than e.g. &quot;stay in the form of a tiger too long, you start exhibiting tiger-y traits.&quot; That's a great roleplaying option, especially if tiger is your totem (and I've seen it done very well by a person with a claw strider totem very much acting like a cold, calculating raptor), but I wouldn't want it to be mandatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:47:35-08:00","id":343450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343433#post343433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hate the notion that the preeminent shapeshifters among the Exalted keeping a form too long basically gives you an Animorphs curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a challenge because no one likes being told how to play their character, but I think it's appropriate to play up this idea that being a Lunar makes you less grounded and stable than other splats. Like shamanistic shapeshifting lore where you had to wear the actual hide of an animal and act like it to don its shape, a sort of sympathetic magic. That said, this might be better represented by including <i>incentives</i> than drawbacks, like allowing you to add mutations or merits to a known form by spending more time in it.<br /> <br /> If shape shifting could include &quot;meta magic&quot; knacks, like techniques in the new Martial Arts system, that unlock as you use a form more often I'd personally be delighted. Example: spending more time in your tiger form gives you enough &quot;shifter XP&quot; to unlock tiger claws on your ape form, and spending more time as an ape unlocks the ability to use your tiger's tail as a prehensile appendage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:20:37-08:00","id":343467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343316#post343316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only comment is Chimerism in 3e should not look anything like Chimerism in 2e. And even with different aesthetics it probably shouldn't be that big of a Terrible Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they said it'll be quite different, maybe a bit more like 1e.<br /> In 1e, essentially you could get a new spirit shape, but it cost you a permanent wp due to damage to your psyche, and the new spirit shape would have some characteristics of your previous spirit shape: ie, an unholy blending of two animals, a Chimera.<br /> Also, it'd really piss off the totem spirits of your old spirit form.<br /> I doubt they'll just copy-paste 1e, it'll probably be something new, but I imagine it'll be more like that.<br /> <br /> As to the limit break, I'd like to see something about it making you more animalistic, because that's what it's supposed to do, but currently it just gives you a Solar limit break with an animal theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-17-2014, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:33:22-08:00","id":343477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343443#post343443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tying their Curse to the Othermoons is probably the best idea I've head so far. Only concern is the expression of that sounds too much like 2e Solar/Lunar Limit Break. Which is not appealing.<br /> <br /> I like it better than e.g. &quot;stay in the form of a tiger too long, you start exhibiting tiger-y traits.&quot; That's a great roleplaying option, especially if tiger is your totem (and I've seen it done very well by a person with a claw strider totem very much acting like a cold, calculating raptor), but I wouldn't want it to be mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this concept quite a bit, and differentiate the behaviours and triggers exhibited by the characteristics of the Othermoons. Completely divide Chimerism away from the Limit mechanic, as they're looking to make Chimerism a more accepted state. This makes more sense to be as mythological animals and beasts were often combinations of traits of animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:37:21-08:00","id":343480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343450#post343450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If shape shifting could include &quot;meta magic&quot; knacks, like techniques in the new Martial Arts system, that unlock as you use a form more often I'd personally be delighted. Example: spending more time in your tiger form gives you enough &quot;shifter XP&quot; to unlock tiger claws on your ape form, and spending more time as an ape unlocks the ability to use your tiger's tail as a prehensile appendage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting concept, perhaps they could use the same resource as the Solar XP that's used for Evocations and the like. This makes sense to me to balance between Lunars who rarely shapeshift and use Evocations, to Lunars who mostly shapeshift and rarely use Evocations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:13:46-08:00","id":343555,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I'm not a fan of stuff you do in character giving you more or less xp, rather than the ST just giving out XP to everyone at the end of each session. It works for a short while, but over a long game you end up with some characters having a lot more xp than others, which makes things a little awkward (though not necessarily massively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:01:09-08:00","id":343958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=338558#post338558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from the usual statements of &quot;no formlock&quot;, &quot;get rid of the tattoo-hiding tax&quot; and &quot;make their history something other than 750 years of failure and irrelevance&quot;, there is a small one--I'd like to see tattoo artifacts stay. Always liked that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say something like &quot;make Tattoos artifacts not specifically a Lunar thing&quot;, because everyone should get in on the fun.<br /> <br /> Yet tattoos are supposed to be a big or at least common thing for Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> It would help if we knew what purpose the Lunars will need the Tattoos for. I certainly hope it's not for keeping internal Wyld Taint at bay, but I could accept that some form of tattoos are necessary for locking the Caste of the Exaltation your previous incarnation jail-broke.<br /> <br /> But if tattoos are going to be mandatory for Casted Lunars, I want them to have an auto-hide feature. That's a lot more relevant and useful than... pretty much any of the other features they've had in the past. Including &quot;reject all outside physical-shaping effects&quot;, and ESPECIALLY &quot;keep a record of your life-debts&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know; as if the Lunar Exalted had more reason to be worried about <i>Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal Wyld Hunts</i> than about the Wyld or other Lunars.<br /> <br /> Besides, the shaping-rejection was a hindrance almost as often as it was a help, and never really protected against the Shaping effects Lunars would have needed to worry about. Their own Charms should have been enough to deal with the passive effects of the Wyld, and any Lunar that would Tattoo a newbie would teach them those tricks if necessary.<br /> <br /> The life-debt thing, like the Renown thing, was invested too deeply into the idea that Lunars were numerous enough to live together in familial tribes like the Garou. Rather than the reality of them being spread so far across Creation that they often don't need to give a shit what another Lunar thinks about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-18-2014, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:55:59-08:00","id":343995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343958#post343958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say something like &quot;make Tattoos artifacts not specifically a Lunar thing&quot;, because everyone should get in on the fun.<br /> <br /> Yet tattoos are supposed to be a big or at least common thing for Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> It would help if we knew what purpose the Lunars will need the Tattoos for. I certainly hope it's not for keeping internal Wyld Taint at bay, but I could accept that some form of tattoos are necessary for locking the Caste of the Exaltation your previous incarnation jail-broke.<br /> <br /> But if tattoos are going to be mandatory for Casted Lunars, I want them to have an auto-hide feature. That's a lot more relevant and useful than... pretty much any of the other features they've had in the past. Including &quot;reject all outside physical-shaping effects&quot;, and ESPECIALLY &quot;keep a record of your life-debts&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know; as if the Lunar Exalted had more reason to be worried about <i>Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal Wyld Hunts</i> than about the Wyld or other Lunars.<br /> <br /> Besides, the shaping-rejection was a hindrance almost as often as it was a help, and never really protected against the Shaping effects Lunars would have needed to worry about. Their own Charms should have been enough to deal with the passive effects of the Wyld, and any Lunar that would Tattoo a newbie would teach them those tricks if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, this edition will not produce tremendous confusion regarding the difference between Shaping and shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The life-debt thing, like the Renown thing, was invested too deeply into the idea that Lunars were numerous enough to live together in familial tribes like the Garou. Rather than the reality of them being spread so far across Creation that they often don't need to give a shit what another Lunar thinks about them. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Renown fares poorly when you change it from the esteem you have with the spirits to a scoreboard for political barbarian demigods. The former nets you amazing power from progressively more powerful spirits as you prove your worth to high rollers. The latter is an overly elaborate Reputation Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:59:28-08:00","id":343998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=343555#post343555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I'm not a fan of stuff you do in character giving you more or less xp, rather than the ST just giving out XP to everyone at the end of each session. It works for a short while, but over a long game you end up with some characters having a lot more xp than others, which makes things a little awkward (though not necessarily massively).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is simple enough to solve. Every time a player would get &quot;Solar XP&quot;, or the proposed &quot;Shifter XP&quot; or whatever other similar thing comes up, it goes to a communal pile. At the end of the story, the ST divides it equally between players. Might require establishing what sort of parity you want between various kinds of weird XP (if there ends up existing more than one such a thing) if you have a multi-splat game going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T11:25:38-08:00","id":344006,"title":"","content":"I want to gain someone's Heart's Blood whenever they swear fealty to me.<br /> <br /> As a separate effect, I want to gain someone's Heart's Blood if they break a blood-oath they swore with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: yay, I can include spaces from my Iphone now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-18-2014, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T11:31:28-08:00","id":344009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344006#post344006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to gain someone's Heart's Blood whenever they swear fealty to me. As a separate effect, I want to gain someone's Heart's Blood if they break a blood-oath they swore with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a question: what do you think the outer limit of &quot;appropriate method to gain someone's Heart's Blood&quot; would be?<br /> <br /> I ask because in previous ends, it was pretty straightforward - eat their heart as a default, with expansions into &quot;drink their blood&quot; (time-limited) or &quot;have sex with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm interested in these other ideas in this thread like swearing fealty....but how far &quot;out there&quot; past &quot;direct body-to-body interaction&quot; like heart-eating, blood-drinking, or sexual fluid transfer would you find appropriate before it just hits gonzo levels of seeming unrelatedness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T11:50:01-08:00","id":344013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344009#post344009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: what do you think the outer limit of &quot;appropriate method to gain someone's Heart's Blood&quot; would be?<br /> <br /> I ask because in previous ends, it was pretty straightforward - eat their heart as a default, with expansions into &quot;drink their blood&quot; (time-limited) or &quot;have sex with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm interested in these other ideas in this thread like swearing fealty....but how far &quot;out there&quot; past &quot;direct body-to-body interaction&quot; like heart-eating, blood-drinking, or sexual fluid transfer would you find appropriate before it just hits gonzo levels of seeming unrelatedness?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Oil-Imbibing Face Seizure</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Strength 4, Essence 2, Any Knack that allows acquisition of a category of forms<br /> Those who cannot secure their valuables and commodities from Lunars lose their shapes as well. By driving a subject away from their territory or taking a significant portion of valuables, such as Resources or an Artifact, a Lunar can take the form of the owner of the object, territory or general valuable. Significance is relative; a wild predator would surely smart from the loss of a single kill, while a fantastically wealthy Guild trader, raksha or Dragon-Blooded may need to lose an entire trading concern, claim over natural resources, Grace, or heirloom Artifact passed down from the First Age. After the kleptopredation has been carried out successfully and the item or land is under the Lunar's secure control, she may spend a Willpower point in order to take the shape of a single associated &quot;owner&quot;. At Essence 3+, she may take the forms of up to (Strength) such associated claimaints.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(There Will Be Heart's Blood!)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T11:53:27-08:00","id":344016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344009#post344009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: what do you think the outer limit of &quot;appropriate method to gain someone's Heart's Blood&quot; would be?<br /> <br /> I ask because in previous ends, it was pretty straightforward - eat their heart as a default, with expansions into &quot;drink their blood&quot; (time-limited) or &quot;have sex with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm interested in these other ideas in this thread like swearing fealty....but how far &quot;out there&quot; past &quot;direct body-to-body interaction&quot; like heart-eating, blood-drinking, or sexual fluid transfer would you find appropriate before it just hits gonzo levels of seeming unrelatedness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I remembered reading or hearing about some kind of &quot;beat someone in a competition and/or battle of wits, get their shape&quot; Knack. Ink Monkeys, maybe...? With some constraints on it so it doesn't look like a no-brainer, I'd be very fond of that manner of acquisition.<br /> <br /> I remember hatewheel saying something about how a method involving Intimacies might be on the table, though that's nebulous enough we can draw only so much from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:05:41-08:00","id":344021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344016#post344016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I remembered reading or hearing about some kind of &quot;beat someone in a competition and/or battle of wits, get their shape&quot; Knack. Ink Monkeys, maybe...? With some constraints on it so it doesn't look like a no-brainer, I'd be very fond of that manner of acquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was in this very thread. And Vance did a 2e home-brew a couple days ago in his 1L thread involving gaining Heart's Blood of people you represent as a lawyer or agent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344013#post344013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Oil-Imbibing Face Seizure</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Strength 4, Essence 2, Any Knack that allows acquisition of a category of forms<br /> Those who cannot secure their valuables and commodities from Lunars lose their shapes as well. By driving a subject away from their territory or taking a significant portion of valuables, such as Resources or an Artifact, a Lunar can take the form of the owner of the object, territory or general valuable. Significance is relative; a wild predator would surely smart from the loss of a single kill, while a fantastically wealthy Guild trader, raksha or Dragon-Blooded may need to lose an entire trading concern, claim over natural resources, Grace, or heirloom Artifact passed down from the First Age. After the kleptopredation has been carried out successfully and the item or land is under the Lunar's secure control, she may spend a Willpower point in order to take the shape of a single associated &quot;owner&quot;. At Essence 3+, she may take the forms of up to (Strength) such associated claimaints.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(There Will Be Heart's Blood!)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>THIS IS FUCKING AMAZING though I wouldn't put it solely in Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:12:27-08:00","id":344024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344009#post344009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: what do you think the outer limit of &amp;quot;appropriate method to gain someone's Heart's Blood&amp;quot; would be?<br /> <br /> I ask because in previous ends, it was pretty straightforward - eat their heart as a default, with expansions into &amp;quot;drink their blood&amp;quot; (time-limited) or &amp;quot;have sex with them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I'm interested in these other ideas in this thread like swearing fealty....but how far &amp;quot;out there&amp;quot; past &amp;quot;direct body-to-body interaction&amp;quot; like heart-eating, blood-drinking, or sexual fluid transfer would you find appropriate before it just hits gonzo levels of seeming unrelatedness?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, you gain Heart's Blood through dominance.<br /> <br /> Kill someone, steal their most valuable possession, defeat them in a contest of skill, win a game of chance, accept their loyalty or force it from them, successfully prosecute them in a court of law, bring them to sexual ecstasy, trick them into an oath they cannot keep...<br /> <br /> I'd also accept &quot;pay them the price they name&quot;, or some other equal exchange.<br /> <br /> There might be room for &quot;escape their attempts to hunt you&quot; or &quot;successfully defend yourself in a court of law&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T17:25:05-08:00","id":344248,"title":"","content":"I think the hours-long ritual hunt (or ritual prayer over a plant) should be gone anyway. It's logistically just a huge pain and doesn't really add anything to the game aside from being a huge pain when a timed objective exists. Remove it and...you have to get rid of Life of the Hummingbird? Big whoop, the speed increase was kind of an air-breathing mermaid anyway (though the &quot;need a bit of blood rather than the heart&quot; was nice).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T18:10:44-08:00","id":344283,"title":"","content":"I agree, the hunt is just really annoying. I think that's kind of the point though, to stop it being too easy. I think there must be other good ways to do that though.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like hunting as dominance. Originally, it was just eating people: literally consuming part of them, taking their power within yourself (which is a key theme of cannibalism in some of the cultures that practice it). Then it expanded to sex, but that is still &quot;consuming&quot; people metaphorically, and if you're having sex with a man then you are still taking part of him inside to gain his power (ie his form).<br /> I don't like the expansion that lets you just beat people unconscious, which is where it just becomes dominance. I feel it lacks the same mythic weight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T18:13:33-08:00","id":344284,"title":"","content":"Although I would be happy for Lunars to be able to craft things that allowed them to take people's forms, such as making a wolf-skin cloak that lets them turn into a wolf if they're wearing it. That's a rather different option to what they do now though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T18:23:43-08:00","id":344294,"title":"","content":"Actually you only need take a single taste of blood. You're not literally eating hearts unless you up and decide to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T19:24:03-08:00","id":344311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344294#post344294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually you only need take a single taste of blood. You're not literally eating hearts unless you up and decide to.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what remotely is the benefit of Life of the Hummingbird? Just a shorter time?<br /> <br /> And maybe some degree of hunt is ok, but hours and hours is just too much. I mean, this is not a real balance issue because you can only be in 1 form at a time, except for when you can easily be anyone you need to be at a moment's notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:05:00-08:00","id":344332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344311#post344311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what remotely is the benefit of Life of the Hummingbird? Just a shorter time?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, you don't have to eat the heart, but you <i>do</i> have to drink blood directly from the heart, and I'm pretty sure the heart's owner has to be dying. Life of the Hummingbird gives a shorter time with the shape, but the Lunar can just drink any of the target's blood without killing the individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And maybe some degree of hunt is ok, but hours and hours is just too much. I mean, this is not a real balance issue because you can only be in 1 form at a time, except for when you can easily be anyone you need to be at a moment's notice. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Some kind of a hunt might be appropriate, and some manner of limitation doesn't bother me, but the current setup is just... not remotely fun or interesting. What would be so terrible about a powerful Lunar massacring an entire village and taking all their faces in an afternoon?* A smart Lunar will likely be careful about studying and stalking them before striking,** so it's not as though we'd be losing those bits. I just don't see any (worthwhile) stories/moments that it creates, instead inducing some frustration that moments where a foe's shape would be dramatically appropriate to acquire can't be acquired at all.<br /> <br /> * Er. Besides the obvious, naturally. &gt;.&gt;<br /> ** And I'd be surprised if there weren't Charms helpful to this approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T22:45:37-08:00","id":344393,"title":"","content":"Without any Knacks at all, you can deliver the final killing blow with a rapier through their heart, and then dab your tongue in the blood coating your blade. No need to literally eat the heart or rip someone's chest open to drink directly from it.<br /> <br /> The minimum time-limit Second Edition imposed on the Sacred Hunt was annoying and stupid. It was nice to have as a guideline for hunting a perfect specimen of a random animal in a random part of the world, but it sucked for everything else.<br /> <br /> Hatewheel has said he's not going to do &quot;temporary Heart's Blood&quot;; either it's in your library for keeps, or it's not at all. So, no Life of the Hummingbird.<br /> <br /> Life of the Hummingbird was also too easy. It's pathetically simple for a Lunar to turn into mosquito and steal someone's blood. There's no challenge, no risk, no possibility of failure. None of the other methods are so SAFE and cheesy.<br /> <br /> Life of the Hummingbird is also a problem in that it focuses too much on the <i>substance </i>of the blood rather than the <i>meaning </i>behind it. Lunars don't use DNA.<br /> <br /> Heart's Blood is about defeating or dominating another creature and marking your victory by taking their essence into yourself, or about making some kind of sacrifice or taking some kind of risk.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meditating next to a plant is fine, since it's just a plant. Unless it's a monster plant that can fight back, of course. But even with a plant that can't fight back, it wouldn't be a problem if a Lunar needed to eat a piece of it, or at least nibble on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-19-2014, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T22:48:04-08:00","id":344398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344284#post344284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I would be happy for Lunars to be able to craft things that allowed them to take people's forms, such as making a wolf-skin cloak that lets them turn into a wolf if they're wearing it. That's a rather different option to what they do now though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earlier in the thread, I mentioned the idea of wearing pelts enabling you to treat that creature as a true form.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea of making artifact-grade gear out of animal hides, <i>a la</i> Monster Hunter.<br /> <br /> With both options, Lunars suddenly have very good reasons to wear furs and feathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:41:39-08:00","id":344435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344248#post344248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the hours-long ritual hunt (or ritual prayer over a plant) should be gone anyway. It's logistically just a huge pain and doesn't really add anything to the game aside from being a huge pain when a timed objective exists. Remove it and...you have to get rid of Life of the Hummingbird? Big whoop, the speed increase was kind of an air-breathing mermaid anyway (though the &quot;need a bit of blood rather than the heart&quot; was nice).</div> </div> </div> </div>The hunt is a big reason few of my Lunars ever had that many shapes. Downtime was about the only moment a shape or two cound reliably be added into the library, so it had to be something that came to mind when we suddenly got downtime.<br /> <br /> Didn't help that a couple of my STs interpreted the hunt as something that had to be performed alone and personally - which on a Lunar whose reaction in combat is to hide in a nearby barrel and wait for the circle to mop up due to the entirety of her combat competence being a dot of Thrown, makes thing complicated, let me tell you :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T01:10:36-08:00","id":344471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344435#post344435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hunt is a big reason few of my Lunars ever had that many shapes. Downtime was about the only moment a shape or two cound reliably be added into the library, so it had to be something that came to mind when we suddenly got downtime.<br /> <br /> Didn't help that a couple of my STs interpreted the hunt as something that had to be performed alone and personally - which on a Lunar whose reaction in combat is to hide in a nearby barrel and wait for the circle to mop up due to the entirety of her combat competence being a dot of Thrown, makes thing complicated, let me tell you :P.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the only point of the hunt was to make the Heart's Blood background worth taking. In 1E, it was pointless, because you could just start with a predator's form, and then vanish into the woods in your first bit of downtime and come out having saved 3-4 Background dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T01:21:49-08:00","id":344473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344471#post344471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only point of the hunt was to make the Heart's Blood background worth taking. In 1E, it was pointless, because you could just start with a predator's form, and then vanish into the woods in your first bit of downtime and come out having saved 3-4 Background dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, now Backgrounds are much easier to balance, as Merits that don't need to exist on a strict 1-to-5 scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:12:30-08:00","id":344608,"title":"","content":"Should Lunars be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot;? Their patron has a clear and direct relation to the Wyld, so, if not, why not?<br /> <br /> More specifically, does it make sense that Lunars don't deal with the Wyld at least as well as Solars do? Even the Lunars' scene long Shaping Defence, Laughing Into the Teeth of Madness, is nowhere near as good as Integrity Protecting Prana. In fact, that charm is a late retroactive explanation for the need for Moonsilver Tattoos, which is why it's deliberately flawed in the first place. <br /> <br /> Are Moonsilver Tattoos so vital to the Lunar concept that the writers have to bend over so far backward to justify them as making intentionally flawed charms for them? Must Lunars have the tats? Or can't the tats be given some other function, if their presence really is needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:53:21-08:00","id":344648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344608#post344608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunars be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot;? Their patron has a clear and direct relation to the Wyld, so, if not, why not?<br /> <br /> More specifically, does it make sense that Lunars don't deal with the Wyld at least as well as Solars do? Even the Lunars' scene long Shaping Defence, Laughing Into the Teeth of Madness, is nowhere near as good as Integrity Protecting Prana. In fact, that charm is a late retroactive explanation for the need for Moonsilver Tattoos, which is why it's deliberately flawed in the first place.<br /> <br /> Are Moonsilver Tattoos so vital to the Lunar concept that the writers have to bend over so far backward to justify them as making intentionally flawed charms for them? Must Lunars have the tats? Or can't the tats be given some other function, if their presence really is needed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No they should not, because while Luna has a connection to the Wyld, it is one of her many connections, and not her entire portfolio. Being a hypothetical Chosen of the Wyld brings connotations of the Wyld that don't really fit the Lunar gamespace, or just dilute the concept of what Lunars are. Lunars are the Chosen of Luna, their powers are inspired by Luna in the same was Solar charms are inspired by UCS. They can have powers that work with the Wyld like Luna does, but that should not be their focus.<br /> <br /> As for Solars being better shaping defense than Lunars, the UCS burned away at the edges of Creation, enforcing reality and protecting Creation. Luna works with the tide of the Wyld, not defending against it. If anything a Lunar's shaping defense should be a more fluid thing.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver tattoos are a visually distinct characteristic unique to Lunars. They do need to be reworked, perhaps keeping hidden and emerging like the caste-mark, but that kind of design is too distinct and interesting to do away with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:14:26-08:00","id":344683,"title":"","content":"I really like the tattoos, and definitely think they should stay. It allows reincarnations of Lunars to have different castes, which is something I find interesting*. (Having played in a game where a character died and the circle searched for the next person bearing his exaltation, I find the moment of &quot;Oh shit, the full-moon is a no-moon now&quot; can be cool).<br /> <br /> I like what it says about Sol and about Luna - the UCS deals in absolutes, strict castes that you can never get out of; Luna allows her chosen to define themselves as who they want or need to be and works <i>with</i> the host, making the Caste an emergent pattern rather than an imposed one.<br /> <br /> So I like needing tattoos to define one's caste, I like the casteless, and I like the added benefit of wyld-protection.<br /> I'm against the idea of needing tattoos to avoid becoming an eldritch abomination because Luna thought it'd be funny.<br /> <br /> <br /> *AFAIK the books don't contradict this... if they do, treat it as head-canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:22:47-08:00","id":344687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344608#post344608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunars be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot;? Their patron has a clear and direct relation to the Wyld, so, if not, why not?<br /> <br /> More specifically, does it make sense that Lunars don't deal with the Wyld at least as well as Solars do? Even the Lunars' scene long Shaping Defence, Laughing Into the Teeth of Madness, is nowhere near as good as Integrity Protecting Prana. In fact, that charm is a late retroactive explanation for the need for Moonsilver Tattoos, which is why it's deliberately flawed in the first place.<br /> <br /> Are Moonsilver Tattoos so vital to the Lunar concept that the writers have to bend over so far backward to justify them as making intentionally flawed charms for them? Must Lunars have the tats? Or can't the tats be given some other function, if their presence really is needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider that just terrible mechanical decisions. I refuse to read in anything potentially worthwhile about &quot;Lunars being narratively worse at dealing with/resisting the Wyld&quot; into mechanics that exist only to emphasize how much a given splat sucks compared to another one, or to justify a stupid design decision like the mechanical implementation of the tattoos in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T08:22:03-08:00","id":344790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344608#post344608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunars be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot;? Their patron has a clear and direct relation to the Wyld, so, if not, why not?<br /> <br /> More specifically, does it make sense that Lunars don't deal with the Wyld at least as well as Solars do? Even the Lunars' scene long Shaping Defence, Laughing Into the Teeth of Madness, is nowhere near as good as Integrity Protecting Prana. In fact, that charm is a late retroactive explanation for the need for Moonsilver Tattoos, which is why it's deliberately flawed in the first place.<br /> <br /> Are Moonsilver Tattoos so vital to the Lunar concept that the writers have to bend over so far backward to justify them as making intentionally flawed charms for them? Must Lunars have the tats? Or can't the tats be given some other function, if their presence really is needed?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6w0jakILepk\" target=\"_blank\">No!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T10:13:31-08:00","id":344885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344608#post344608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunars be &quot;the Wyld Exalted&quot;? Their patron has a clear and direct relation to the Wyld, so, if not, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if anyone would be the Wyld Exalted, it would be the Chosen of an Ishvara or some other Creature Of The Wyld. Luna is not a creature of the Wyld; she is something else, which happens to have facility with dealing with the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More specifically, does it make sense that Lunars don't deal with the Wyld at least as well as Solars do? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though it would also make sense if Lunars could deal with the Wyld more strongly than they have in past Editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even the Lunars' scene long Shaping Defence, Laughing Into the Teeth of Madness, is nowhere near as good as Integrity Protecting Prana. In fact, that charm is a late retroactive explanation for the need for Moonsilver Tattoos, which is why it's deliberately flawed in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Lunar design was hobbled in many ways in previous Editions; they didn't know what to do with Lunars, and struggled to make them seem relevant while also explaining why they hadn't actually been relevant.<br /> <br /> Third Edition is a chance to wipe the slate clean and fix the problems from the foundation upwards. Holden has promised that Lunars will actually feel like an integrated part of the setting now. Pervious Editions needed to rely on the Wyld as a place to shove Lunars out of the picture, and as a leash to keep them from returning to the picture before the Solars returned.<br /> <br /> That kennel and leash are no longer necessary. The Lunars don't need to be hobbled in regards to the Wyld anymore.<br /> <br /> In part because the Dragon-Blooded, Sidereals, the Shogunate Wyld Hunt, and the Empress's Wyld Hunt will be very sufficient threats to keep Lunars on the run and hiding.<br /> <br /> Also because the devs don't need the Wyld to break the Lunar Castes; not when the Lunars themselves are going to break their own Castes as a deliberate step towards creating new Castes with which to wage war against the Terrestrial Host.<br /> <br /> This time, history is not something done to the Lunars. This time, Lunars are making their own history in defiance of what others would do to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Moonsilver Tattoos so vital to the Lunar concept that the writers have to bend over so far backward to justify them as making intentionally flawed charms for them? Must Lunars have the tats? Or can't the tats be given some other function, if their presence really is needed? </div> </div> </div>The Tattoos are important, but they were given bad reasons to be important, and a bad backstory. Lunars can still have Tattoos, but with a proper backstory and good reasons for using them in the present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344683#post344683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the tattoos, and definitely think they should stay. It allows reincarnations of Lunars to have different castes, which is something I find interesting*. *AFAIK the books don't contradict this... if they do, treat it as head-canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not made very explicit, but yes, Lunars can have different Castes with each incarnation.<br /> <br /> That was never because of the Tattoos, though. In previous Editions, Lunars always started Casteless before settling into the Caste which best fit their current incarnation. Tattoos only later became necessary as a way to keep that one Caste.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm against the idea of needing tattoos to avoid becoming an eldritch abomination because Luna thought it'd be funny. </div> </div> </div>It was never because of that, either. But it's also not going to be a thing in the next edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T10:39:16-08:00","id":344924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344885#post344885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was never because of that, either. But it's also not going to be a thing in the next edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. It was in reference to the &quot;Luna made fallible exaltations and Lunars had to fix her screwup&quot; arguments I've seen here and on the old forums in the past.<br /> Ultimately I dislike Chimarism as being a thing that just happens &quot;because there's wyld in you and you should have gotten your tattoos to fix that&quot;, and am very happy to see it go back to the ways of 1e (or, well, closer to them). Eldritch horror lunars should still be a thing, by choice rather than by accident though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:28:55-08:00","id":345076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I sort of like the idea of the Wyld being connected to Chimeraism.<br /> <br /> We know Chimerae are changing and being a thing that is a viable option for Lunar advancement. Basically your Spirit Shape is supposed to have these Keywords or something like that, and those keywords either modify Charms, or switch where they are in the tree, or have some other benefit, and that it's possible to go back and add Keywords to your Spirit Shape(somehow). At least, that's something I remember reading while Lurking here.<br /> <br /> If Chimeraism lets a Lunar add &quot;Keywords&quot; that wouldn't normally be appropriate for their Spirit shape to that shape by Altering it with the physical traits of other animals, and if Moonsilver Tattoos still exist for the purposes of preventing enemies/the wild from shaping your form or mind against your will, than perhaps 3E chimerae are Lunars who deliberately &quot;turned off&quot; their tats, just for a second, and let in just a bit of Wyld Taint, before shutting out the rest and binding that teensy bit of wyld to their totemic Spirit Shape, allowing them to alter it into more potent and versitile hybrid shapes and probably do the same with their Warform if they have one.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Tattoos being a precaution against hostile body alterations. for a splat that's supposed to fluidly shift from one fom to an other, an increased vulnerability to baleful polymorphic effects sounds like a logical weakness</div> </div> </div> </div>Overpowered but &quot;dangerous&quot; options aren't good for play balance. If you want them, keep playing 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:45:31-08:00","id":345132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I sort of like the idea of the Wyld being connected to Chimeraism.<br /> <br /> We know Chimerae are changing and being a thing that is a viable option for Lunar advancement. Basically your Spirit Shape is supposed to have these Keywords or something like that, and those keywords either modify Charms, or switch where they are in the tree, or have some other benefit, and that it's possible to go back and add Keywords to your Spirit Shape(somehow). At least, that's something I remember reading while Lurking here.<br /> <br /> If Chimeraism lets a Lunar add &quot;Keywords&quot; that wouldn't normally be appropriate for their Spirit shape to that shape by Altering it with the physical traits of other animals, and if Moonsilver Tattoos still exist for the purposes of preventing enemies/the wild from shaping your form or mind against your will, than perhaps 3E chimerae are Lunars who deliberately &quot;turned off&quot; their tats, just for a second, and let in just a bit of Wyld Taint, before shutting out the rest and binding that teensy bit of wyld to their totemic Spirit Shape, allowing them to alter it into more potent and versitile hybrid shapes and probably do the same with their Warform if they have one.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Tattoos being a precaution against hostile body alterations. for a splat that's supposed to fluidly shift from one fom to an other, an increased vulnerability to baleful polymorphic effects sounds like a logical weakness</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make sense for your greatest splat-specific powers to also be the source of your most dire weaknesses (see also: Paradox and DB Charms that fail when they oppose Essence-fueled powers). Especially if that kind of theme only applies to certain splats and not all of them.<br /> <br /> This sort of theme is much more of a WoD conceit (both OWoD and NWoD) than an Exalted one (ex. for Garou, how Rage makes them much more dangerous in combat but attracts undue hostile attention and fear from just walking down the street; for Mages, how manifesting their most powerful magic makes collective-reality literally smack them in the face).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:43:55-08:00","id":345162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about OP or Dangerous? I imagine that 3E Chimeraism will have trade offs like every other thing has been said to have trade offs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The third paragraph of the post I quoted sounded an awful lot like it - letting in the Wyld for an &quot;increase in potency and/or versatility&quot;. I don't think that forcing life on the edge is a very good balance mechanic for Exalted. It's more the bag of Double Cross.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:57:48-08:00","id":345165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it does make sense for a group whose primary power is &quot;Easily change shape&quot; to have the weakness &quot;It's hard to resist having my shape changed&quot;, the same way that a guy whose power is &quot;I am made of fire&quot; would logically have he weakness &quot;Is harmed by water&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Exalted, it doesn't really make sense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'd buy &quot;This is a thing we made to negate a problem that's otherwise unavoidable do to the nature of our powers&quot; over &quot;This is a thing we made to negate a problem that Luna/and The Elder's fleeing the userpation could have prevented or fixed better if they weren't so lazy/Sucky&quot; as a justification for the existance of the &quot;Anti Hostile Shapeshifting&quot; tats any day, wouldn't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather rollback the problem into non-existence and thus greatly negate any of the dumb mechanical implementation of the so-called solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T15:57:17-08:00","id":345197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's not a theme of Exalted. The great, intrinsic strength of each splat does not also form the foundation of their great weakness; the weakness of the Exalted is their drift from humanity and what it means to be both more and less than human, particularly when cursed to inhuman excesses of emotion by the creators of the world that they overthrew. To take your example, it's not the case that Fire Aspect DBs or even fire elementals suffer extra damage from water.<br /> <br /> I see what you're getting at in that it <i>logically might make sense</i>, and how that weakness plays out in other media/games, but it's simply never been the case for Exalted. The times where it's come up in Exalted, it's felt kludgy and like a grafted-on punishment mechanic that doesn't really narratively follow from the themes Exalted tries to emphasize. See also Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:09:50-08:00","id":345241,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think that Lunars would still use tattoo artifacts pretty commonly even if they weren't necessary to preserving their sanity, because artifacts in your skin are very practical for shapeshifters. A daiklaive or super heavy plate quickly lose utility when you change size, or add/lose appendages. Being able to apply similar benefits <i>all the time</i> regardless of your chosen form is useful to Lunars in a way that other splats don't really have to consider. I think we could keep all the cool factor of tattoo artifacts and still have them be a &quot;Lunar thing&quot; without having to make them necessary in other ways that limit the splat, frankly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:15:56-08:00","id":345267,"title":"","content":"Clarification: when I said chimarism, I meant the 2e version - hence eldritch abominations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I sort of like the idea of the Wyld being connected to Chimeraism.<br /> <br /> We know Chimerae are changing and being a thing that is a viable option for Lunar advancement. Basically your Spirit Shape is supposed to have these Keywords or something like that, and those keywords either modify Charms, or switch where they are in the tree, or have some other benefit, and that it's possible to go back and add Keywords to your Spirit Shape(somehow). At least, that's something I remember reading while Lurking here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That seems to be somewhat the way they're going, for now at least (from what I gather it might still change between here and the Lunars release, because it's just the current working idea).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Chimeraism lets a Lunar add &quot;Keywords&quot; that wouldn't normally be appropriate for their Spirit shape to that shape by Altering it with the physical traits of other animals, and if Moonsilver Tattoos still exist for the purposes of preventing enemies/the wild from shaping your form or mind against your will, than perhaps 3E chimerae are Lunars who deliberately &quot;turned off&quot; their tats, just for a second, and let in just a bit of Wyld Taint, before shutting out the rest and binding that teensy bit of wyld to their totemic Spirit Shape, allowing them to alter it into more potent and versitile hybrid shapes and probably do the same with their Warform if they have one.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Tattoos being a precaution against hostile body alterations. for a splat that's supposed to fluidly shift from one fom to an other, an increased vulnerability to baleful polymorphic effects sounds like a logical weakness</div> </div> </div> </div>They can already develop charms (and Knacks if those are still a thing) to do that though.<br /> <br /> The way I'd do it is that Lunars that refuse to get tattoos and choose to become lone wolves out in the wyld can become eldritch abominations. That, to me anyway, seems totally in-theme, and it could/would couple with Chimerism (the 1e/3e definition of it) rather well (e.g. repeatedly Sacred Hunting really messed up wyld-mutated beasts/behemoths and taking them as Spirit Shapes to get access to crazy weird features). Or something akin to performing rabid Vision-Quests over and over again until you get what you want.<br /> <br /> But it wouldn't necessarily be an avenue to power any more than normal, requiring as much investment as, say, Sorcery or Evocations; the difference being that you're losing your body and mind to the Wyld - not because of your exaltation, but because your relentless thirst for power/revenge/etc. is keeping you in the wyld, and you purposefully refused help and (shape) protection. <br /> <br /> Hence by choice, not by accident (where, by comparisson, accident is 2e's &quot;Oops, we didn't tattoo you soon enough and you got a permanent arm sticking out of your forehead. Sucks to be you.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want that to be anywhere close to the baseline PC Lunar play style though. This would be for, like, The Big Bad.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't want the tattoos to be able to be turned off by any means (aside for storytelling I guess. Like taking your true human form and deliberately ripping all of your (tattooed) skin off, using no charms to heal, or some other hugely significant event. Like Dracula forsaking God, just so much <i>will</i> and raw <i>Fuck You</i> that the rules break.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:18:53-08:00","id":345271,"title":"","content":"As an aside: Tattoos don't protect your sanity. They only protect your physical shape. The Wyld can still drive tattooed Lunars insane barring other magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:37:11-08:00","id":345279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345241#post345241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think that Lunars would still use tattoo artifacts pretty commonly even if they weren't necessary to preserving their sanity, because artifacts in your skin are very practical for shapeshifters. A daiklaive or super heavy plate quickly lose utility when you change size, or add/lose appendages. Being able to apply similar benefits <i>all the time</i> regardless of your chosen form is useful to Lunars in a way that other splats don't really have to consider. I think we could keep all the cool factor of tattoo artifacts and still have them be a &quot;Lunar thing&quot; without having to make them necessary in other ways that limit the splat, frankly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Lunars don't see a return of Many Pockets Meditation, I'd like to see them store possessions AS tattoos.<br /> <br /> If I have a Nemean Lion hide, a Dragon hide, and a Solar Skull Cap, then I could go around practically naked save for some visible lion, dragon, and sunburst tattoos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:55:37-08:00","id":345285,"title":"","content":"With Third Edition making it easier to gain Heart's Blood without killing the victim, I want Heart's Blood more thoroughly integrated with the Lunar Charmset.<br /> <br /> I want someone's Heart's Blood to give my--<br /> <br /> * Perception Charms a boost to locating, finding, spotting, hearing, identifying, and reading them.<br /> <br /> * Intelligence Charms a boost to healing, cursing, anticipating and understanding them. Not just understanding their motives and what they'll do next, but also piercing through their lies or communicating with them despite not knowing their language. Of course, understanding them regardless of language becomes easier if I ransack through their copied memories to learn their skills and secrets.<br /> <br /> * Social Charms a boost to persuading, inspiring, seducing, intimidating, commanding and deceiving them.<br /> <br /> * Dexterity Charms a boost to defeating their defenses and avoiding their attacks<br /> <br /> * Strength Charms a boost to damage, and Stamina Charms a boost to soak.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T18:07:47-08:00","id":345286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=339805#post339805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self, Sidereal Martial Art involving armor. Silver Fortess of Unassailability Style or something along those lines...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spire of Communication style","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T19:39:33-08:00","id":345348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the Idea of &quot;Totally viable and accepted state&quot; 3E Chimeraism being something restricted to the Castless...</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said it would be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:13:00-08:00","id":345399,"title":"","content":"My biggest complaint about Heartsblood has always been that it was inherently messy and brutish in acquisition and I'd like to see that changed. A Lunar social build should be able to copy faces they see in court by knowing their intimacies, or by becoming the focus of an intimacy themselves. I'd like to see form-acquisition advance more character concepts than just &quot;barbarian hunter&quot; and I'd like to see that <i>at character generation</i>. <br /> <br /> One idea I had some time ago was that form-acquisition could be handled differently by various knacks, and that you could pick your first knack for free at character gen. However with what we have been hearing about Lunars in Ex3 it seems increasingly likely to me that Lunars might not all be shape-shifters, in which case I'd be very happy just to see them given a variety pf charms that let them take other forms through different methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:45:05-08:00","id":345411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345286#post345286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spire of Communication style</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Styles always have a color at the start of them, so you might have to work on that. Also, Spire of Communication sounds like the Creation-equivalent of a Communication Tower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 12-20-2014, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:47:54-08:00","id":345428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fata-Ku suggested something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>what? how?<br /> I only talked about casteless becoming eldritch abominations and that it would meld well with 1e chimarism. Never said or even approached chimarism as being limited to casteless.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T02:29:09-08:00","id":345596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest complaint about Heartsblood has always been that it was inherently messy and brutish in acquisition and I'd like to see that changed. A Lunar social build should be able to copy faces they see in court by knowing their intimacies, or by becoming the focus of an intimacy themselves. I'd like to see form-acquisition advance more character concepts than just &quot;barbarian hunter&quot; and I'd like to see that at character generation.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel as though this is the kind of thing that needs to be handled carefully to avoid diluting the Lunar concept. Maybe they don't need to be barbarian hunters, but even without consuming blood, I feel there should be something inherently predatory to their methods. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However with what we have been hearing about Lunars in Ex3 it seems increasingly likely to me that Lunars might not all be shape-shifters</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems about the exact opposite of the impression I've gotten; what are you basing it on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:20:21-08:00","id":345614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345596#post345596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel as though this is the kind of thing that needs to be handled carefully to avoid diluting the Lunar concept. Maybe they don't need to be barbarian hunters, but even without consuming blood, I feel there should be something inherently predatory to their methods. That seems about the exact opposite of the impression I've gotten; what are you basing it on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think what they're trying to say is that in 3E a Lunar who doesn't shapeshift is a viable character without being gimped. The abllity to shapeshift will still be there, but it will be something the character can do instead of something they have to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:34:51-08:00","id":345621,"title":"","content":"The idea that you can have a viable Lunar swordfighter without having to go to the warform (and possibly shifting into animal shapes) does not strictly track to the idea that... actually, I'm not even sure what the chain of logic is supposed to be. :s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T04:46:35-08:00","id":345675,"title":"","content":"Not fighting in a warform doesn't mean you're not a shapshifter. There's plenty of other uses for shapeshifting after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T04:51:03-08:00","id":345677,"title":"","content":"Actually, checking the what-we-know wiki, the Devs said that a Lunar swordsman will be just as effective as a Lunar who used DBT,<br /> They'll still be shapeshifters, even their swordmen, their sorcerors and their kings, but not all of them will use 'Waagh, now I'm a bearman' as their primary method of fighting things.<br /> <br /> Something I really want for the Lunars are Intelligence Charms and Wits Charms. This is mostly because A: I don't have the Lunar books, and thus have no idea how they fill in these Charmsets, and B: Because I can't really picture Lunar Intelligence/Wits Charms, while I can easily picture Charms for the rest of their attributes.<br /> <br /> And hopefully a lot of interaction between their shapeshifting (because that sounds awesome so far) and their Charms (which I haven't heard a lot of yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:12:59-08:00","id":345684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345677#post345677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I really want for the Lunars are Intelligence Charms and Wits Charms. This is mostly because A: I don't have the Lunar books, and thus have no idea how they fill in these Charmsets,</div> </div> </div> </div>Badly, for the most part. Wits essentially consists of Elsewhere charms and copies of Dex charms. Int is a little better. It has the social defence charms, and a bunch of random charms that are are reasonably decent for the most part but have little in common with each other. It's a pretty small charmset.<br /> I'm hoping there will be a lot more in the next book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:53:22-08:00","id":345714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345684#post345684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Badly, for the most part. Wits essentially consists of Elsewhere charms and copies of Dex charms. Int is a little better. It has the social defence charms, and a bunch of random charms that are are reasonably decent for the most part but have little in common with each other. It's a pretty small charmset.<br /> I'm hoping there will be a lot more in the next book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, let's hope that 3e is capable of giving us better Charms, and that the 3e Dev team are capable of writing better Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:02:28-08:00","id":345719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345714#post345714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, let's hope that 3e is capable of giving us better Charms, and that the 3e Dev team are capable of writing better Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of it is hoping that Wits gets an actual good definition. I think a lot of problems with past eds is not really being able to draw a firm distinction between some of the Attributes - Charisma/Manipulation and Intelligence/Wits being the most memorable pairs. Especially when you remove the objective moral badness of Manipulation that was prevalent in OWoD and 1e. But to me, the &quot;logical thinking vs quick thinking&quot; has never been a truly meaningful difference, nor has it provided fertile soil for Charm differentiation.<br /> <br /> I also hope chargen is closer to the Domino model simply because of how those two Attribute pairs can just be super redundant for characters. Given that Solars have more of a pick-and-choose where it comes to their Caste Abilities than they previously had, I assume (and hope) something similar will happen for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T08:20:22-08:00","id":345776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345675#post345675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not fighting in a warform doesn't mean you're not a shapshifter. There's plenty of other uses for shapeshifting after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, you'll probably be running through even more shapes, because you're not sticking with one in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T08:33:55-08:00","id":345787,"title":"","content":"I used to object to the idea that Lunars should need to universally be animal-focused shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Then the devs gave us Chernozem for our Alex Mercer, Startling Tentacle Attack, Tentacle Spear Strike, Grasping Pseudopod Method, flesh-as-clay shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Now I can have the spiritual or the sci-fi, each undiluted by the other and thus more strongly oriented towards their own flavor and style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T09:20:47-08:00","id":345801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345776#post345776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, you'll probably be running through even more shapes, because you're not sticking with one in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much hope that Beast Boy style fighting is not only supported, but part of the baseline assumption for how Lunars fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T09:23:17-08:00","id":345803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345787#post345787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to object to the idea that Lunars should need to universally be animal-focused shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Then the devs gave us Chernozem for our Alex Mercer, Startling Tentacle Attack, Tentacle Spear Strike, Grasping Pseudopod Method, flesh-as-clay shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Now I can have the spiritual or the sci-fi, each undiluted by the other and thus more strongly oriented towards their own flavor and style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel similarly about many of the alternate form acquisition methods tbh.<br /> Because to me, Lunars are primal and predatory, so having a Lunar gain a shape because they made a favorable contract and shook hands with their prey feels... off.<br /> It seems to me like it'd belong to a different splat, like the Chosen of Masks (were those shapeshifters? Or were they focused on literal masks? I can't recall. Anyway, e.g. an exigent of Koh the Face Stealer)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  many of* 12-20-2014, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T09:39:12-08:00","id":345809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345803#post345803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel similarly about many of the alternate form acquisition methods tbh.<br /> Because to me, Lunars are primal and predatory, so having a Lunar gain a shape because they made a favorable contract and shook hands with their prey feels... off.<br /> It seems to me like it'd belong to a different splat, like the Chosen of Masks (were those shapeshifters? Or were they focused on literal masks? I can't recall. Anyway, e.g. an exigent of Koh the Face Stealer)</div> </div> </div> </div>Handshakes are very predatory in some contexts. Most of them involve business and government, as a way of playing a brief dominance game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:14:56-08:00","id":345833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345801#post345801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much hope that Beast Boy style fighting is not only supported, but part of the baseline assumption for how Lunars fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes.<br /> <br /> But also the &quot;bear-shirt'er&quot; and &quot;wolf-head'er&quot;. That is Berserker and Ulfhednar warriors who went into battle in hooded cloaks made from the head and hides of beasts.<br /> <br /> The Monster Hunter player, bearing his weapon made from a legendary beast, and armor made from same, charging into battle with berserker fury and the bestial Evocations of his trophy-gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:26:13-08:00","id":345839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345833#post345833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes.<br /> <br /> But also the &quot;bear-shirt'er&quot; and &quot;wolf-head'er&quot;. That is Berserker and Ulfhednar warriors who went into battle in hooded cloaks made from the head and hides of beasts.<br /> <br /> The Monster Hunter player, bearing his weapon made from a legendary beast, and armor made from same, charging into battle with berserker fury and the bestial Evocations of his trophy-gear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds awesome.<br /> <br /> What I really mean is...if animals are getting somewhat &quot;proprietary&quot; techniques that probably stack with Charms, it makes it much more viable and exciting to decide &quot;okay I'm going to open from ambush above in the shape of a leopard, taking advantage of its Terrible Death From Above Pounce ability, then shift into a longhorn to take advantage of its Ten-Foot Horn Gore ability.&quot; Versus 2 eds of &quot;yeah I'll just be in DBT because nothing can really compete with that&quot; or even &quot;welp the choice is really only either DBT and no Evocations or Evocations and no DBT.&quot; More option is great. Having 2 main options (DBT or Evocations) is cool but i'd definitely prefer 10 viable combat options over 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:14:18-08:00","id":345939,"title":"","content":"Much as I'm all for the expansion of splat concepts if you give Lunars too many things that turn them into matter rather than into other lifeforms they start to infringe on terrestrial charm concepts I think. Luna has strong ties to Gaia but her expression of that connection is more &quot;complete&quot; than individual elements. Being able to turn into other sentient entities is a somewhat unique purview for her and I think should be unique to her exalts as well.<br /> <br /> And I really wish I could find the forum post but at one point I remember Holden saying that they would be adding support for non-shapeshifter Lunar in Ex3. I think what was probably meant was just that Warbeast-form would no longer be a requirement for a lunar combat build, but it's the start I hope of them taking shapeshifting in a new direction.<br /> <br /> What I'd like more than anything for Lunars is for them to be divorced from this barbarian thematic. Others have said that they have trouble conceiving of &quot;smart&quot; Lunars and that their intelligence charms don't support that play style. That's ridiculous to me. Lunars should be able to rock the &quot;mad genius&quot; archetype in a unique way form Solars, like the self-taught alchemist or the insane shaman who knows more than they should and isn't fettered by training or even common sense. I'd also like to see their social builds be less predatory in general. Lunars supposedly bring balance to other elements but I never say a Lunar negotiator or diplomat that was playable in Ex2, and that seems very on point for them conceptually. They have all these things that they <i>could</i> be if they would just kill this preconception of them all being wild celestial hillbillies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:25:59-08:00","id":345956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345839#post345839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I really mean is...if animals are getting somewhat &quot;proprietary&quot; techniques that probably stack with Charms, it makes it much more viable and exciting to decide &quot;okay I'm going to open from ambush above in the shape of a leopard, taking advantage of its Terrible Death From Above Pounce ability, then shift into a longhorn to take advantage of its Ten-Foot Horn Gore ability.&quot; Versus 2 eds of &quot;yeah I'll just be in DBT because nothing can really compete with that&quot; or even &quot;welp the choice is really only either DBT and no Evocations or Evocations and no DBT.&quot; More option is great. Having 2 main options (DBT or Evocations) is cool but i'd definitely prefer 10 viable combat options over 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, I hadn't realized how that change would let you invest DEEPER into the Beastboy combat style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:29:26-08:00","id":345958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345939#post345939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'd like more than anything for Lunars is for them to be divorced from this barbarian thematic. Others have said that they have trouble conceiving of &quot;smart&quot; Lunars and that their intelligence charms don't support that play style. That's ridiculous to me. Lunars should be able to rock the &quot;mad genius&quot; archetype in a unique way form Solars, like the self-taught alchemist or the insane shaman who knows more than they should and isn't fettered by training or even common sense. I'd also like to see their social builds be less predatory in general. Lunars supposedly bring balance to other elements but I never say a Lunar negotiator or diplomat that was playable in Ex2, and that seems very on point for them conceptually. They have all these things that they <i>could</i> be if they would just kill this preconception of them all being wild celestial hillbillies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you read that huge post from Holden about Lunars and barbarism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:35:12-08:00","id":345961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liminals tome seem like they're going to be more &quot;rip of an arm and permanantly graft it onto my body&quot; than &quot;Absorb his biomas and then turn my arms into a tentacle&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not rehashing this argument, Rater. I've already stated my case here and over in your other thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345803#post345803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because to me, Lunars are primal and predatory, so having a Lunar gain a shape because they made a favorable contract and shook hands with their prey feels... off.<br /> It seems to me like it'd belong to a different splat, like the Chosen of Masks (were those shapeshifters? Or were they focused on literal masks? I can't recall. Anyway, e.g. an exigent of Koh the Face Stealer)</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of you are too focused on the basic, default power which is basic and default precisely because it is most iconic to both Hosts. That doesn't mean more convenient options can't be made available to them, and in fact those options are still very much peripheral precisely because they're not the default. They are masteries you have to earn, not options you are obligated to buy.<br /> <br /> For a Sidereal, it would be like needing to weave Astrological masks, blessings and curses at the Loom of Fate, and then progressing to the point where they can whip those things up anywhere in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:44:43-08:00","id":345970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345956#post345956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, I hadn't realized how that change would let you invest DEEPER into the Beastboy combat style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, it's a cool insight to me, too. It also raises the idea of even what is typically a DBT-/Evocations-focused Lunar possibly using some of those options to opportunistically change the context of the fight. Taking advantage of a change in the battle's tempo is great, as is forcing adversaries with fighting styles well-suited to a particular type of opponent to instead deal with something they very much weren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:49:58-08:00","id":345985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345958#post345958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest you read that huge post from Holden about Lunars and barbarism.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">It's helpful reading</a>, alright. Heck, I'll even repost it here:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'll get this out of the way so it doesn't immediately tackle the thread off a cliff and into a bottomless pit:<br /> In 3e you can play a Lunar who was born and grew up in Nexus, who joined the Guild and made a fortune in business, who regularly attends high-society galas in expensive imported Calinese silk gowns, sips tea with her pinky out, and who thinks the centralized welfare state is a pretty great idea. This is just as viable as Solar Conan. Good? Good.<br /> That said, there's a default stone-and-leather slant that colors Lunars. This is your guide to not freaking out: what's going on and why.<br /> Let's start by looking at the idea of &quot;barbarism,&quot; because people conflate a lot of stuff into that word. Let's split it up into three sub-concepts:<br /> \u2022 Ideological barbarism - barbarism-as-philosophy, barbarism as a deliberate rejection of civilization<br /> \u2022 Political barbarism - barbarism-as-lifestyle\u2014 the daily socio-economic-technological realities of groups we identify as 'barbarian' in Exalted<br /> \u2022 Stylistic barbarism - the visuals and tropes conjured up by the word 'barbarian' for us, the audience, mostly composed of fantasy readers<br /> We'll start with that first one, because it's the one people are scared to death of. Ideological barbarism is some kind of intentional &quot;barbarian ethos,&quot; of the sort that people sometimes think Conan espoused because of quotes that get tossed around\u2014 and to be fair, Conan did say things like &quot;barbarians are much more polite than civilized men, since civilized men do not think, as a matter of course, that they may have their skulls cloven in twain.&quot; Ideological barbarism is a deliberate rejection of 'civilized comforts' on philosophical grounds\u2014 a demonization of city-dwelling folks for being 'soft' and 'weak' and 'false' and generally 'non-people,' and thus valid targets for abuse. It's a platform for glorifying the lifestyle of the &quot;political barbarian&quot; (see below) and justifying the superiority of his way of life.<br /> In First Edition, the Lunars were built around ideological barbarism. It was their rock, their way of life, and their thesis as a splat.<br /> Now forget about that completely for a moment\u2014 pretend it has never crossed your mind, because we're going to look at political barbarism as something fully divorced from that concept.<br /> Political barbarism is &quot;real&quot; barbarism (as your average fantasy-fiction-consuming American would understand the term) \u2014 i.e. it's the daily realities of &quot;barbarian&quot; type peoples. In the real world, this is an incredibly diverse grouping that you really don't want to generalize about because it runs the gamut from the historical Mongols (who almost conquered the world) to the plains nations of North America to the Mayans and Olmecs, who had incredibly complex and sophisticated societies and empires, despite that they never really did much of anything with metallurgy or the wheel.<br /> We're going to simplify it down to &quot;guys who don't really build cities, or sustain themselves primarily on sedentary agriculture, or have really good metallurgy or at least not the capabilities for large-scale application thereof.&quot; I.e. the wilderness-dwelling, furry-underwear, we-call-our-boss-a-chieftain crowd.<br /> These are extremely diverse groups in Creation, as in the real world, but there are some generalities you can lay down that won't be hilariously wrong too often. Generally they're located in resource-poor regions and are exploited or marginalized by more powerful neighbors. Generally they have much stronger ties to the local spirits than 'civilized' folks do, because they have much greater need of divine protection and assistance. Generally they are impoverished in comparison to their 'civilized' neighbors. Generally some degree of predation on other communities is necessary to handle the necessities of life (you'll notice everything keeps tying back to the fact that these are people situated in resource-poor or otherwise undesirable locations).<br /> Notably, the political barbarian is usually <i>not</i> an ideological barbarian\u2014 like Conan, give him the chance to fill his pockets with jewels and indulge himself in wine, women, fine clothing, and to otherwise reap the benefits of a high-sophistication society, and he'll jump at it. There's a reason these guys raid settled, built-up locations: They want the shit those guys have.<br /> Finally, stylistic barbarism is kind of our tentpole here\u2014 there's a definite aesthetic vibe to sun-darkened skin and rippling muscles, which are on display because the character in question is just wearing some animal skins; to a character well-versed in the ways of the wilderness, with honed instincts and practical wisdom; to the idea of fast living, easy violence, and living in the moment. This often doesn't actually mesh with the realities of the political barbarian, but it's the <i>imago</i> that guides our attempts to categorize him, above.<br /> So what about Lunars?<br /> The idea in First Edition was that each splat was a dedicated aesthetic and stylistic package, except for Solars, who were highly versatile. Solars could do most everything, but if you wanted a custom-crafted experience FOCUSED on one thing, you went to the other Exalts: DBs were there for decadent political intrigue, Abyssals for gothic melodrama, and Lunars for barbaric savage fantasy. As a result, they were modeled after the stylistic barbarian, and to really hammer the experience home, were built as ideological barbarians. They were philosophically anti-civilization and anti-intellectual. They were barbarians because &quot;civilization makes you weak.&quot;<br /> 3e Lunars are not ideological barbarians. Many of them were not born to barbarian peoples (although many were) and have no particular fondness for or attachment to a minimalist frontier lifestyle. They enjoy luxury as much as any other Exalt.<br /> 3e Lunars also can't quite be said to be political barbarians. I mean, some of them were! Because political barbarians are marginal peoples, they often don't have much in the way of resources to exploit\u2014 the Realm often looks at them as nuisance groups or potential slave labor pools rather than subjects to be assimilated and exploited. This often pushes them even further out into the wilderness, away from the Realm's sphere of influence. Alternately, those in resource-rich environments (such as the forests of the deep, deep East) are often living in hostile areas that are difficult for outsiders to reach. What that all adds up to is, &quot;a Lunar living in a barbarian society is often much more difficult for the Wyld Hunt to quickly and efficiently target than one living in the Lap.&quot; There's natural selection at work there.<br /> But think back to what we said earlier\u2014 the political barbarian is a dude who comes from certain circumstances. He's not usually ideologically married to his lifestyle\u2014 even if he says &quot;being dirt-poor is a virtue!&quot; he is generally saying that because he has no way to change his situation so he may as well take some kind of pride in it. Given the sudden ability to go out and grab whatever he wants from the world, he will generally do so\u2014 his outlook and ambitions won't remain limited and provincial for very long. So even Lunars who are born of barbarian cultures will usually get a perspective bigger than that culture in short order\u2014 either by moving outside of it directly, or by taking it over and transforming it and starting to bump into their political and supernatural neighbors, necessitating a bigger-picture view.<br /> They are, however, intended to partake of stylistic barbarism\u2014 they're designed for it from the ground up and many of their problems in Second Edition came from a deliberate attempt to reject this, I think as a result of conflating it with the other two kinds of barbarism. The fact of the matter is, to the degree that the Exalted splats echo other source material, Lunars are werewolves, tribal legends, and pagan culture-heroes. They're supposed to look rough-edged compared to the more refined Solars; their Attribute magic is supposed to look raw and powerful compared to the deft, polished sheen of Ability magic; their shapeshifting points to a primal font of imagery and aptitude\u2014 their archetypes are &quot;warrior, trickster, shaman.&quot;<br /> You can put a twist on this and have Lunar who emphasizes polished sophistication (same as you can have a heavily-armored Sidereal)\u2014 you absolutely can! The Vikings were one of the earlier cultures to have both lawyers and lawsuits. Nothing up there says Lunars have to be simple or dumb. But there's a lot of stuff in the Lunar design that pushes toward a powerful, primal, nature-saturated set of iconography.<br /> The trick, of course, is answering the question &quot;Well, why?&quot; If they tend to get a bigger view of the world and a greater ability to achieve their ambitions than the average tribal dude, why would they continue to hang around and mess with margin cultures? 1e answered &quot;because they are barbarians on an ideological level\u2014 they have a philosophical devotion to the SUPERIORITY of that lifestyle.&quot;<br /> That's not the answer 3e is going for. There are some things about 3e Lunars we're not ready to reveal yet, but in general, what we're looking at is to retain some of the baked-in barbarian iconography\u2014 it's a VERY strong wellspring of concepts and images to play with, and I think we'd be fools to discard it in favor of something more amorphous or shallow\u2014 and to maintain the setting phenomenon of heavy Lunar involvement with politically barbaric cultures (note that &quot;heavy&quot; is not &quot;exclusive&quot;). The impetus to such involvement in 3e comes from the history that has shaped the Lunars, and the realities of their current position in Creation. What that means is that, yes, a Lunar may decide to burn down a city or tear up a road\u2014 but if he does so, he has a specific reason for it, because Lunars aren't motivated by the idea that &quot;cities and roads are bad.&quot;<br /> Why even do it this way at all, if there are so many thorns to navigate around? Mostly because it's <i>cool</i>. I've been working on Liminals for most of the day today, basking in how awesome it is to get to play with <i>all</i> these peripheral themes branching out from the core idea of Frankenstein\u2014 clone stories, alienation stories, stories about belonging\u2014 and reflecting, occasionally, on how the werewolf gets an even broader range of stuff to play with if you blow it up enough\u2014 never mind bringing in things like the Anansi stories or Robert E. Howard's evocative writing to back it up. All Exalt types need a strong well of iconography to draw on, and it would be foolish not to go mining in a vein as rich as the one the old school Lunars offered up.<br /> I was going to go into the particulars of Lunar-barbarian involvement in 3e in this post but it's already like, jesus, almost 2,000 words long? If I keep going much more I'll have to revive Ink Monkeys and make it a blog post. So how about instead, I open the floor to questions and discussion? If you want to know more about why Lunars are positioned the way they are, shoot. If you don't like the idea of barbarian anything, let's look at the reasons why it may not have been presented in an appealing manner in the past. The shorter and simpler your post, the more likely it is to get a response. Also, before posting it, scroll back up to the top and read the second paragraph again, because it didn't stop being true over the course of the last 1700 words.<br /> Let the posting commence! <hr /><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I guess my first question would be, can you possibly give an example of a politically barbaric Lunar?</div>It would be tough to do so, because it doesn't really apply to Lunars\u2014 it's not that Lunars <i>are</i> politically barbarian so much as that some of them come from that background, and many of them interact with such groups. But like all Exalts, they're individuals that are bigger than their backstory, or very quickly become that way.<br /> The takeaway here should not be &quot;Lunars are barbarians,&quot; that is false. A Lunar interacting with a barbarian culture is generally going to be moving through it as a hero or patron or god, standing <i>above</i> the barbarian peoples, rather than among them.<br /> edit: A true &quot;Lunar barbarian&quot; is probably going to be about as common as a Sidereal patriot. That is to say, it's possible, but not tremendously likely\u2014 their post-Exaltation experiences are going to exert a lot of pressure to distance them from their cultural background and push them toward a bigger perspective. <hr /> The British considered the Chinese to be barbaric backwards people speaking gibberish. The Chinese considered the British to be uncultured smelly barbarians. Ultimately the word is a slur meaning &quot;you're too stupid to appreciate my cultural values, which are the correct ones.&quot; But that's not a useful position for us because we're proceeding from the desire to capture a set of aesthetics and moods (which neither the Chinese nor British fit, and which are kinda culturally insensitive, but still hella fun to play with and deeply rooted in the pulp fantasy source material of the game). <hr /> Plenty of civilized places are also like &quot;fuck the Realm,&quot; usually because it has its boot on their neck. Very few places actually like the Realm. The Lunars have a far more personal grudge against the Realm, and marginal tribal groups are one of their primary weapons of choice against it because it fits very well with their collective aptitudes and attitude, and the strategic necessities they find themselves facing.<br /> (Ironically, one of the best tools by which a Lunar can harness a barbarian culture into a weapon is by cultivating or stressing a purist barbarian ideology, which the Lunar in question probably doesn't really buy into. Just about no culture really has the kind of PURE barbarian ideology shown in the 1e book\u2014 anything like that is generally an expression of cultural superiority, and is particular to THAT culture, not to that culture and all other cultures vaguely like it.) <hr /><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">In any case, I think a sidebar on this might be useful in the 3e Lunars book, especially if there are any Lunars who still spout Ideological Barbarism around.</div>There probably are. But note that these aren't terms/categories you'll probably ever see me mentioning again\u2014 certainly they won't show up in a book. I'm mostly breaking it down this way to get people accustomed to <i>not</i> automatically conflating &quot;barbarian&quot; with &quot;frothing lunatic looking to burn down all the cities and make everyone sleep on the ground.&quot;<br /> As John pointed out to me recently, the native American nations are kind of a good example of a &quot;barbaric&quot; group with some ideological elements. Note that the various nations <i>enthusiastically</i> adopted the horse, the gun, and various other European things that either provided them with luxury or made supporting their preferred way of life easier, but then wanted nothing to do with anything that would shift that lifestyle into some radically different mode (i.e. they were not interested in milling, mining, share-cropping, etc) \u2014 to say nothing of having their culture or traditions paved over or relocating themselves.<br /> But that's still a very far cry from &quot;tear down all the cities, salt the earth where they stood.&quot; Probably you'll see some Lunars like that\u2014 Exalts are prone to extreme expressions of their favored ideology because they can actually implement those expressions\u2014 but you won't see a majority of Lunars like that. <hr /> (The Native American nations are also kind of a funky subject of examination because they violate one of the major tenets of the sort of 'barbarism' we're talking about\u2014 and this also applied to the big Mesoamerican empires. Specifically, even though they had mostly stone age technology, they were <i>not</i> occupying marginal, resource-poor land situated next to much more powerful, wealthy, and successful neighbors. They were, in fact, far more comfortable and successful than the European settlers for a good long time\u2014 they had plenty of food, comfortable shelter, and all their ducks in a row while the colonists were still shitting into their water supply upstream from their settlements and then wondering why they kept getting sick and dying in droves. The Indians didn't wipe them out as soon as they appeared because to them, the colonists looked harmless, primitive, and kind of half-retarded at first. It took generations for the colonists to build up enough infrastructure to turn the tables on the natives.) <hr /><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I was merely curious how does that help in making daiklaves or repairing the weather controls in Rathess or in any other thing that requires a bit more specialized knowledge than &quot;hammer, nail, hit&quot; assuming a Lunar would not be out of place doing any of those things.</div>Shapeshifting doesn't help you with those things. (Well, I mean, maybe you could turn into a mouse to crawl inside a sky mantis tower and jigger some delicate parts back into alignment by hand? I dunno. Mostly it doesn't.)<br /> It's not like Lunars have some kind of special brain damage that makes them less-able to learn things than other Exalts. They can study Lore, Craft, Occult, sure. Their magic isn't the best in the world at building stuff, although they have stuff to help with it. They're certainly not the peers of the Solars in that category or anything (but then, who is?).<br /> Generally speaking, as a group, Lunars are less dependent on external props than anyone else\u2014 from artifacts to infrastructure\u2014 and this is one reason why they tend to favor simple, robust tools that are either very difficult to break, or which are easy to replace.<br /> That said, keep in mind\u2014 they have Intelligence Charms. You will, from time to time, see Lunar Tony Stark building amazing shit in a cave, out of scraps. But as a whole they don't trend toward sophisticated big-scale manufacturing projects, in large part because the majority of Lunars don't like doing <i>anything</i> that requires them to set up an immobile and semi-permanent base of operations, like a fully-stocked-and-kitted artificer's workshop. It's more common to see a Lunar set up a temporary work site, build a daiklave or some armor or some similar piece of personal kit for himself or for someone else, and then break down the site, hide any of the components he can't easily replace, and then move on until he needs it again some years later. Most Lunars operate on wartime footing at all times, and they are all priority targets.*<br /> *There are exceptions to all these things, and they tend to be interesting subjects in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Having read that now (or having read it before), it's possible kindledRadical still takes issue with it. If so, it would help to narrow down to what those issues are in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  To the best of my knowledge, Rater and kindledRadical are not the same. 12-20-2014, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:51:36-08:00","id":345987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345970#post345970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, it's a cool insight to me, too. It also raises the idea of even what is typically a DBT-/Evocations-focused Lunar possibly using some of those options to opportunistically change the context of the fight. Taking advantage of a change in the battle's tempo is great, as is forcing adversaries with fighting styles well-suited to a particular type of opponent to instead deal with something they very much weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opportunistically changing the context of a fight is also why I want to see more options for acquiring Heart's Blood without needing to kill a target.<br /> <br /> Because maybe you can't kill them... yet. Maybe instead you can seduce them, steal from them, get the better of them in a court of law, defeat them in a child's card game... anything at all where you have the advantage.<br /> <br /> Then you take the secretly stolen Heart's Blood and leverage that to give you new advantages in conflicts where you might have had poor odds. Use their form's strength against them, learn their secrets, unerringly track them by blood they haven't shed (yet), trick their allies with their face, seduce their wives or husbands...<br /> <br /> Become the Trickster Animal Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:20:41-08:00","id":346026,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the link, Gaius!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:24:20-08:00","id":346027,"title":"","content":"I'd like a way to get my beast-weapon and beast-armor from my own Spirit Shape / Totem without having to hunt down and murder the closest mortal equivalent.<br /> <br /> Not because I'm opposed to killing, but because &quot;killing my kindred spirit&quot; never sat right with me. I am a Wolf already, so why should I kill a wolf to become Wolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> It might be nice to instead have a Face Yourself ritual, where you fight your own Totem and symbolically overcome yourself, so that you can make your trophy-gear from yourself.<br /> <br /> This might be related to the final two options I listed in the original thread post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:40:07-08:00","id":346037,"title":"","content":"Having read this I still have some reservations about it as a direction because it's sort of unclear to me still what parts of the &quot;barbarian&quot; theme Holden is wanting to preserve and which he want excised or watered down. Also, a lot of these examples of &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures like the Mongols were extremely advanced in a cultural and technological sense <i>in their own time</i>. The recurve bow and saddle stirrups were the six-gun and iron horse of their age. So to what meaningful degree are these cultures &quot;barbaric?&quot; Barbarian in the &quot;political barbarian&quot; sense just means the &quot;other&quot; it seems. If Lunars are going to be the exalts of the politically disenfranchised then <i>that</i> idea might have some merit, but what it really seems like is the same bullshit I heard in Ex2 where people told me &quot;well you can play a non-combat Lunar if you want nothing is stopping you&quot; while also giving me like five charms to play that concept which were objectively shit and piling on new mechanics to support the hulk-smash archetype that was the only powerful choice in Ex2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:18:23-08:00","id":346057,"title":"","content":"( fyi, I have read the post in the past ).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345961#post345961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of you are too focused on the basic, default power which is basic and default precisely because it is most iconic to both Hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how'd you'd think that, but I don't think so*. I mean, I like sophisticated Lunars. I like Exalted Moder Lunars too. But there's something about <i>gaining heart's blood</i> in such a &quot;polite&quot; and modern manner that really turns me off. The main thing that attracts me to the splat is the animalistic brutality and ruthlessness - not just in the physical sense (hell, my main Lunar is a social crocodile that metaphorically death-rolls his opponents in social combat). The juxtaposition of the civilized with the animalistic. It's just that some of those methods seem too removed from the personal and primal nature of the Sacred Hunt (and thus going only towards the civilized, having neary a trace of the animalistic). Breaking a deal or an Oath seems more in line with Demon's soul-pacts than it does with animistic shapeshifters (even those living in society like Seven-Devil Clever). It doesn't strike me as anywhere near <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">stylistic barbarism.</span></span><br /> <br /> I mean, if it was an appearance charm unrelated to regular shapeshifting, or an anima power, I'd have no problem with it. It's the fact that you get <i>heart's blood</i> out of it that I find off. Especially when coupled with some of the other heart's blood enhancing effects (memories, fates, ability dots).<br /> <br /> Disclaimers: Of course, I'm definitely not saying that it's badwrong fun or anything. I'd just prefer it if those kinds of options stayed homebrew, and it's not something I'd berate people over.<br /> <br /> *then again I'm cleared biased towards myself here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=345961#post345961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't mean more convenient options can't be made available to them, and in fact those options are still very much peripheral precisely because they're not the default. They are masteries you have to earn, not options you are obligated to buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about being against more options, I said <i>some</i> of those options (that are mostly fanon at the moment anyway) seem out-of-place to me for the splat.<br /> <br /> Though I haven't seen 3e Lunars yet, and they're apparently going through some thematic changes beyond what is detailed in the post, so my opinion is subject to change depending on presentation. Who knows, the sacred hunt might be pretty different in next edition, since Lunars are moving away from Animal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:18:44-08:00","id":346058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346037#post346037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read this I still have some reservations about it as a direction because it's sort of unclear to me still what parts of the &quot;barbarian&quot; theme Holden is wanting to preserve and which he want excised or watered down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the club.<br /> <br /> We can at least tell that Lunar Charms are going to encourage the stereotypical &quot;barbarian&quot; image. In this thread, I've spoken about those possibilities.<br /> <br /> Wearing animal hides, bones and feathers as functional armor <i>and</i> as a way to more easily use the forms of animals other than your Totem. Magical tattoos. Creating lingering auras of fear or desire from actions like pissing on a tree, gouging claw-marks into a door, scarring a messenger, or smearing your blood on a rock. Berserker fury. Magically binding blood-oaths. Witch-curses.<br /> <br /> Others have mentioned vision quests, dreamwalking, and teaching-riddles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a lot of these examples of &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures like the Mongols were extremely advanced in a cultural and technological sense <i>in their own time</i>. </div> </div> </div>You need to go back and re-read his essay more carefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:22:17-08:00","id":346061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346027#post346027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a way to get my beast-weapon and beast-armor from my own Spirit Shape / Totem without having to hunt down and murder the closest mortal equivalent.<br /> <br /> Not because I'm opposed to killing, but because &quot;killing my kindred spirit&quot; never sat right with me. I am a Wolf already, so why should I kill a wolf to become Wolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> It might be nice to instead have a Face Yourself ritual, where you fight your own Totem and symbolically overcome yourself, so that you can make your trophy-gear from yourself.<br /> <br /> This might be related to the final two options I listed in the original thread post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be super-duper down for this.<br /> Also Monster Hunter Lunars (with Evocations). All of my yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:26:27-08:00","id":346062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346037#post346037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read this I still have some reservations about it as a direction because it's sort of unclear to me still what parts of the &quot;barbarian&quot; theme Holden is wanting to preserve and which he want excised or watered down. Also, a lot of these examples of &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures like the Mongols were extremely advanced in a cultural and technological sense <i>in their own time</i>. The recurve bow and saddle stirrups were the six-gun and iron horse of their age..</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the notion of ideological barbarians is kind of ridiculous and ahistorical and only works in fiction that you don't look at too closely. <i>Maybe </i>the Mongols thought there was great virtue to living on horseback versus in cities, but given the chance they definitely took over cities (and destroyed the ones who refused to pay a tithe to them), amassed incredible riches, and held court.<br /> <br /> Most groups that are &quot;barbarian&quot; are really political and, often, stylistically barbarian. They're in certain circumstances but they don't hold their have-not position as an inherently good thing. I think in Creation, groups that are considered &quot;barbarian&quot; are going to be political and to a degree stylistically barbarian. Ideological barbarism doesn't make a lot of sense, ever, unless you have really really good reasons to hate civilization (see: Garou beliefs in WtA, where cities and industrialization are literally killing Gaia). And that was a big problem with 1e Lunars: borrowing heavily from WtA as an inspiration for character aesthetic, while not really getting that the Garou environmentalist/anti-industry themes make sense when you view the natural world and spirit world as precious living things being deliberately killed by pollution and stasis. But those are not themes in Creation, for a number of reasons (Crusaders of the Machine God tried to bring this in a bit as well, with Autochthonian industrial pollution being super-toxic to Creation's spirits, and that bit was was fucking <i>terrible </i>not least because how out of place it was).<br /> <br /> Sine those major WtA themes are not present in Creation, it was and is inappropriate to port them into Lunars and really added nothing to their themes - it just made them sort of scattered (and we got it a bit in one of the 2e Silver Pact camps, and it made no fucking sense there either).<br /> <br /> Basically, I expect ideological barbarism to be super culture-specific if it exists in Creation at all and political and stylistic are going to be the things played up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346037#post346037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to what meaningful degree are these cultures &quot;barbaric?&quot; Barbarian in the &quot;political barbarian&quot; sense just means the &quot;other&quot; it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm is the best example of the notion of Empire in Exalted. It's Rome at its height (both as a Republic and as an Empire); it's China during the Han and Tang Golden ages; it's (in different ways) both Tokugawa and Meiji Japan; it's Bismarckian Prussia. This is important to note because what is &quot;barbarian&quot; is often defined by the culture that views itself as the most civilized.<br /> <br /> Thus what is &quot;barbarian&quot; is basically &quot;the people the Realm dominates by its presence, versus dominating directly.&quot; The satrapies are not really barbarian in a strict sense; they're more analogous to the Roman Provinces, where Germany is the barbarian. The Realm is America, where the Native Americans are barbarian. The Realm is Saxon England, where the Vikings are barbarian. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:48:37-08:00","id":346077,"title":"","content":"...Too Terrestrial. [/Hedley Lamarr]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:04:10-08:00","id":346083,"title":"","content":"Rater: Steven Universe Gem fusion is the first thing that comes to mind. This amuses me.<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: this is basically what I mean by saying that they are the &quot;other,&quot; just that the ruling class or centralized power which considers itself authoritative is the one who decides what is &quot;barbaric&quot; behavior. What I'm having a hard time with is how that translates into themes and mechanics, though, since this is essentially a <i>subjective</i> term. Like if this were the qualifier for Lunar exaltation anyone might qualify. A Haltan might exalt Lunar because they see themselves as opposed to the authority of the Realm, but a minor tribesman might also exalt because they see themselves opposing Halta.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see this &quot;idealistic barbarism&quot; falling to the wayside because it does make very little sense, but what I'm left with just seems so amorphous. Like if they want to support &quot;stylistic&quot; barbarism which is animal hides and feather headresses then strictly speaking I don't think this would do that, since if the Realm is Han dynasty then the people of the West with their late-Victorian garb are equally &quot;barbaric.&quot; Barbaric in this sense of the word is not a concise style, yet Holden seems to want to preserve that feel while removing its justification.<br /> <br /> Though for the record I'm totally on board with the idea of Lunar swashbucklers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:23:47-08:00","id":346110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346083#post346083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zelbinnean: this is basically what I mean by saying that they are the &quot;other,&quot; just that the ruling class or centralized power which considers itself authoritative is the one who decides what is &quot;barbaric&quot; behavior. What I'm having a hard time with is how that translates into themes and mechanics, though, since this is essentially a <i>subjective</i> term. Like if this were the qualifier for Lunar exaltation anyone might qualify. A Haltan might exalt Lunar because they see themselves as opposed to the authority of the Realm, but a minor tribesman might also exalt because they see themselves opposing Halta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Dynasts and Guild Princes can Exalt as Lunars I doubt needing to be a member of an Othered group will be a criterion. <br /> <br /> I really hope hard, splat-specific criteria are never written. If a character seems Lunar-ish and solves problems more by their own innate talents versus trained skills...they're Lunary. Hard criteria for Celestials just imposes creative barriers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346083#post346083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad to see this &quot;idealistic barbarism&quot; falling to the wayside because it does make very little sense, but what I'm left with just seems so amorphous. Like if they want to support &quot;stylistic&quot; barbarism which is animal hides and feather headresses then strictly speaking I don't think this would do that, since if the Realm is Han dynasty then the people of the West with their late-Victorian garb are equally &quot;barbaric.&quot; Barbaric in this sense of the word is not a concise style, yet Holden seems to want to preserve that feel while removing its justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're referring to as amorphous. <br /> <br /> I think stylistic barbarism is going to be in the context of what we might see as lacking a formality of dress that was quite prevalent in ex. Rome (togas and other formal attire), England (powdered wigs) or feudal Japan (kimono). But to me it's important that both, say, Zulu and Inuit looks are given weight; it's really easy to fall into stylistic barbarism as only temperate/tropical forms of attire; it's as much the Iroquois as it is the Mayans and Comanche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:37:53-08:00","id":346120,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is that if your character is Iroquois and living in the age and place where the Iroquois were undisputed masters of their territories then there isn't anything &quot;barbaric&quot; about that. Exalted has a lot of this because its a massive setting with many different cultures all claiming to be &quot;authoritative&quot; within their own realms, so nearly anything could be &quot;barbaric&quot; and thus it's not really a useful theme. Once you inject cultural relativism into the setting (which is already there) there is no way to make cultural barbarism mean anything from the player's perspective. If they wanted to pursue the theme of all Lunars being opposing forces to an established power that might work, but that is not barbarism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:40:33-08:00","id":346128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346026#post346026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the link, Gaius!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! Also, apologies for getting you mixed up with Rater in that post; edited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346037#post346037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are going to be the exalts of the politically disenfranchised then <i>that</i> idea might have some merit, but what it really seems like is the same bullshit I heard in Ex2 where people told me &quot;well you can play a non-combat Lunar if you want nothing is stopping you&quot; while also giving me like five charms to play that concept which were objectively shit and piling on new mechanics to support the hulk-smash archetype that was the only powerful choice in Ex2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was a consequence of a different problem. I mean, throughout most of 2nd edition, there were <i>lots</i> of Abilities/Attributes that were pretty bereft of Charms. In the corebook, Solar Larceny had exactly six Charms going for it. Solar Dodge had <i>four</i>. Part of this owed to the core systems and rules themselves,* part of this may have owed to developmental priorities,** and part of this probably owed to a number of different factors and circumstances. For comparison, take a gander at <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/589448\" target=\"_blank\">this KS update</a>. There are <i>eighteen</i> Dodge Charms in there. We know the set's gone through a rewrite, granted, but they're definitely going for a hefty number of options in all areas. Given what they've mentioned elsewhere (see my second footnote), I don't foresee them withholding this philosophy from other splats. Mental -- and Social, to a slightly lesser degree*** -- Attributes shouldn't be the red-headed step-children**** of the Lunar Charmset in EX3.<br /> <br /> * When writing Charms, you need to refer to those core systems/mechanics: you will either hang the effects off of hooks the system gives you or invent your own new bit of mechanics. If those systems aren't robust enough to give you plenty of hooks -- and the 2e systems often weren't -- then that's going to mean either writing Charms that very quickly exhaust everything one can possibly do in that mechanical area, or more Charms in which you have to invent your own bits of mechanics to get an effect you want. This means they're going to tend to be wordier, which means fewer Charms the writers can squeeze out of a given block of word count. Word count basically always being at a premium, this generally means the Charm writer either bites the bullet and goes with those wordier Charms or kind of avoids that mechanical area. Where the writer <i>does</i> bite the bullet, there might still be further complexity: writers on future splat books need to either repeat those mechanics because it's not fair to refer players to mechanics from outside of the core book or come up with a different way of mechanically representing it. It also probably means more errata and/or screwy circumstances, as it may mean you now have a bunch of different mechanics across several splats for doing what is basically the same thing.*****<br /> <br /> ** This is not really a shot at Mr. Chambers, just that John and Holden are certainly placing a higher priority on having oodles and oodles of Charms. Like, I remember some thought they had about fitting in multiple elements within each Ability for the Terrestrial Charmset, despaired at how much word count that would use, and then delighted on remembering that they get to decide word count allocations. That's encouraging.<br /> <br /> *** Also not counting broken stuff, like Pretty Kitty Revolution.<br /> <br /> **** Big apologies to red-headed step-children everywhere!<br /> <br /> ***** <i>How</i> did this footnote get bigger than the body of my actual post? o_o<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346110#post346110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Dynasts and Guild Princes can Exalt as Lunars I doubt needing to be a member of an Othered group will be a criterion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, this is definitively the case.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden, at the beginning of that giant essay</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3e you can play a Lunar who was born and grew up in Nexus, who joined the Guild and made a fortune in business, who regularly attends high-society galas in expensive imported Calinese silk gowns, sips tea with her pinky out, and who thinks the centralized welfare state is a pretty great idea. This is just as viable as Solar Conan. Good? Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Footnotes in footnotes! 12-20-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:44:56-08:00","id":346134,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this answers anything you've asked, but obviously a person is going to have to examine the question of &quot;what trappings/themes do we consider barbaric&quot; from an OOC standpoint and yes this is inevitably (and probably unfortunately) going to be colored by 21st-century Western notions of what &quot;civilization&quot; entails. There's cultural reasons for this, not the least being that Lunars have historically wanted to be in the savage fantasy genre, and probably that will remain a central influence even if it's no longer virtually required for every character.<br /> <br /> In any case I think Holden described the trappings pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:15:29-08:00","id":346153,"title":"","content":"Zelbinnean: Pretty much <i>exactly</i> that. I don't want what we (and I am going to make an assumption here) as European-centric people think of as &quot;barbaric&quot; to be placed on some sort of pedestal as being the &quot;barbaric cultures of exalted.&quot; Exalted is a <i>huge</i> canon and people from Rathis, from Halta, from Ang Teng and others should all be able to feel very much like the &quot;normal&quot; people in their own communities. I just really don't like the idea of Lunars being associated with specific cultures, also. Holden said he wouldn't do this but at the same time if he actually wants to enforce this &quot;stylistic barbarism&quot; theme then I think it's very possible that the Lunars book will be all exalts from pseudo-indian or pseudo-african tribes.<br /> <br /> Basically, I just really want there to be an <i>actual example</i> in the Lunar book of a functioning Lunar who is not wearing pelts and the skulls of their enemies just because of aesthetic. Like people are already saying it's <i>possible</i> to play a not-barbaric Lunar, it has never been <i>supported</i> though and that is a very narrow character concept to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:31:49-08:00","id":346190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346153#post346153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I just really want there to be an <i>actual example</i> in the Lunar book of a functioning Lunar who is not wearing pelts and the skulls of their enemies just because of aesthetic. Like people are already saying it's <i>possible</i> to play a not-barbaric Lunar, it has never been <i>supported</i> though and that is a very narrow character concept to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird to me that you're acting like 2e Lunars didn't do this (and didn't let you play a non-combat character), because it totally did. 2e Lunars was a deliberate and categorical rejection of everything about 1e Lunars, so it's extremely difficult to apply a <i>specific</i> criticism to both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:39:02-08:00","id":346195,"title":"","content":"Seven Devil Clever has been there since 1e.<br /> <img src=\"http://seventh-legion.net/images/thumb/9/97/SevenDevilsClever.jpg/180px-SevenDevilsClever.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Edit: Also there's Anja Silverclaws. And Magnificent Jaguar isn't very skulls-on-belty either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-20-2014, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:45:28-08:00","id":346203,"title":"","content":"Hm, another thing for my Lunars wishlist: I don't want them to be able to create Beastmen via goat fucking any more. They can do it other ways, maybe ritualistic giving of blood or other some such mythical/magical shenanigans, but if they're still goat fuckers, I'm not going to touch them with a ten foot pole, and will actively discourage my circle of friends from playing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:51:55-08:00","id":346205,"title":"","content":"I can't speak to what Ex1 had of Lunars since I never played it, but the only non-combat build I've ever seen a Lunar take that was successful compared to a celestial of similar experience was the pretty kitty build which did exactly one thing. I understand the reasons for narrow charm focus, it's been discussed here even, but what has always been missing was any sort of developer support for these character types. I suppose you're right that there has been an example present but perhaps that's not good enough by itself. if the split of combat/non-combat charms is something like 90-10 then you're playing a combat exalt, and I don't think that's good form when other play styles are just as rewarding in the system. Lunars could not play a powerful crafter in Ex2, nor a powerful bureaucrat, nor a powerful trader. Saying that &quot;you can play these characters too&quot; is meaningless if you give no magic powers in your book to excel in those positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:07:19-08:00","id":346215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346153#post346153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want what we (and I am going to make an assumption here) as European-centric people think of as &quot;barbaric&quot; to be placed on some sort of pedestal as being the &quot;barbaric cultures of exalted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is what the savage fantasy genre did, for good or ill. And that is the direct inspiration for Lunars, for good or ill.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't think of it as a pedestal so much as a reference point for the vast majority of Exalted consumers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346153#post346153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden said he wouldn't do this but at the same time if he actually wants to enforce this &quot;stylistic barbarism&quot; theme then I think it's very possible that the Lunars book will be all exalts from pseudo-indian or pseudo-african tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be willfully ignoring his statements about a Guild prince Exalting as a Lunar from the aforementioned post...<br /> <br /> &quot;Enforce&quot; is a pretty strong word. I would be completely shocked to get anything on the scale of 1e ideological barbarism requirements in 3e Lunars, except with &quot;ideological&quot; scratched out and replaced with &quot;stylistic.&quot; I have no reason to believe that the design goal will entail concept limitation or aesthetic pigeonholing. If nothing else it should be establishing a thematic baseline. After all, Solar inspiration comes from Herakles, Achilles, etc. but nobody is going to say that Agatha Heterodyne is not a potentially great example of Solar inspiration either. And it's relevant that Sun Wukong is the quintessential Lunar, but he's hardly a &quot;barbarian&quot; as far as culture or trappings are concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346153#post346153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I just really want there to be an <i>actual example</i> in the Lunar book of a functioning Lunar who is not wearing pelts and the skulls of their enemies just because of aesthetic. Like people are already saying it's <i>possible</i> to play a not-barbaric Lunar, it has never been <i>supported</i> though and that is a very narrow character concept to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven Devils Clever would like a word. I would also hate to see the notion of First Age Ma-Ha-Suchi completely deleted, because aside from the dumb shit he was still a poncy socialite who charmed people with sheer animal magnetism over anything else. Gerd Marrow-Eater is another good example of more of a middle ground since the Haslanti League has some north-barbarian stylistic trappings but is presented in a very federal-power sort of way.\u200b I consider the Haslanti to be the Vendel to the Icewalkers' Vesten, for a 7th Sea-based comparison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346205#post346205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars could not play a powerful crafter in Ex2, nor a powerful bureaucrat, nor a powerful trader. Saying that &quot;you can play these characters too&quot; is meaningless if you give no magic powers in your book to excel in those positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that was that for all intent and purposes, 2e had no bureaucratic system rules until its final days. Lunars sucking at crafting never made any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:07:38-08:00","id":346216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346205#post346205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak to what Ex1 had of Lunars since I never played it, but the only non-combat build I've ever seen a Lunar take that was successful compared to a celestial of similar experience was the pretty kitty build which did exactly one thing. I understand the reasons for narrow charm focus, it's been discussed here even, but what has always been missing was any sort of developer support for these character types. I suppose you're right that there has been an example present but perhaps that's not good enough by itself. if the split of combat/non-combat charms is something like 90-10 then you're playing a combat exalt, and I don't think that's good form when other play styles are just as rewarding in the system. Lunars could not play a powerful crafter in Ex2, nor a powerful bureaucrat, nor a powerful trader. Saying that &quot;you can play these characters too&quot; is meaningless if you give no magic powers in your book to excel in those positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you say &quot;celestial of similar experience&quot; I can only assume you mean &quot;Solar&quot; because Lunars curbstomped pre-errata Sidereals and Abyssals in many fields in 2e. Solars were, of course, brokenly amazing compared to nearly everybody, but that was a problem with Solars, not a problem with Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'm skeptical that 2e lunars had a 90/10 split of combat/non-combat charms. It would be interesting to see a direct comparison between the Lunar and Solar books on that front, actually! But I am off on Christmas holiday and don't have my stuff with me, so it will have to wait. Lunars certainly <i>had</i> plenty of charms for non-combat stuff, and almost none of their 2e charms had a &quot;barbarian&quot; aesthetic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:19:52-08:00","id":346225,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd really like for Lunars (and it's very probable that we're going to be getting it anyway) is more charms that are broadly applicable or flexible. Not in the sense of excellencies, but in the sense of Tool Hand Technique - it can climb, it can stab, and it can saw! Or [that one that lets you see through the eyes of your prey], it's great for everything from spying to aligning archery/thrown shots that would otherwise be a random guess (hell, it can even let a blind Lunar see again).<br /> <br /> Highlighting their adaptability by having Charms open up options by having their strength be breadth rather than (or in addition to) potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-20-2014, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:20:22-08:00","id":346226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars could not play a powerful crafter in Ex2, nor a powerful bureaucrat, nor a powerful trader. Saying that &quot;you can play these characters too&quot; is meaningless if you give no magic powers in your book to excel in those positions.</div> </div> </div> </div> If the system can't let you be good at that stuff without Charms, then it has already failed. I feel as though the Lunar space is one in which such endeavors are complemented by what they are, rather than expressed by it. I mean, what would &quot;Lunar bureaucrat/trader&quot; even look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T17:35:02-08:00","id":346250,"title":"","content":"Though I'm coming around on a few fronts I stand by my statement that Ex2 Lunars could not be good crafters or bureaucrats and that this was a failing of the MoEP: Lunars book. To answer Isator Levi's question I think there are several answers that all <i>could</i> be distinctly Lunar in theme, <i>if</i> we had charm support for them. The anarchistic economist who beggers the rich and drops piles of money on the poor while in Strix form would be a great trader Lunar. The village chieftain who leads his people through the difficult process of Realm &quot;relocation&quot; ala Trail of Tears but who poisons the process so that the Realm garrison forces assimilate to <i>his</i> culture ala Dances With Wolves would be a great Lunar bureaucrat. <i>Neither</i> of these ideas are possible using the pretty kitty technique that was the <i>entire </i>backbone of Ex2 Lunar social combat.<br /> <br /> Have had time to think about and having heard people's arguments, here is what I'd like: more generally useful charms. The solar splat is well rounded and allows a multitude of concepts because their charms apply in a wide variety of situations. There are a multitude of character concepts that use Speed the Wheels, not just magistrates. Lunars should bring something unique to the table, yes, but in Ex2 all of their charms reinforced a narrow character concept. This was also a big problem for Abyssals. And this should be <i>easier</i> to do when their magic is already attribute-based! I'd like more charms in Intelligence that make you &quot;think better&quot; and fewer that are unnecessarily limited to &quot;thinking better while you hunt and trap game animals.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T17:41:55-08:00","id":346270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346250#post346250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'm coming around on a few fronts I stand by my statement that Ex2 Lunars could not be good crafters or bureaucrats and that this was a failing of the MoEP: Lunars book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in no way the MoEP's fault that the Corebook completely lacked a bureaucracy system. That was a Corebook failure that wasn't resolved for, what, a <i>decade</i>? <br /> <br /> Also you could totally be a good bureaucrat, even if no Charms directly improved an &quot;X + Bureaucracy&quot; roll. I have no idea where you are getting the notion that you can't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346250#post346250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The anarchistic economist who beggers the rich and drops piles of money on the poor while in Strix form would be a great trader Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this supposed to be Robin Hood-esque? Not really sure and thus not sure how to respond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346250#post346250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The village chieftain who leads his people through the difficult process of Realm &quot;relocation&quot; ala Trail of Tears but who poisons the process so that the Realm garrison forces assimilate to <i>his</i> culture ala Dances With Wolves would be a great Lunar bureaucrat. <i>Neither</i> of these ideas are possible using the pretty kitty technique that was the <i>entire </i>backbone of Ex2 Lunar social combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could totally do this one without Pretty Kitty. But the way Appearance, MDVs, and social combat were set up, you always wanted Pretty Kitty in your back pocket just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T18:17:06-08:00","id":346277,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is that there was no charm support and without charm support you could not do those things <i>at exalted tier</i>. Literally no one wants to play a celestial exalt who's only magical ability in their chosen field is an excellency. Charms are how Exalted models the ability to be supernaturally gifted at a thing and Lunars had a wide range of potential goals that they could not be supernatural gifted at because they had no charms to supplement those actions. All pretty kitty allowed you to do was be so pretty people gave you what you wanted. Yes it was powerful but saying that's enough to satisfy the needs of social players is like saying that the Solar melee charms <i>by themselves</i> were everything the combat player needed. We all want to feel like our characters are unique and that is what charmsets allow us to do, <i>if</i> they have variety.<br /> <br /> So while it was true that the core book did not provide good rules for bureaucratic rolls the fact that no charms even attempted to support that character concept is a failure. Solars had charms that allowed them to advance that character concept long before we had Masters of Jade. If you include absolutely no charms that interact with a focus then it may as well not exist to your exaltation type because no one is going to be able to play that and feel useful in a party where everyone else is taking concepts that <i>are</i> supported by the charmset. So it is very important that in Ex3 the developers provide charms for the Lunars that are varied enough that they can support <i>many</i> playstyles that are not just barbarian beastman, not just one or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:18:15-08:00","id":346320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344283#post344283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the expansion that lets you just beat people unconscious, which is where it just becomes dominance. I feel it lacks the same mythic weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though I am onboard with things like winning riddle contests or gambling games to co-opt someone's shape. That feels like a thing that fits the trickster archetype I see some Lunars occupying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=344398#post344398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With both options, Lunars suddenly have very good reasons to wear furs and feathers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, looking cool is good enough reason for me even if the monster hunters aren't getting tangible benefits from their trophies. How can anyone argue against <a href=\"https://mlkshk-ada.kxcdn.com/r/1MAZ\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:41:21-08:00","id":346356,"title":"","content":"KindledRadial, this is a wish list for things we want to see for the Lunar Exalted we were promised.<br /> <br /> If you haven't read up on all the developer comments (check the Useful Links thread stickied to the top of the forum!) to know what those promises were, please do so now, because you're dragging the thread off-topic to discuss something everyone already discussed several months ago in a different thread.<br /> <br /> This is not a thread to debate about what barbarism means or whether it's appropriate for the Lunar Exalted. That ship has SAILED.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the event that the developers decide to read this thread, I do NOT want them to get bored reading old arguments and close the browser before they've read all of the wishes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T21:22:24-08:00","id":346440,"title":"","content":"Lunars were pretty damn bad crafters, that is true. On the other hand, basically nobody had a good crafting suite except Solars. Bureaucrats? I'll have to look at the charmset when I get back home. I bet there's a way to do it, but it probably wouldn't (and ideally shouldn't) involve charms specifically for bureaucracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:00:41-08:00","id":346458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346277#post346277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is that there was no charm support and without charm support you could not do those things <i>at exalted tier</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is simply not true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346277#post346277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while it was true that the core book did not provide good rules for bureaucratic rolls the fact that no charms even attempted to support that character concept is a failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want Charms to build system hooks instead of supporting them? That's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346277#post346277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars had charms that allowed them to advance that character concept long before we had Masters of Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were functionally rather useless and depended solely on ST fiat to work, which is not better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346440#post346440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars were pretty damn bad crafters, that is true. On the other hand, basically nobody had a good crafting suite except Solars. Bureaucrats? I'll have to look at the charmset when I get back home. I bet there's a way to do it, but it probably wouldn't (and ideally shouldn't) involve charms specifically for bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I mean obviously it deals with the Attribute in a general way. Lunars have a degree of macro-magic that was appropriate for 2e as well as weird interpersonal manipulation stuff as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:04:27-08:00","id":346462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346440#post346440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars were pretty damn bad crafters, that is true. On the other hand, basically nobody had a good crafting suite except Solars. Bureaucrats? I'll have to look at the charmset when I get back home. I bet there's a way to do it, but it probably wouldn't (and ideally shouldn't) involve charms specifically for bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Bureaucracy-impeder in the Ink Monkeys. It's an Intelligence Charm that conjures up phantom pests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:08:10-08:00","id":346464,"title":"","content":"Fine fine fine, I'll parse this out differently then:<br /> <br /> In Ex3 I want more non-violent options for the Lunars that are supported with general-use charms.<br /> <br /> Charms that allow Lunars to do <i>something</i> with large social groups even if they do not fit into the Solar bureaucrat/godking thematic would be appreciated. Perhaps Manipulation charms that allow them to set group policy through <i>popular</i> opinion rather than edict.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see smart Lunars become more of a thing as well. If they are more cagey than brainy that's fine, but if an Intelligence excellency actually makes you smarter then that provides some powerful charm concepts just in and of itself. Perhaps charms that allow them to &quot;fake&quot; proficiency in academic abilities like Lore and Occult by rolling just their Intelligence with non-charm bonus dice?<br /> <br /> And for Auto's sake give them some decent crafting. In line with the previous, perhaps they gain more benefits so long as what they produce is completely new and somewhat improvised? There's nothing in the crafting rules leaks that needs to be Solar-specific that i see and gimping them on that front was just perpetuating the Ex2 narrative that they'd built and done basically nothing since the Usurption which is a narrative the Devs have claimed they want to eliminate anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T23:20:13-08:00","id":346498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346057#post346057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I like sophisticated Lunars. I like Exalted Moder Lunars too. But there's something about <i>gaining heart's blood</i> in such a &quot;polite&quot; and modern manner that really turns me off. The main thing that attracts me to the splat is the animalistic brutality and ruthlessness - not just in the physical sense (hell, my main Lunar is a social crocodile that metaphorically death-rolls his opponents in social combat). The juxtaposition of the civilized with the animalistic. It's just that some of those methods seem too removed from the personal and primal nature of the Sacred Hunt (and thus going only towards the civilized, having neary a trace of the animalistic). Breaking a deal or an Oath seems more in line with Demon's soul-pacts than it does with animistic shapeshifters (even those living in society like Seven-Devil Clever). It doesn't strike me as anywhere near <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">stylistic barbarism.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can see a barbarian witch cutting his palm and insisting that someone else cut her palm, and they shake on a promise -- a blood-oath -- right?<br /> <br /> Well, if it's magically binding and capable of inflicting harm upon an oath-breaker (maybe it curses them with lycanthropy, or a fixed animal transformation?), could it not also exact a price by taking Heart's Blood?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said anything about being against more options, I said <i>some</i> of those options (that are mostly fanon at the moment anyway) seem out-of-place to me for the splat. </div> </div> </div>How do you feel about the one involving a contest of strength/skill or a game of chance? The Lunar and his opponent agree to a competition with set rules (even if &quot;there are no rules, just make the other guy cry Uncle&quot;, and the Lunar gains Heart's Blood if he wins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I mentioned earlier that I was cold on the idea of Compassionate Mirror Nature, since &quot;beat them unconscious&quot; was just the default violent method with less violence. The contest method can easily involve violence, but the difference is that the violence has to be consensual. You can't just ambush someone and KO them, because that's completely superior to the default method, which renders the default completely obsolete.<br /> <br /> The contest method isn't as simple as that, because you can't always convince someone to fight you on specific terms, especially not on the terms you need for victory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T01:00:01-08:00","id":346534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalkum artifacts would make it too obvious that he's a Lawgiver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would this be the case?<br /> <br /> Remember that one of the setting changes intended for Ex3 is for Artifacts to be rarer; if a Dynast finds an orichalcum daiklave, he's not gonna throw it away in favor of a jade one, <i>he's gonna snatch that shit</i>. Per Ex3, possession of orichalcum isn't necessarily an indicator of anything except that you're badass enough to hold it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T09:39:16-08:00","id":346744,"title":"","content":"What are some fictional characters that people see as inspiring Lunar concepts that they'd like to see more of? Conan has always sort of been the standard for combat builds but what about for social and mental builds? Would Walter White (Breaking Bad) make a good Lunar crafter? If you have a head canon what attracts you to it and makes you think &quot;oh yeah, this is totally a Lunar character?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T09:46:50-08:00","id":346776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346744#post346744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some fictional characters that people see as inspiring Lunar concepts that they'd like to see more of? Conan has always sort of been the standard for combat builds but what about for social and mental builds? Would Walter White (Breaking Bad) make a good Lunar crafter? If you have a head canon what attracts you to it and makes you think &quot;oh yeah, this is totally a Lunar character?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be unfriendly, but we should have threads like those already laying around, or it would be easy to make a new one.<br /> <br /> I fear that discussing and debating sources of inspiration would get in the way of simply expressing wishes we've already discovered from previous similar conversations.<br /> <br /> Please, I <i>really </i>want to keep this thread simple and direct. A place for voicing wishes rather than debating what wishes we should voice. This thread should be as easy as possible for a developer to read through for learning what we want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T10:01:37-08:00","id":346779,"title":"","content":"I suppose I have to admit that Alcina from Masters of Jade as a characteristic Lunar trader, probably even a No Moon Caste (certainly most of her tricks seem like they'd be conveyed through Wits). She doesn't even seem especially barbaric, more iconoclastic. I doubt she would have Charms specifically <i>about</i> trade (or cons), nor does she seem strictly focused on being &quot;the best&quot; at it, or even necessarily good at it (which probably helps with being drawn to Lacen Mercer). I'm not sure how to articulate it at this moment, but it does give me the vague outline of a Lunar whose sense of being idiosyncratic and an outsider is conveyed more through being unconventional and a bit of a trickster (although I also feel that the Lunar intellectual milieu, at least in the Age of Sorrows, includes a heavy dose of being very good at discerning and exploiting the vulnerable spots of people and things). It's not about being a mad scientist so much as kind of colouring outside of the lines...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T10:13:55-08:00","id":346795,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to formulate my own thesis for what the Lunars might be... I have a lot of defense for the therianthrope issue, but that's not at the heart of it. I don't really have the words, just this mental image of a person who has a certain wild look to them, not necessarily in how they're dressed but in their body language, sitting laconically upon a fence or a crumbling wall, looking down at you with a grin, probably framed against a backdrop of the night sky which softly illuminates them with a sense of subtle but energetic and even a bit dangerous beauty.<br /> <br /> Really, the main reason I defend the therianthropy as core to the Lunar is because I view it as enhancing that image more than generic or body horror shapeshifting does; if Sun Wukong has a place as inspiration to Lunars, to me it's because the combinaion of human actors to portray him with animal features very effectively conveys somebody who lives on the edge of convention and reason and society. Hell, even if the specifics of what his powers actually are seem better placed elsewhere, some of the narratives of how he got them (such as crashing around the Underworld until he took his name off of the book defining when things die, or being sealed in a sacred cauldron and emerging unscathed), <i>those</i> things feel very Lunar (which is not to say they should be ways Lunars get powers).<br /> <br /> I keep feeling as though that central image I have looks a lot like Ryoko Hakubi. Who... I don't <i>think</i> is an actual cat person, but seems to still have a lot of the anime conventions conveyed by such in her, playing into my sense of what the juxtaposition between human and animal gives to Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T10:54:38-08:00","id":346840,"title":"","content":"To draw a bit from Isator Levi, what if whereas Solars get charms that enhance or empower their own intimacies Lunars got charms for opposing the intimacies of others? Like a social overdrive (though we may or may not see actual overdrives in Ex3) that restores motes or gives bonuses when <i>challenging</i> intimacies? Something to represent that Lunar socials are so tricky that even when they are campaigning against your interests you don't realize it? A Lunar politician with those charms would be someone who could work both sides of an argument and both sides might take them in confidence.<br /> <br /> (And I'm literally proposing charm concepts right now, hopefully that fits the criteria of a &quot;wish list&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:18:46-08:00","id":346854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346498#post346498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see a barbarian witch cutting his palm and insisting that someone else cut her palm, and they shake on a promise -- a blood-oath -- right?<br /> <br /> Well, if it's magically binding and capable of inflicting harm upon an oath-breaker (maybe it curses them with lycanthropy, or a fixed animal transformation?), could it not also exact a price by taking Heart's Blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Yes, yes I can. Admittedly my problem might be more with aesthetics than mechanics or dynamics, because the aesthetics of &quot;blood-enforced witch-bond&quot; resonates much more with me than &quot;signing a contract and shaking on it&quot;.<br /> I'll try to keep aesthetic interpretations in mind.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm not great at lateral thinking)</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346498#post346498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you feel about the one involving a contest of strength/skill or a game of chance? The Lunar and his opponent agree to a competition with set rules (even if &quot;there are no rules, just make the other guy cry Uncle&quot;, and the Lunar gains Heart's Blood if he wins.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> The contest method isn't as simple as that, because you can't always convince someone to fight you on specific terms, especially not on the terms you need for victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd see it as a sort of &quot;If you can beat me, I'll leave your people alone. But if I win, I get your Face.&quot;, which could be interesting indeed.<br /> <br /> Though truthfully, I'm not sure what the difference between that and the default Sacred Hunt is - I mean, you're still pretty much performing the same actions: watching your prey, getting to know how they act and react, etc. The only difference is that it's in a guise of &quot;sports&quot; (which doesn't necessarily disqualify it as a default sacred hunt - e.g. if it's a wrestling match or a rapier-duel to the death, circumstances haven't really changed) and the person doesn't necessarily die - the latter is worth a charm purchase I suppose, however, in Creation, death doesn't have the big personal/cultural impact that it does for us, so I don't really see a problem with the loser being killed, reverse-Maya style (where instead of the winners joining their gods, the loser is sacrificed to the Lunar, and the Lunar immediately gets the shape as the hours of competition fulfill the Sacred Hunt).<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is: if the loser dies, I don't think there's a difference. If the loser lives, I suppose it works. I'd probably put a requirement of at least some blood being shed (though not necessarily because of combat; bruises from falling, gashes from running through trees/bushes, etc.) as part of the competition, as a sort of metaphysical proof that no one's holding back.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, I mentioned earlier that I was cold on the idea of Compassionate Mirror Nature, since &quot;beat them unconscious&quot; was just the default violent method with less violence. The contest method can easily involve violence, but the difference is that the violence has to be consensual. You can't just ambush someone and KO them, because that's completely superior to the default method, which renders the default completely obsolete. </div> </div> </div>I fully agree. I think of the Sacred Hunt along the same lines as I think of Demons' Souls: Hard But Fair (for varying degrees of &quot;fair&quot; when a Lunar stalks a Human vs. when they stalk a Tyrant Lizard). Not that it's hard to hunt the human, but that it's not trivial for the character to fulfill the requirements of the hunt. There's more to it than just shanking a dude. (The ST might choose to handwave it, but it doesn't mean the character didn't expend energy and time).<br /> <br /> I suppose it's true that I'm stuck in the destructive nature of it. In part it might be my dislike of &quot;Shoot HIM, HE's the fake one!&quot; scenes.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about Lunar crafting a bit, and I think it'd be cool if, as a GSS analogue, they could take pieces of beasts and imbue them with essence, in a way that works both with beast-artifacts (e.g. Monster Hunter again) and improvised remains. Dismember a shark's fin and use it as a knife, rip out a Claw Strider's lower jaw and use it like tiger claws. Later, craft the jaw into an Artifact 1 machete pseudo-daiklave and the charm still works, granting enhanced stats and maybe some Gift-like effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-21-2014, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:29:49-08:00","id":346858,"title":"","content":"What about taking the form of things which no longer exist? So just as taking the form of an animal you have killed is viable you might take the form of a Solar crafted species that is non-extant but which you research heavily in lore? That might fit some of Luna's themes of impossibility and also restorative balance, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:44:00-08:00","id":346862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346858#post346858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about taking the form of things which no longer exist? So just as taking the form of an animal you have killed is viable you might take the form of a Solar crafted species that is non-extant but which you research heavily in lore? That might fit some of Luna's themes of impossibility and also restorative balance, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some love for the no-moon researcher-shapeshifter would be cool.<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;each [time unit] spent researching an extinct species counts as an hour of Sacred Hunt, and then you have to find a piece of said species (fossils, bones, etc.) and [do something to] it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though it could meld well with a sorcerous project too: reanimate a dead species by reconstructing its skeleton and giving it flesh, then hunt it down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, something else that could be cool: reconfigurable weapons/armors or reconfiguration charms/evocations.<br /> Say you have a Moonsilver grand daiklave made of Dragon Wings. Through shapeshifting it might reconfigure itself to give you wings, or a cloak. Similarly to how moon-faced items can adapt to your shape, except that now you're in control of how it manifests, and don't need to change shape for it to change. Although such items probably wouldn't have any additional powers, as this is in and of itself a power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:57:31-08:00","id":346868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=346862#post346862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some love for the no-moon researcher-shapeshifter would be cool.<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;each [time unit] spent researching an extinct species counts as an hour of Sacred Hunt, and then you have to find a piece of said species (fossils, bones, etc.) and [do something to] it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though it could meld well with a sorcerous project too: reanimate a dead species by reconstructing its skeleton and giving it flesh, then hunt it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another possibility for accessing an extinct species might be tracking down the ghost of such a creature. If research is an accessible route, then studying that ghost would likely give an extra bit of insight into how it worked when it was alive. For less studious Lunars, some means of hunting a ghost to acquire both its ghostly shape and its formerly living shape would also seem appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:40:52-08:00","id":347007,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more interactions between the Lunars and the Underworld in general to be honest. They are sort of &quot;light but also darkness&quot; to me and I like that they are equally good at sorcery and necromancy but I think sacred ghost hunts is a cool idea. Or for an occultist feel maybe helping spirits pass into lethe or capturing their fetter?<br /> <br /> For a crafter concept I'd be happy to see them have the most access to &quot;kit-bashing&quot; artifacts, or improvising artifacts to serve different purposes for the scene like the above suggestions so that a Lunar craftsman isn't defined so much by what they can build but by how well the <i>use</i> artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T17:24:16-08:00","id":347074,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's a dissonance of principles - Lunar &quot;physicality&quot; vs. Ghostly ephemera.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine, to hunt a ghost, you'd have to &quot;consume&quot; (literally or metaphorically, as the case may be) their anchors. There's a theme of &quot;dehumanization&quot; running through the treatment of ghosts, and I don't know if it serves the game's themes for the Lunars to treat them as beings (rather than, say, the memories of beings. Treating ghosts as just echoes or reflections of the physical shape they're truly after. <i>Ceci n'est pas une pipe</i> comes to mind. The image of a thing is not the actual thing.)<br /> <br /> That's not to say that they shouldn't be able to take the shapes of the dead, just that maybe it should have a unique approach to it (similar or identical to the one for extinct species).<br /> <br /> Maybe. I don't actually know if any of this is a good idea though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T03:06:35-08:00","id":347303,"title":"","content":"I think overall when it comes to crafting, the key thing is not to specify a particular product, but that other Exalts should have a characteristic method (even if it's not really a superior one). I'm less interested in Lunars having this one kind of thing they're better at making than Solars than in them having a way of making things that is distinct to them. I'd also see these distinctions would be less apparent in a visualisation than in having a way to articulate the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T08:29:17-08:00","id":347436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347074#post347074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there's a dissonance of principles - Lunar &quot;physicality&quot; vs. Ghostly ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this a greater problem than Lunar physicality versus godly or demonic immateriality?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd imagine, to hunt a ghost, you'd have to &quot;consume&quot; (literally or metaphorically, as the case may be) their anchors. </div> </div> </div>That seems to be analogous to needing to eat a demon's Second or Third Circle progenitor, or a god's domain/purview.<br /> <br /> Ghosts have hearts like everyone else, even if it's more symbolic than biologically necessary. In the Underworld, a Lunar is perfectly capable of ripping one out, or of gulping down the &quot;vital&quot; fluids that pump from the spirit's corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, if I eat a ghost, it would be nifty to gain some kind of benefit or connection to its fetters, if only to learn what they are and where.<br /> <br /> If I eat a Second or Third Circle Demon, I'd like to gain some kind of benefit towards any First Circles they've created, or their Second Circle Souls.<br /> <br /> If I eat someone, I'd like to take what they own, Not just gaining their metaphysical &quot;ownership&quot; of objects and places, but also inheriting their attunement to artifacts, hearthstones, demenses and manses, Grave Goods, raksha Graces, and even their Destiny within the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T08:51:12-08:00","id":347463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347436#post347436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this a greater problem than Lunar physicality versus godly or demonic immateriality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them as being thematically different, even though they're technically all immaterial at the start (similarly, it's why you'd need Green Sun Child for demons and not just a generic &quot;now you can eat all immaterial beings&quot; power that gives you access to gods, demons and ghosts in one fell swoop).<br /> <br /> Gods and demons still have a mythological physicality to them - Zeus is not known for how people walk through him, Beelzebub doesn't have trouble touching or being touched by people.<br /> Ghosts however are &quot;all about that shit&quot; so to speak. I find it'd be interesting if, because of that, the hunt needed to take a slightly roundabout route.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347436#post347436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be analogous to needing to eat a demon's Second or Third Circle progenitor, or a god's domain/purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... seems like a deliberately huge exaggeration. Why? Anchors can rarely defend themselves on the same level that Progenitors can, and aren't as expansive / intangible / etc. as Domains.<br /> Though consuming <i>all</i> their anchors might be a bit of a stretch. Just one should be enough.<br /> Additionally, if an anchor <i>can</i> somehow defend itself to such an extent, you can go seek out a different one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347436#post347436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts have hearts like everyone else, even if it's more symbolic than biologically necessary. In the Underworld, a Lunar is perfectly capable of ripping one out, or of gulping down the &quot;vital&quot; fluids that pump from the spirit's corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, if there's ever such a thing, it would probably actually be done like that. I'd just find it kind of boring. It could be an opportunity to add a tad of variety, enough to make each type of &quot;specialization&quot; feel more distinct from one another, and help differentiate the methods of PCs that focus on different kinds of shapes.<br /> <br /> For me, it's the difference between &quot;oh, I can become a ghost. cool I guess.&quot; and &quot;oh shit, hunting ghosts is <i>cool</i>!&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I digress. Personal preference and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T08:58:22-08:00","id":347465,"title":"","content":"Having to hunt a ghost's anchor(s) would make it annoying. Literally anything else in the world, a Lunar can look at, say &quot;I want that&quot; and kill it on the spot to take its face. But ghosts get additional protection in that the Lunar has to leave the Underworld and go hunting for its anchors instead? After figuring out what those anchors ARE in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T09:05:03-08:00","id":347470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347465#post347465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having to hunt a ghost's anchor(s) would make it annoying. Literally anything else in the world, a Lunar can look at, say &quot;I want that&quot; and kill it on the spot to take its face. But ghosts get additional protection in that the Lunar has to leave the Underworld and go hunting for its anchors instead? After figuring out what those anchors ARE in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which can all be part of the sacred hunt which is supposed to take hours. Not really on-the-spot.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you really feel like arguing about what I've stated multiple times as being my personal preference, we should probably do it over PM. This isn't really related to the wish-list any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-22-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T14:07:27-08:00","id":347662,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be cool that if you hunted a ghost, you also gained their when-alive form as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347470#post347470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which can all be part of the sacred hunt which is supposed to take hours. Not really on-the-spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hours thing really sucks, but being completely and totally on the spot seems off (and overpowered) too. Wonder if we can figure out some common ground there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T14:13:20-08:00","id":347664,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd prefer them to toss the Hunt and just make it &quot;anything, anytime&quot;, maybe with purchases to gate certain classes of forms as with 2e. It <i>is</i> a bit too strong, but whatever, it's flash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:08:50-08:00","id":347749,"title":"","content":"The Sacred Hunt is indeed a time spent &quot;hunting&quot; that which you seek to take the shape of, by understanding them. With loose interpretations of &quot;hunt&quot; it could be observing and pursuing another participant at a party, hours spent exploring a lover's body, diligently attending a scholars lectures, or a observing the petty machinations of nobles at court. In some cases the hunted acts as a lure to their target to better understand them, appearing as a person of their target's sexual tastes, or a clever and observant student who attends the scholar's classes diligently. The hunt isn't necessarily a creepy stalking thing, but it is a pursuit of understanding the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-22-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:24:23-08:00","id":347775,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://fc06.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2012/361/b/a/ba7deb3d30e08c0aa6ccc5822006b5a3-d572z8g.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> &quot;be the leaf&quot;<br /> ----<br /> I like the hunt. I don't really have much to add other than that.<br /> <br /> Edit 2 years later: no, I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-21-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:33:53-08:00","id":347786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347775#post347775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">http://fc06.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2012/361/b/a/ba7deb3d30e08c0aa6ccc5822006b5a3-d572z8g.jpg<br /> &quot;be the leaf&quot;<br /> ----<br /> I like the hunt. I don't really have much to add other than that.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUQjY-iHiUE\" data-code=\"QUQjY-iHiUE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QUQjY-iHiUE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T18:44:37-08:00","id":347931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347007#post347007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026I like that they are equally good at sorcery and necromancy\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not, though. It's a somewhat-common houserule people use with Lunars (especially with the terrible argent witches), but Lunars by default can only initiate into the first circle of necromancy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a crafter concept I'd be happy to see them have the most access to &quot;kit-bashing&quot; artifacts, or improvising artifacts to serve different purposes for the scene like the above suggestions so that a Lunar craftsman isn't defined so much by what they can build but by how well the <i>use</i> artifacts. </div> </div> </div>Ugh, can't we have an edition where characters might find crafting things that aren't artifacts worthwhile? I <i>am</i> glad you didn't say &quot;MacGyver,&quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T18:59:25-08:00","id":347935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347931#post347931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, can't we have an edition where characters might find crafting things that aren't artifacts worthwhile?</div> </div> </div> </div>^_________________________________________________ ______^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T19:05:31-08:00","id":347937,"title":"","content":"Hey, Vance, just so ya know, my mobile device here won't display your emoji as one line, so I'm getting two halves of your little broad grin on two lines, and it looks silly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also I'm assuming that you intend that to mean that mundane crafting will indeed pay off in Ex3; the seafaring group's shipwright should appreciate that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T19:12:10-08:00","id":347940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347937#post347937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Vance, just so ya know, my mobile device here won't display your emoji as one line, so I'm getting two halves of your little broad grin on two lines, and it looks silly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Through my long contemplation of the BIFURCATED VISAGE PRANA, there are no boundaries that cannot be shattered by my emoticons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T22:30:38-08:00","id":347998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere on What We Know that Lunars were getting Second Tier on both this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misremembering; there's no such mention of it on the Wiki, and precious little mention of Necromancy at all. I suspect you're thinking of a remark made years ago by a (possibly current?) writer/developer that there wasn't really a good reason for Lunars not to have Labyrinth Circle Necromancy. That comment was directed toward second edition's Lunars, long before EX3 was even on the table.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/11/03/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-post-3/\" target=\"_blank\">more recent comments</a>, Lunars may well not have any particular aptitude with Necromancy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RPG.Net thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: </b><i><b>Mostlyjoe</b></i><br /> 8. Do you see Lunars gaining powers over the world in a style of Druids? Commanding beasts, the land itself? We have heard of Shamanistic magic being at their command, but I\u2019m trying to understand what is the them of their magic in EX3 beyond shapeshifting. Gaia is their link to animal forms. Do they call upon her aid (or that of her children) to do their bidding? If they are Loki\u2026how? Is Lunars being on the forefront of Sorcery and Necromancy with Solars still a thing?<br /> <br /> <b>A: <i>hatewheel</i></b><br /> 8. Re: Druidism: Not really, no. Lunar magic is focused through their bodies. It is heavily based on shapeshifting and physicality. Not command of the world or command of reality, but command of self. Re: sorcery and necromancy: no, we have moved away from that vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T23:06:30-08:00","id":348028,"title":"","content":"Gotta keep in mind, anyway, that what necromancy <i>is</i> in Exalted is gonna be different in the new edition; from what I understand, it's gonna be one stripe of the veritable rainbow that is sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T00:17:58-08:00","id":348086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347749#post347749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sacred Hunt is indeed a time spent &quot;hunting&quot; that which you seek to take the shape of, by understanding them. With loose interpretations of &quot;hunt&quot; it could be observing and pursuing another participant at a party, hours spent exploring a lover's body, diligently attending a scholars lectures, or a observing the petty machinations of nobles at court. In some cases the hunted acts as a lure to their target to better understand them, appearing as a person of their target's sexual tastes, or a clever and observant student who attends the scholar's classes diligently. The hunt isn't necessarily a creepy stalking thing, but it is a pursuit of understanding the target.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>THIS.</i> This is what I want on the top of my shapeshifting wishlist, more methods for form acquisition that keep the theme of &quot;focused pursuit&quot; while opening the floor to academic and social Lunars to excel. I'd also like to add to this list of examples the appreciation of an artist's work to mimic the artist either in form or talent (who else would like to see Lunars get mimicry powers?) and the adoption of cultural taboos and norms in order to imitate a native of that culture, similar to Mastery of Small Manners but also allowing you to look like the &quot;standard&quot; race within that culture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>I'm pretty sure you're referring to information that's only been presented in playtest documents, please refrain from doing so. </b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-23-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T00:26:06-08:00","id":348088,"title":"","content":"New addition to my Lunar wishlist: That I not see any more extrapolations from people resulting in Lunars breeding 25,000 beastmen in a year, trivially, by themselves. Ma-Ha-Suchi's breeding camps may be revolting, but getting an entire generation's worth of half-caste beastmen should be more difficult than &quot;turn into ant queen, use Lunar gestation Charms, have a shit-ton of babysitters ready.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T04:32:32-08:00","id":348182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348086#post348086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the adoption of cultural taboos and norms in order to imitate a native of that culture, similar to Mastery of Small Manners but also allowing you to look like the &quot;standard&quot; race within that culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure they have a charm like that, but in one of the later books. Errata or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:06:13-08:00","id":348214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347937#post347937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Vance, just so ya know, my mobile device here won't display your emoji as one line, so I'm getting two halves of your little broad grin on two lines, and it looks silly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also I'm assuming that you intend that to mean that mundane crafting will indeed pay off in Ex3; the seafaring group's shipwright should appreciate that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as silly as the little tooth his smile is missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:29:52-08:00","id":348224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348028#post348028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta keep in mind, anyway, that what necromancy <i>is</i> in Exalted is gonna be different in the new edition; from what I understand, it's gonna be one stripe of the veritable rainbow that is sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may not see the return of Lunar zombie-making Charms, either.<br /> <br /> It depends on how much the new and focused Lunar direction overlaps with the last-minute &quot;straddle the borders of all worlds&quot; theme the Ink Monkeys introduced to Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:56:15-08:00","id":348246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348088#post348088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New addition to my Lunar wishlist: That I not see any more extrapolations from people resulting in Lunars breeding 25,000 beastmen in a year, trivially, by themselves. Ma-Ha-Suchi's breeding camps may be revolting, but getting an entire generation's worth of half-caste beastmen should be more difficult than &quot;turn into ant queen, use Lunar gestation Charms, have a shit-ton of babysitters ready.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>hahaha has someone really fucking done that with the ant queen thing?<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller I don't think I'd even be upset, just impressed (the fact that I get a swarm of magical ant-folk to give the PC's problems helps).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:03:41-08:00","id":348249,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd go with turtlefolk, because turtlefolk.<br /> <br /> Any argument about how such and such an animal can easily produce x ridiculous number in a generation is easily countered by pointing out that you are producing human hybrid people.<br /> <br /> Humans have a lower birth rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:08:37-08:00","id":348275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347664#post347664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd prefer them to toss the Hunt and just make it &quot;anything, anytime&quot;, maybe with purchases to gate certain classes of forms as with 2e. It <i>is</i> a bit too strong, but whatever, it's flash.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sacred Hunt was a thing even in First Edition, before Second Edition imposed the time-limit. You could pass someone on the street, turn around on a whim, plunge your dagger into their back, take one lick of the blood and wipe the rest off on their sleeve as they fall dead to the street, then turn back around and walk on like nothing happened, and THAT would have been a Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> In fact, let me just quote the first manual (Page 118):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order for the heart's blood to count as tasted, the beast must die, the Lunar must kill it, and the Lunar must drink its blood as it dies. Several Lunars can take part in the hunt, but only one can strike the killing blow and drink the blood.<br /> <br /> The blood must be drunk on the spot, from the throat or the heart of the dying beast, and cannot be decanted, stored, transported, preserved, or otherwise meddled with. Immediately eating the creature's heart also counts, and some large-jawed Lunars simply crunch down the entire small beasts in one mouthful. </div> </div> </div>Ugh. Be grateful for that, because I had to go back through <i>Exalted: The Lunars</i> and looked in the wrong places first. &quot;Heart's Blood&quot; and &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot; weren't in the index at all, and &quot;ritual hunt&quot; just lead to that First Edition, head-bangingly terrible &quot;Lunars as unadulterated Garou&quot; writing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=347749#post347749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sacred Hunt is indeed a time spent &quot;hunting&quot; that which you seek to take the shape of, by understanding them. With loose interpretations of &quot;hunt&quot; it could be observing and pursuing another participant at a party, hours spent exploring a lover's body, diligently attending a scholars lectures, or a observing the petty machinations of nobles at court. In some cases the hunted acts as a lure to their target to better understand them, appearing as a person of their target's sexual tastes, or a clever and observant student who attends the scholar's classes diligently. The hunt isn't necessarily a creepy stalking thing, but it is a pursuit of understanding the target.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348086#post348086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>THIS.</i> This is what I want on the top of my shapeshifting wishlist, more methods for form acquisition that keep the theme of &quot;focused pursuit&quot; while opening the floor to academic and social Lunars to excel.</div> </div> </div> </div>There can and will and should be academic Lunar Exalt characters, but why should that mean they get ANY direct support towards being academic?<br /> <br /> You're still a No Moon if you spy on a target's habits, learn when he's going to be eating alone, poison his food beforehand, and then kill him when he's helpless.<br /> <br /> The killing involved in the basic Sacred Hunt doesn't make it a Full Moon activity. A Full Moon charging at his prey openly with fangs bared, chasing the prey down, and then beating it to death with his bare hands is what makes his hunt a Full Moon activity. A Changing Moon and No Moon should and do still need to kill their target; they just use different, less forceful methods. Typically, with tricks and traps.<br /> <br /> Heck, in First Edition, a Changing Moon could<i> seduce a team of mortal hunters to capture a beast</i> for her and it doesn't matter; so long as she is the one who puts the final arrow in the heart of the totally restrained, blinded, dismembered, poisoned, nearly-bleed-out beast, it counts! THAT is a Changing Moon using her strengths as a Changing Moon, which was convincing others to use <i>their </i>strengths <i>for </i>her.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now remember,<i> I also</i> want the Sacred Hunt to take on many other forms. Many of those forms lend themselves very well to Mental and Social trickery.<br /> <br /> But I do not want people to start thinking that the basic Hunt is &quot;just a Full Moon thing&quot;. It's a LUNAR thing, and you can't get away from the basic nature of hunting without also getting away from the basic nature of Lunars. You can't say that the first kind of hunt can only be a physical thing without saying that ALL hunts must be purely physical.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's a very physical element to the basic Hunt. But remember that all Lunars are very physical; they all shapeshift into animals! The weakest academic could turn into a hawk or bear or elephant!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the problem with merely observing someone as a method to stealing their Heart's Blood is that there's no confrontation. If you deny the target a chance to defend against your attempt to steal, then it's not HEROIC enough to be a proper Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-23-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:18:52-08:00","id":348285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348275#post348275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sacred Hunt was a thing even in First Edition, before Second Edition imposed the time-limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e it was a ritual form of hunt done in veneration to Luna that wasn't strictly necessary to acquire a shape. But then, in 1e, you also had to be able to turn into nearly every variety of natural beast and be to alter every incidental feature of the body in order to be able into order to turn into a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:53:41-08:00","id":348326,"title":"","content":"Now I've got an image of an ant-person version of the Hakkenden, who I don't <i>think</i> were actual octuplets, but there you go. Point is that one can invoke the image of there being a lot of them within reasonable limits. I might also be coming around to the image of an Exalt who between long life and getting around <i>can</i> form an army (albeit a small one, probably in the low hundreds at most) of their first-generation descendents, just not the kind where they're a battle group; you want to go with that, you've got to take them on their merits as individuals, and probably deal with a whole lot of family drama. Nobody is trying to weaponize their own reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:58:23-08:00","id":348329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348285#post348285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e it was a ritual form of hunt done in veneration to Luna that wasn't strictly necessary to acquire a shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was the &quot;ritual hunt&quot; that had me banging my head. That was completely separate from, though not incompatible with, the act of taking Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then, in 1e, you also had to be able to turn into nearly every variety of natural beast and be to alter every incidental feature of the body in order to be able into order to turn into a human. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Shh, only reasonable Charm progessions now.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:03:52-08:00","id":348333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348326#post348326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is trying to weaponize their own reproduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I didn't have to hear that annoyance I wouldn't have posted. Besides, you need only dip into a typical Lunar or Dragon-Blooded thread to see posters attempting to weaponize reproduction. Or read some of the poorer fluff from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-23-2014, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:11:24-08:00","id":348336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348333#post348333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I didn't have to hear that annoyance I wouldn't have posted. Besides, you need only dip into a typical Lunar or Dragon-Blooded thread to see posters attempting to weaponize reproduction. Or read some of the poorer fluff from 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paraphrased: &quot;Your gaming group is not <i>my </i>gaming group.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:32:58-08:00","id":348356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348246#post348246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hahaha has someone really fucking done that with the ant queen thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it was a Thoth scheme. So probably a white room mechanical exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:51:18-08:00","id":348362,"title":"","content":"Lunar wants: not expecting this so planning on making it a house rule: Lunars having access to Labyrinth Circle Necromancy, because the moon is a thing of both Light and Dark in equal proportions, between the shining sun and the deep endless void, and because the Lunars are as much hunters of the dead as they are the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T09:12:01-08:00","id":348368,"title":"","content":"I dont know if this something the game should handle. But I have had a problem that has repeated itself with 75 procent of the lunar i have had to store for. And that is using incest to maxsimise the mutations of their beastmen offspring. How do you as At del with that? Its been a While since i have brought this up. But as far as i remember that these planets had a way to avoid handicaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T11:17:46-08:00","id":348428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348088#post348088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New addition to my Lunar wishlist: That I not see any more extrapolations from people resulting in Lunars breeding 25,000 beastmen in a year, trivially, by themselves. Ma-Ha-Suchi's breeding camps may be revolting, but getting an entire generation's worth of half-caste beastmen should be more difficult than &quot;turn into ant queen, use Lunar gestation Charms, have a shit-ton of babysitters ready.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I need this for my Lunar PC who is infiltrating the realm with anchor babies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T11:57:50-08:00","id":348458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348356#post348356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure it was a Thoth scheme. So probably a white room mechanical exploit</div> </div> </div> </div>Still gets annoying hearing it again and again. And again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T12:06:13-08:00","id":348462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like the new eddition to have more than three upgrade powers for Deadly Beastman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you for reminding me of an idea I'd had some time ago. I'd be interested in support (examples, advice, etc.) for a personalized cascade of Charms extending off of DBT, through which a Lunar might define a distinct and personal fighting style using the synthesis of human and totemic forms, roughly analogous (in concept more than power) to Evocations or a Martial Arts style. Though, on further thought, possible executions of that keyword idea John mentioned ages ago may well give rise to something like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:06:42-08:00","id":348526,"title":"","content":"Oh, something in my wishlist that just came to mind. I wants some bloody legit illusions. In so many places around the globe the moon is associated with falsehood, hallucinations, and seeing things that aren't there, so I think that if anyone is going to have an illusionist suite in Exalted at last it should probably be Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:17:16-08:00","id":348549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348526#post348526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, something in my wishlist that just came to mind. I wants some bloody legit illusions. In so many places around the globe the moon is associated with falsehood, hallucinations, and seeing things that aren't there, so I think that if anyone is going to have an illusionist suite in Exalted at last it should probably be Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>About that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: What about other themes? Like Illusions, magic, what if I want to play a non-combat Lunar? Social, mysterious, etc? How thick is the support for that? <b>(Mostlyjoe)</b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A: Definite support for social, mysterious Lunars. Not so much illusions. A Lunar has the most majestic god-body ever. They are all about being seen. </span></span><b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:22:26-08:00","id":348552,"title":"","content":"Well, time to homebrew a suite of illusion charms whatever the book says yet again, I guess. I like illusions and Lunars are the best fit in Exalted for having illusionary powers far as I can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:32:08-08:00","id":348555,"title":"","content":"I feel as though illusions in general wind up fitting better with Sorcery. I mean, depending on how they're being defined in this particular cosmology; it's kind of a vague term. I'd also say moon themes of &quot;things aren't what they appear&quot; might be encompassed in the projected idea of Lunars being able to shape perceptions of themselves (occasionally in synergy with the ability to actually change what they are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T15:10:05-08:00","id":348587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348526#post348526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, something in my wishlist that just came to mind. I wants some bloody legit illusions. In so many places around the globe the moon is associated with falsehood, hallucinations, and seeing things that aren't there, so I think that if anyone is going to have an illusionist suite in Exalted at last it should probably be Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of manipulative effects in the Lunar Charmset which historically have been described as Illusions for purposes of Keyword defense; that said, I wouldn't call them illusions in the same vein as, say, Shadow Conjuration/Evocation from D&amp;D. I feel like it's that Shadow Conjuration type stuff that John is referring to.<br /> <br /> And Lunars just creating shadowy figments moving about isn't really within their purview, because that's not really a human-focused power and Attribute Exalts are pretty much shaping human-isn power through the lens of an Attribute. Lunars convincing someone that they are someone/something they're not, or leading pursuers astray by making the forest close around them, or any of the Butterfly Eyes screw-with-perceptions-to-confuse (which admittedly were pretty meta) or Glories Charms...I don't see why those aren't appropriate illusion-type effects. But they're not wiggling your fingers and making a phantasm float by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-23-2014, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T15:56:45-08:00","id":348605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348555#post348555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though illusions in general wind up fitting better with Sorcery. I mean, depending on how they're being defined in this particular cosmology; it's kind of a vague term. I'd also say moon themes of &quot;things aren't what they appear&quot; might be encompassed in the projected idea of Lunars being able to shape perceptions of themselves (occasionally in synergy with the ability to actually change what they are).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. As I see it, Illusion is about not being obvious (being deceitful or redirecting attention being a primary objective of illusion spells) while, at least in 2E Sorcery, is all <i>about </i>being as obvious and grand as a motherfucker can be (hell, if memory serves correctly, even the smallest sorcery sends your anima immediately to the &quot;bonfire that everyone in like two miles radius can see&quot; level, didn't it?), which would make illusion &quot;handy&quot; sorceries rather a problematic thing to use. Who knows what 3E Sorcery would look like, but at least in 2E I'd probably not make any illusion under the range of &quot;veil a valley from the eyes of men&quot; a Sorcery Spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 12-23-2014, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T16:27:24-08:00","id":348617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348362#post348362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar wants: not expecting this so planning on making it a house rule: Lunars having access to Labyrinth Circle Necromancy, because the moon is a thing of both Light and Dark in equal proportions, between the shining sun and the deep endless void, and because the Lunars are as much hunters of the dead as they are the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure there's no such thing as Labyrinth Circle Necromancy in 3e. Necromancy is being folded into Sorcery as one of the various ways your power can manifest, it's not going to be a separate thing any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T17:22:22-08:00","id":348651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348617#post348617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure there's no such thing as Labyrinth Circle Necromancy in 3e. Necromancy is being folded into Sorcery as one of the various ways your power can manifest, it's not going to be a separate thing any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. From the What We Know wiki:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Necromancy still has its own circles. When we get to the necromancy mechanics, you will see where I had the writers work to blur the distinctions a bit. In previous editions, there were some spells shared between Sorcery and Necromancy. That is still true. The difference is that the two disciplines use entirely different Shaping techniques in order to cast spells, resulting in characters that act and feel different, and deploy the same spells differently.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you've seen something to the contrary, say from the RPG.net thread or Reddit AMA something, by all means present your source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:08:25-08:00","id":348692,"title":"","content":"Well bear in mind that Luna (and thus her exalts) has historically been defined as the Incarna most likely to get her hands dirty hunting fae and beating them at their own game. That's probably where a lot of this illusion association comes from, in addition to just how we culturally perceive the moon. That said, maybe it's best to keep Luna's powers distinct from fairy nonsense. Maybe it's more on theme for her to perform the impossible but when the fairy pushes at this miracle hoping to see a man behind the curtain they find that Oz was all too real after all. In shorter prose, maybe Luna should be able to do anything a fairy can do without losing her sense of self or ceasing to be real. Hence <i>actual</i> shapeshifting instead of glamor, charms that really do make you stronger and smarter instead of just pretending to be, and mental defense set that allows mutable characters while preserving the aspects you care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T19:47:05-08:00","id":348723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348651#post348651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. From the What We Know wiki:<br /> <br /> [/B]<br /> <br /> If you've seen something to the contrary, say from the RPG.net thread or Reddit AMA something, by all means present your source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant site a source but I too could have sworn that I read that Necromancy was going to get folded into Sorcery as a separate island of powers with different initiations, but that still functioned in the same system as Sorcery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T20:11:03-08:00","id":348737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348723#post348723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cant site a source but I too could have sworn that I read that Necromancy was going to get folded into Sorcery as a separate island of powers with different initiations, but that still functioned in the same system as Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same system meaning?<br /> <br /> I mean, I bet the action of casting spells with be the same, the ways of gathering motes will be different etc but I doubt that having CCS is going to give you access to Bone Lion, was my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T20:28:26-08:00","id":348744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348737#post348737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same system meaning?<br /> <br /> I mean, I bet the action of casting spells with be the same, the ways of gathering motes will be different etc but I doubt that having CCS is going to give you access to Bone Lion, was my point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh ya totally, by same system I just meant they were more mechanically unified now as all part of the &quot;Sorcery System&quot; even if you can break it down into two separate parts &quot;Sorcery&quot; and &quot;Necromancy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T21:11:45-08:00","id":348779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348744#post348744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh ya totally, by same system I just meant they were more mechanically unified now as all part of the &quot;Sorcery System&quot; even if you can break it down into two separate parts &quot;Sorcery&quot; and &quot;Necromancy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll probably have to wait to see the shape of Sorcery in the core book before we can properly speculate about Necromancy. At the very least, I'd expect to still see the terms for the circles of Necromancy sticking around; those always felt distinctive and evocative to me. I'm curious whether the other Initiations alluded to will have their own circle names for spells/workings (e.g. the Wyld Initiation could borrow its names from raksha Oneiromancy, giving &quot;Dreaming,&quot; &quot;Waking,&quot; and &quot;Shinma&quot; circles) and will be roughly as distinct from &quot;vanilla&quot; Sorcery* as is Necromancy, or if Necromancy having its own reflects something distinct about it compared to other subsets of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> * For the record, I don't believe there's really such a thing as &quot;vanilla&quot; Sorcery, but the term tickled me.<br /> <br /> Er, and getting back to the thread topic... I'm sure someone's already mentioned it, and it's probably not a wish list item, exactly, as it's kinda already appeared in print. But whatever other changes Lunars have seen since it did, I'd like this to remain possible:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masters of Jade, p. 43</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empowered by the prayers of the river tribes, Ghost Wolf was able to transform himself into a variety of horrific guardian totems in order to terrorize the Guild.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:51:51-08:00","id":349598,"title":"","content":"Going back to more humble powers...<br /> <br /> I want a Charm for convincing my opponents that I'm stalking and striking at them from the shadows because I'm too weak to face them directly... so that they'll underestimate my actual strength and lower their guard.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I also want to convince my hunters that I'm hitting and running because I'm so much stronger than them that I feel like having fun... even though it's really because I'd be totally screwed in a direct confrontation, and I need to discourage them from taking the initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T00:29:53-08:00","id":349679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=348651#post348651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've seen something to the contrary, say from the RPG.net thread or Reddit AMA something, by all means present your source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no such source. I must have been misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T11:48:30-08:00","id":349980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=349679#post349679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no such source. I must have been misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think it might be a persistent idea from an older version of sorcery? Not sure - it's been a thing that has popped up a few times in threads over the last year or so but I've never been able to find a dev who's implied it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:35:06-08:00","id":351244,"title":"","content":"Lunar healing has traditionally been much better than something requiring rest from being pulped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:52:12-08:00","id":351281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean pulped, I mean &quot;Why the fuck are you not dead?! You wera pile or gore and broken limbs for the gods' sake&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, normally I'd be dead right now, but I've achieved full mastery of my stamina and thus as long as I have my heroic will and have respired enough essence to burn, I can't die, even if it takes me a month to get back to one hundred percent</div> </div> </div> </div>That might not be the best way for Lunars to ablate over-damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T21:36:10-08:00","id":351317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation seemed like it was on to something. Failing that, fixing Luna's Fortitude so that you can go over and not die if you use the extra time to heal the damage that's over your limit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, I'm just looking for a power that's a nice logical extension of &quot;Even more imune/resistant to disease and poison than most exalts&quot; <i>and </i>&quot;I can survive wounds that would have killed ten lesser men&quot; <i>and</i> &quot;heals really fucking fast&quot; <i>and &quot;</i>flat out ingnores things like environmental heat, cold, or bug bites&quot; and figured &quot;burn essence to avoid sucombing to your wounds long enough to heal enough that your normal super healing will fix ya&quot; made sense. </div> </div> </div>When you say &quot;burn Essence&quot;, it sounds like one of the functions of Immortal Malevolence Enslavement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T06:14:17-08:00","id":355701,"title":"","content":"If Lunars can shape how others perceive them, and shape their own bodies, then...<br /> <br /> I'd like Lunars to be able to completely soak an attack but make it seem like they were badly wounded. They might actually have to take a wound penalty to their next couple of actions to &quot;sell&quot; the damage to their opponent, but they can drop the act to launch a surprise offensive.<br /> <br /> In reverse, I'd like Lunars to be able to become badly wounded but make it seem like they soaked the damage completely. They still actually suffer wound penalties, and the greater the penalty, the easier it is for the opponent to see through the deception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T10:54:21-08:00","id":355869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=355701#post355701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reverse, I'd like Lunars to be able to become badly wounded but make it seem like they soaked the damage completely. They still actually suffer wound penalties, and the greater the penalty, the easier it is for the opponent to see through the deception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds very Butterfly Eyes to me. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:04:37-08:00","id":355877,"title":"","content":"If Lunars are going to continue to be the iconically super-tough, hardy, regenerating Exalted, this time it'd be nice if that's actually something they get a little of out-of-box, rather than &quot;this is one of the iconic Lunar things but you need to have Stamina X and a couple specific charms to do it at all&quot;. Hard to say how feasible this will be until we see what damage and healing look like in 3e, but I'd like to see <i>something</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:12:28-08:00","id":355882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=355701#post355701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars can shape how others perceive them, and shape their own bodies, then...<br /> <br /> I'd like Lunars to be able to completely soak an attack but make it seem like they were badly wounded. They might actually have to take a wound penalty to their next couple of actions to &quot;sell&quot; the damage to their opponent, but they can drop the act to launch a surprise offensive.<br /> <br /> In reverse, I'd like Lunars to be able to become badly wounded but make it seem like they soaked the damage completely. They still actually suffer wound penalties, and the greater the penalty, the easier it is for the opponent to see through the deception.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=355869#post355869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds very Butterfly Eyes to me. I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can upgrade it still further.<br /> <br /> The 2.5 errata introduced an Abyssal soak Charm that, as a knock-on effect, would inflict an attacker (and witnesses?) with horror if the Abyssal completely soaked the attack with the Charm. If that can be an incidental effect of a Resistance-based soak Charm, then a Lunar could use a whole Charm to upgrade his &quot;pretend I wasn't hurt&quot; social-Attribute Charm to have similar effects. Terrify your enemies or inspire your allies with your appearance of invincibility.<br /> <br /> On the flipside, use your facade of injury to inspire your enemy to overconfidence.<br /> <br /> Naturally, these Charms have cousins and allies in my earlier suggestions for Charm that you use to fool your enemy about whether you're using a hit-and-run strategy out of fear or whimsy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T12:48:58-08:00","id":355979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=355877#post355877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are going to continue to be the iconically super-tough, hardy, regenerating Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Were they ever supposed to be? I think that idea comes from the echo-chamber, and the fact that Stamina-favoring Full Moon warriors were the most successful of the few successful Lunar builds. (Revlid explained to me how a properly built Lunar is factually impossible to kill.)<br /> <br /> Certainly, it's a thing that Lunars <i>should </i>be able to be, but that doesn't mean it is a thing that all Lunars <i>must </i>be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this time it'd be nice if that's actually something they get a little of out-of-box, rather than &quot;this is one of the iconic Lunar things but you need to have Stamina X and a couple specific charms to do it at all&quot;. Hard to say how feasible this will be until we see what damage and healing look like in 3e, but I'd like to see <i>something</i>. </div> </div> </div>It depends on whether or not DBT comes free, this edition. One comment from Hatewheel suggests that it will, but it's very much not certain.<br /> <br /> Second Edition DBT not only gave you a dot of Stamina, but also more Dying health levels and better ability to recover from crippling wounds, especially with Bruise-Relief Method, which is a tier-one Charm with low prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T13:12:07-08:00","id":356002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=355979#post355979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were they ever supposed to be? I think that idea comes from the echo-chamber, and the fact that Stamina-favoring Full Moon warriors were the most successful of the few successful Lunar builds. (Revlid explained to me how a properly built Lunar is factually impossible to kill.)<br /> <br /> Certainly, it's a thing that Lunars <i>should </i>be able to be, but that doesn't mean it is a thing that all Lunars <i>must </i>be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes and no. In 1e, it was as important to their build as persistent defenses were to Solars, so it was <i>de facto</i> mandatory in that newbie-trap way. In 2e it was just a fanon thing based on how iconic it was, admittedly. However, Holden's comments do make me think that it's being viewed as more of a core Lunar competency in 3e. We'll see, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:31:26-08:00","id":356158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does going into a coma to accelerate their already rapid rate of healing sound like a Lunarry thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hibernating like a bear or dragon, with a bonus to recovery, might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T19:01:52-08:00","id":356170,"title":"","content":"It does seem fitting, but considering they can heal Stamina levels of damage in a round, I don't see how it could be even faster.<br /> Maybe it could be for healing crippling wounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T00:13:02-08:00","id":356348,"title":"","content":"Like the Topic Creator, i would like to see more interaction between a Lunar and their familliars.<br /> <br /> I would like to see Lunars capable of making their spirit shape into a larger, more combat capable form. basically a second war form, but instead of bing a hybrid between the human form and the spirit shape, it would be a monsterous version of the spirit shape. totally okay if this advances a Lunar along the path of chimeraism.<br /> <br /> And i would like to see a Full Moon Lunar be as effective in combat as a Dawn Cast Solar. or at least nearly so. it chaffes my hide that in the 1st edition, Dragon Bloods could generate higher dice pools than Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:47:14-08:00","id":356484,"title":"","content":"Eh, to be honest I felt Full Moons were really good (definitely better at combat than No Moons were at mental stuff). Enormous soak, rapid regeneration, high damage, being able to become immune to your enemy's weapon, etc. In my group, Full Moons was generally where people went when they wanted to be good at combat.<br /> Their dice pools for attacking was probably their only real weakness... except when they turned into a T-Rex with strength 16 and grappled you of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:49:06-08:00","id":356485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=356348#post356348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And i would like to see a Full Moon Lunar be as effective in combat as a Dawn Cast Solar. or at least nearly so. it chaffes my hide that in the 1st edition, Dragon Bloods could generate higher dice pools than Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the dice cap limits have always been screwy, particularly for Lunars and especially Sidereals. That said Dawns were not that effective in combat in 2e until the Dawn Solution (compared to any other Caste favoring a Dawn Ability or two), where Full Moon Lunars at least always had their soak regen DBT/Gift/Fury tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T06:36:59-08:00","id":356595,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Sidereals had awful dice caps. It was a little strange that DBs had one of the best first excellencies (dirt cheap and with a pretty decent dice cap).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:34:36-08:00","id":356635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=356595#post356595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Sidereals had awful dice caps. It was a little strange that DBs had one of the best first excellencies (dirt cheap and with a pretty decent dice cap).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the logic of their Excellencies being cheap, what with them having (1) shitty little mote pools; and (2) being Ability-based thus giving them a dice cap keying off of Ability.<br /> <br /> The thing there was I don't think writers realized (or cared) how easy it was to get Ability 5, Specialty +3 in a few things you wanna be good at as a DB, versus getting Attributes to 5. Sidereals just made no sense at all, even with the Fateful Excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:40:13-08:00","id":356975,"title":"","content":"The DB 2-for-1 excellency thing came from 1e, where each defense required a separate rolled action by default. Celestials got powers that let them defend at full pool against everything, and the whole combat system revolved around those at Exalted level, but DBs were stuck building defense pools one by one from their Excellency (you could &quot;build&quot; a defense action from zero dice using an excellency). 2e removed this dynamic but left in a lot of the things that relied on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:50:29-08:00","id":356982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=356975#post356975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DB 2-for-1 excellency thing came from 1e, where each defense required a separate rolled action by default. Celestials got powers that let them defend at full pool against everything, and the whole combat system revolved around those at Exalted level, but DBs were stuck building defense pools one by one from their Excellency (you could &quot;build&quot; a defense action from zero dice using an excellency). 2e removed this dynamic but left in a lot of the things that relied on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars got powers that let them defend at full pool. Sidereals got them and then some (use Impeding the Flow, deny attack), although not always in places you'd expect. Lunars not so much. There were some that could be used for defense, but they had restrictions like not being able to work if you already acted in a turn, not being able to move or make multiple attacks (even with Charms), or requiring the Lunar concentrate entirely on dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:32:41-08:00","id":357032,"title":"","content":"Guys, guys, guys. <br /> <br /> Wrong thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:48:33-08:00","id":357056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=357032#post357032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, guys, guys.<br /> <br /> Wrong thread!</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think it would be better that the discussion above would cease or move to an appropriate thread, I can't help but find a bit of humor, given that this board has coined &quot;Meerkat Steals the Spotlight Prana&quot;, in a Lunars thread being hijacked by something else ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:19:38-08:00","id":357080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=357056#post357056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I think it would be better that the discussion above would cease or move to an appropriate thread, I can't help but find a bit of humor, given that this board has coined &amp;quot;Meerkat Steals the Spotlight Prana&amp;quot;, in a Lunars thread being hijacked by something else ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't appreciate the irony the <i>last</i> two or three times it happened before this thread, or the two or three times within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:33:35-08:00","id":357087,"title":"","content":"I always wanted a version of Mighty Thews/Crouching Tiger Exercise that wasn't so underwhelming or reliant on dice rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:38:10-08:00","id":357092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=357087#post357087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wanted a version of Mighty Thews/Crouching Tiger Exercise that wasn't so underwhelming or reliant on dice rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck yes, can we finally have Lunars with a proper Hulk Out Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-01-2015, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T18:10:12-08:00","id":357105,"title":"","content":"I have a confession to make.<br /> <br /> I found the layout of the second Lunar manual boring.<br /> <br /> I lied to myself at first. I told myself that losing the rough-stone imagery of the first book was a good thing, as part of getting away from the ideological barbarism of First Edition Lunars. I accepted the generic, clean, straight lines of the new book.<br /> <br /> But I always, always missed the rough and living energy conveyed by the style and artwork and -- yes -- even the flawed Charms of <i>Exalted: The Lunars</i>. It was very much part of what made me fall in love with them; a love that endured the revelation of how terrible their mechanics were, and how pointless their fluff was. The love that made me so very, very angry and driven for so long.<br /> <br /> I want it back. I want the humble, rough-cut rocks. I want unpolished wood, bleached bone, claws, feathers. I want hair and fang and blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T15:39:41-08:00","id":359628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">does swallowing a heartstone in order to intergrate it's magic(both in a &quot;Mote respired&quot; sense and a &quot;Special abillity&quot; sense) sound like a Lunarry thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, though not trivially. Kind of like reproducing a skin-mount amulet, but within your stomach, using shape-shifting and committing motes (with enough experience/upgrade charms you might not need to swallow them any more too).<br /> <br /> Reminds me of those unofficial heart-stone charms the DBs got (can't find them anymore, my google-fu is weak), Lunars could probably do something along similar lines, but more physical / shapeshifty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T16:33:54-08:00","id":359672,"title":"","content":"Working under the assumption that Knacks won't exist in the next edition (because they really only existed to prevent Eclipses from learning them), I'd tend to make such a power similar to Many Pockets Meditation, in a way that you can hide things inside your body (possibly a low-cost upgrade to MPM), and an upgrade of <i>that</i> being that you have your own hearth-stone sockets (1 per purchase), probably based in Intelligence or Stamina, since it's a body thing, but also a knowing-essence-flows thing.<br /> <br /> Although &quot;pockets&quot; would be entirely metaphorical. I'd love to have an Angler-Fish Lunar with a Hearth-Stone at the end of his lure.<br /> <br /> As for empowering a Lunar's attacks, hmm... maybe his tattoos around his natural attacks glow with the colors of the stone, and charms like Claws of the Silver Moon benefit from the effect? I think that'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:18:49-08:00","id":360278,"title":"","content":"I liked Monkey Shaping Emulation and Argent Saga Immortalized (Upload?).<br /> <br /> It would be nice if Lunar Charms could represent skill-independent talent for recreating the spitting image of anything you've seen, for the purpose of creating art, teaching aides, evidence, or counterfeits.<br /> <br /> Extending beyond mere sight, this could mean being able to perfectly play a song you heard once, assuming your skill is actually up to the task. And perhaps with sufficient knowledge of baking, you can intuit how to recreate any pie you smelled or tasted.<br /> <br /> (But Chompy can never make it quite as good as that Solar! *sniff sniff* Poor Chompy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:01:04-08:00","id":360581,"title":"","content":"I definitely echo the wish for a take on Lunar Crafting that includes making artifacts out of the hides, bones, etc. of fallen monsters rather than the magical materials. I just can't see my prospective Lunar walking around in some clanking suit of plate mail, but the nigh-impenetrable hide of a Nemean Lion-esque creature? Oh yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:10:07-08:00","id":360587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=360581#post360581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely echo the wish for a take on Lunar Crafting that includes making artifacts out of the hides, bones, etc. of fallen monsters rather than the magical materials. I just can't see my prospective Lunar walking around in some clanking suit of plate mail, but the nigh-impenetrable hide of a Nemean Lion-esque creature? Oh yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if you were to use the moonsilver tattoo ink that the Lunars use on themselves to create designs on the pelt? Maybe draw some moonsilver into a wiry thread that you use to stitch the hide into a shape you can wear?<br /> <br /> No one ever said that you have to make Artifacts solely or even mainly of the Magical Materials. They just have to be integrated in some way. That's without changing a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:29:08-08:00","id":360811,"title":"","content":"You don't actually need to use any magical materials to make artefacts, just weapons and armour.<br /> But currently, Lunar crafting charms are just about moonsilver. I do like the idea that they could make a lot of stuff with animal (or behemoth, perhaps demon) skins, bones, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:08:56-08:00","id":360986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=360811#post360811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't actually need to use any magical materials to make artefacts, just weapons and armour.<br /> But currently, Lunar crafting charms are just about moonsilver. I do like the idea that they could make a lot of stuff with animal (or behemoth, perhaps demon) skins, bones, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition had Shaping the Once-Living Form, which was based on a CWoD Garou Gift called Reshape Object.<br /> <br /> I think it was actually WORSE than the Gift, but then First Edition Lunar Charms generally sucked like that.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the original Gift and Charm weren't limited to corpses. It also let you work magic with plants, doing anything from making chairs to mixing perfume. I'd like to retain that feature, while adding synergies with Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> As regards magical materials, while Lunars may retain the feature of being most talented with moonsilver, it WOULD be nice to use red jade when forging a sword from the fangs of a fire elemental dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-06-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:56:11-08:00","id":361406,"title":"","content":"It would be cool if certain Elsewhere Den-Charms were repurposed into Charms that progressed from &quot;talent at creating hiding places / shelter&quot; to &quot;creating pseudo-sanctums&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Spider's Trapdoor for making hidey holes (or for hiding traps), Invisible Warren Creation for hidden living spaces, Secure Den Prana for sealing those hidden places against intrusion, Frozen Ripple Lair for changing the very nature of reality within those hidden places (such as making it bigger on the inside, or altering the flow of time).<br /> <br /> None of this &quot;vanishing into thin air&quot; business. You actually have to build a real place within the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T07:46:31-08:00","id":367356,"title":"","content":"I'd like Lunars to favor five Abilities, one of which absolutely does not have to be Survival. The way it was back in First Edition (when you couldn't favor any out-of-Caste Attributes, but let's ignore that).<br /> <br /> With the exception of Martial Arts Style Charms, Lunars couldn't learn any Charms at favored costs because of Abilities. Second Edition did give you one favored Ability to pick (in addition to Survival), but the only mechanically sensible choice was Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Even spells are favored through Intelligence rather than Occult... though given how difficult picking an out-of-Caste Attribute to favor is, perhaps Lunars <i>should </i>be able to enjoy favored Sorcery costs through favoring Occult.<br /> <br /> Though if Martial Arts Style Charms are going to be based on abilities other than Brawl/Martial Arts -- if the purely sword-based Styles are going to be at least partially Melee-based, or even totally Melee-based! -- then the pressure to always choose just one particular Ability to favor is off.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Attributes, I'd like Lunars to be able to trade one Caste Attribute to favor an additional out-of-Caste Attribute. I seldom see a case in which I would personally want to do this, but it's a little bit more flexibility at the cost of basically nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T07:52:52-08:00","id":367360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that an Attribute based Exalt will get ability Charms at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying they will get <i>native </i>Ability-based Charms.<br /> <br /> But Lunars have <i>always </i>been able to learn <i>universal </i>Ability-based Charms, such as those in Martial Arts Styles. Even Alchemicals can do that. Being able to Kung Fu Fighting is a staple of the genre upon which the game of Exalted is built!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:06:59-08:00","id":367367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367356#post367356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> As for Attributes, I'd like Lunars to be able to trade one Caste Attribute to favor an additional out-of-Caste Attribute. I seldom see a case in which I would personally want to do this, but it's a little bit more flexibility at the cost of basically nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>After what happened with Alchemicals, I'd actually expect them to get two Favored Attributes and the three Caste Attributes. Combine with a better designed Charm set and they should feel less pigeonholed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:19:40-08:00","id":367378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367360#post367360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying they will get <i>native </i>Ability-based Charms.<br /> <br /> But Lunars have <i>always </i>been able to learn <i>universal </i>Ability-based Charms, such as those in Martial Arts Styles. Even Alchemicals can do that. Being able to Kung Fu Fighting is a staple of the genre upon which the game of Exalted is built!</div> </div> </div> </div>Their gong fu is going to be rather heavily de-emphasized. The ask the devs thread on rpg.net revealed that the current plan is to not have Martial Arts Charms (possibly also techniques? Not sure) available to Lunars in beast forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:22:24-08:00","id":367380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367378#post367378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their gong fu is going to be rather heavily de-emphasized. The ask the devs thread on rpg.net revealed that the current plan is to not have Martial Arts Charms (possibly also techniques? Not sure) available to Lunars in beast forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really doesn't seem like it's heavily de-emphasised to me. Were there a lot of people busting out tiger style in their <i>actual</i> tiger form? It seems like DBT would be a better choicein almost every situation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:28:29-08:00","id":367387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367380#post367380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That really doesn't seem like it's heavily de-emphasised to me. Were there a lot of people busting out tiger style in their <i>actual</i> tiger form? It seems like DBT would be a better choicein almost every situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your Strength is less than five in human form, 2e DBT would put you under the Strength of a great cat, particularly with Mountainous Spirit Expression active. Or Emperor Ox Expansion, for that matter. Internal Form Mastery would let you keep your Dexterity. You'd need at least Stamina 4 to match a great cat's Stamina rating with basic DBT as well. So for characters that don't emphasize physical Attributes, or don't emphasize Strength and Stamina, a great cat's form might have been better, yes. And tyrant lizards? DBT couldn't match them in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:42:44-08:00","id":367397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367380#post367380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really doesn't seem like it's heavily de-emphasised to me. Were there a lot of people busting out tiger style in their <i>actual</i> tiger form? It seems like DBT would be a better choicein almost every situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe not every situation. A Lunar who wants to combine Evocations with a Martial Arts style probably isn't gonna have DBT as the go-to. Hopefully, there will be other reasons it's not automatically the best solution to all Lunars. ... Or, given context, you were clearly talking about actual experiences with 1e/2e Lunars, so never mind. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> I agree with your main thrust: it doesn't seem like this is intended as a de-emphasis to Lunar Martial Artist capabilities. It feels more like a statement that Martial Arts moves designed for a human-like physiology kind of depend on having a human-like physiology to perform them. Which makes perfect sense to me. I also feel like &quot;de-emphasis&quot; is kind of a funny way to describe this happening, given the splat's never really had much of a Martial Arts emphasis in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:47:28-08:00","id":367426,"title":"","content":"Sunder, I have this feeling that based on what has been written in this thread, you are going to be incredibly disappointed with Lunars in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:00:59-08:00","id":367437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367426#post367426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunder, I have this feeling that based on what has been written in this thread, you are going to be incredibly disappointed with Lunars in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's been disappointed with Lunars for two editions now. Why would we expect that to change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:10:22-08:00","id":367441,"title":"","content":"Those were legitimate disappointments because Lunars were either mechanically unsound, thematically a mess, or both. Here I suspect that the disappointment is going to come from the fact that Lunars are going to be completely different from what is wanted in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:19:42-08:00","id":367444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367367#post367367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After what happened with Alchemicals, I'd actually expect them to get two Favored Attributes and the three Caste Attributes. Combine with a better designed Charm set and they should feel less pigeonholed.</div> </div> </div> </div>After <i>what </i>happened? Alchemicals treated Attributes the same way in Second Edition as they did in First. This impacted Lunars insofar as Lunars got even ONE out-of-Caste Attribute to favor.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind &quot;just one&quot; is that Lunars have a totally different relationship with their Charms than Alchemicals do, what with multiple-Attribute progression trees (especially considering submodules) and the fact that they can't have all Charms loaded at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:23:44-08:00","id":367447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367426#post367426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunder, I have this feeling that based on what has been written in this thread, you are going to be incredibly disappointed with Lunars in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say! Without telling me what you presumably know, you have no way of knowing that I'd love that direction as much or more than the ideas I've been left to imagine based on <i>practically no information</i>.<br /> <br /> Could you perhaps point me at particular figures in movies, comic books or video games who capture what YOU know about Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:27:54-08:00","id":367454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367447#post367447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you perhaps point me at particular figures in movies, comic books or video games who capture what YOU know about Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>No-one really knows about Lunars at theis point. Even in the best possible case the book is at least a year away from serious development.<br /> <br /> I think what he's saying is that your dreams are so grand that no reality could satisfy in comparison. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:32:32-08:00","id":367458,"title":"","content":"Mostly I say that because you seem to want Lunars to have a bunch of weird bullshit* animal/territory/guardian powers, which were what 2E Lunars were all about. This seems to go against what the Devs have said about their design goals when it comes to refocusing the game on the human aspect and personable nature of the Exalted. Weird bullshit* powers tend to make the focus about the powers, rather than the people who use them and the stories that could be told, which is what the Storyteller system is all about.<br /> <br /> *I use weird bullshit as a term of endearment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 01-12-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:34:49-08:00","id":367461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367444#post367444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After <i>what </i>happened? Alchemicals treated Attributes the same way in Second Edition as they did in First. This impacted Lunars insofar as Lunars got even ONE out-of-Caste Attribute to favor.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind &quot;just one&quot; is that Lunars have a totally different relationship with their Charms than Alchemicals do, what with multiple-Attribute progression trees (especially considering submodules) and the fact that they can't have all Charms loaded at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanical execution of Alchemical Charms was the smoothest functioning Charm set of them all, largely because you didn't have to hyper-calculate which Attributes you wanted to favor for maximum efficiency. You could almost pick any random Caste and three random Favored Attributes and still run the exact same Charms. I usually had at least one Favored Attribute to spend on something entirely concept related.<br /> <br /> Lunars may not learn Charms the same way, but just looking at why the Alchemical set worked well and the Lunar set worked poorly would point at the Lunar set having too many constraints, too little flexibility, and too little support for anything other than &quot;pretty kitties&quot; and &quot;RAWR! *SMASH*&quot; builds. Adding one more Favored Attribute would help with at least two of the three problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:15:00-08:00","id":367567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367458#post367458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I say that because you seem to want Lunars to have a bunch of weird bullshit* animal/territory/guardian powers, which were what 2E Lunars were all about. This seems to go against what the Devs have said about their design goals when it comes to refocusing the game on the human aspect and personable nature of the Exalted. Weird bullshit* powers tend to make the focus about the powers, rather than the people who use them and the stories that could be told, which is what the Storyteller system is all about.<br /> <br /> *I use weird bullshit as a term of endearment</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have been more helpful to the discussion if you had been more specific about your disagreement rather than implying &quot;everything I ever wrote in this thread&quot;. Especially since that made you sound like you had insider knowledge. (At least, it sounded that way to me. I'm extremely on-edge this morning for various reasons.)<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could go back and quote a particular suggestion or two which I made, to make your case in refuting them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-12-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:18:47-08:00","id":367569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367454#post367454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what he's saying is that your dreams are so grand that no reality could satisfy in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that this is an opinion you also hold, might you also be kind enough to quote and debate which of my specific wishes seem too grandiose?<br /> <br /> If it is not actually your shared opinion, I apologize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:30:08-08:00","id":367686,"title":"","content":"...honestly? After quickly skimming the thread again for proper examples, roughly 2/3rds of the stuff you said you (and a lot of other people) wanted is in the territory of &quot;outrageous superpowers&quot;, rather than &quot;expressions of attributes&quot;. Given how we seem to be moving away from the former and closer to the latter, not everything you (and a lot of other people) said is unlikely, but a decent chunk of is.<br /> <br /> I will confess that I had misremembered some things that other people said they wanted as things that you said, so while I stand by my prior statement of disappointment, it probably wont be as severe as I had thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:59:10-08:00","id":367862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars getting favored abilities feels wrong, and Martial Arts isn't an Abillity anymore-it' been replaced in the abillity set with Brawl, and Martial Arts is a separate Mechanic now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have always had at least one favored Ability. Everyone except ordinary mortals and Alchemicals get at least one and Alchemicals lacking Favored Abilities felt weird, like a knee-jerk reaction to the &quot;Always favor Martial Arts&quot; problem that Lunars had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:16:32-08:00","id":367946,"title":"","content":"-Get rid of the Lunar's inferiority complex. SERIOUSLY. The entire Lunar splatbook felt like a diatribe about how much the Lunars suck and everyone else was cooler. That should NEVER be the case for the exalt's OWN SPLATBOOK. Give us a good reason to play a Lunar over another Exalt type, don't spend the whole time talking about all these cooler exalts we could be playing.<br /> <br /> -Most importantly, mechanics that don't suck. Yeah, I know, should be obvious. But it's apparently not.<br /> <br /> -Give Lunars the ability to alter their own strengths on the fly. This is something that makes sense for Lunars since they're shapeshifters, so I'm kind of surprised it's not there: charms that allow the Lunar to switch up their attribute points. Maybe make it so they can only alter their caste and favored abilities?<br /> <br /> -Lunar's blood as a charm component. In particular, I'm thinking about creating beastmen from the Lunar's blood. Picture it: under the full moon in a ruined temple, a cult meets to pray to their patron diety. At the height of their ceremony, the candles suddenly blow out, leaving only a shaft of moonlight from the ruined roof. From the moonlight itself steps a massive beast, with the figure of a woman but the mask and tail of a raccoon. Before her faithful she holds out a cup crafted from the moonlight, filled to the brim with her blood. Each member of the congregation takes a sip, and they are transformed.<br /> <br /> ... it's a work in progress, I'm just trying to reconcile how any Celestial with a brain decided needing an entire year of bestiality to create an army was the most efficient solution.<br /> <br /> -If any Lunar at any point says some variation of &quot;Everywhere you are weak, I am strong.&quot; or &quot;If I cannot outfight them, I will outsmart them. If I cannot outsmart them, I will outfight them!&quot; I will be happy.<br /> <br /> -Sublime Danger's perspective on the Sword Sage comic's events. Seriously, so many implications from that story.<br /> <br /> -One of the few things I liked about the 2e book was the idea that the Lunars were Creation's shield wall against the Wyld, its defense against everything that didn't exist. Yes, I know the Fae aren't as big of a threat anymore and there's not as much need for someone to defend the borders of creation, but it was still a cool concept that I was thoroughly intrigued by. I'd like it to be a bigger thing in the Lunar splatbook, even if only as a fluff thing rather than as a player thing. Maybe an endgame where the Lunar gains enough power to fight alone at the edge of the Wyld, or offering this as an explanation for why so many lunars were away from their solar mates at the time of the usurpation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:28:02-08:00","id":367951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367946#post367946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Give Lunars the ability to alter their own strengths on the fly. This is something that makes sense for Lunars since they're shapeshifters, so I'm kind of surprised it's not there: charms that allow the Lunar to switch up their attribute points. Maybe make it so they can only alter their caste and favored abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not quite that kind of shapeshifter. They capitalize on their power, rather than spreading it around. It works for the kind of monster that they were based off of in the cWoD because Body Shift isn't competing with common and more effective Excellency-esque effects (the most you'll likely be able to add to a pool is three dice, and only if you have Channel, Flame Dance or the like). Because Lunar Charms are so heavily dependent on Attribute ratings and we do have Excellencies for them, this sort of effect is likely to stay with the Mountain Folk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -One of the few things I liked about the 2e book was the idea that the Lunars were Creation's shield wall against the Wyld, its defense against everything that didn't exist. Yes, I know the Fae aren't as big of a threat anymore and there's not as much need for someone to defend the borders of creation, but it was still a cool concept that I was thoroughly intrigued by. I'd like it to be a bigger thing in the Lunar splatbook, even if only as a fluff thing rather than as a player thing. Maybe an endgame where the Lunar gains enough power to fight alone at the edge of the Wyld, or offering this as an explanation for why so many lunars were away from their solar mates at the time of the usurpation. </div> </div> </div>They've already confirmed that &quot;Lunars are in the Wyld away from Creation&quot; isn't on the table for being a thing. Lunars will be in Creation, and Fair Folk will have been a formerly unstoppable horde now reduced to a shadow of its former glory by walls of iron thistles, courtesy of the Empress. The fae are broken; no one needs, strictly speaking, to defend Creation from them as a whole. You might need to protect a place from a raksha and attendant retinue, but not from a contingent of nameless hordes that have boiled over the bordermarches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:54:05-08:00","id":367988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367951#post367951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not quite that kind of shapeshifter. They capitalize on their power, rather than spreading it around. It works for the kind of monster that they were based off of in the cWoD because Body Shift isn't competing with common and more effective Excellency-esque effects (the most you'll likely be able to add to a pool is three dice, and only if you have Channel, Flame Dance or the like). Because Lunar Charms are so heavily dependent on Attribute ratings and we do have Excellencies for them, this sort of effect is likely to stay with the Mountain Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are supposed to be the most adaptable of the Exalted though, right? Being able to shift around their abilities would fit with that theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:15:09-08:00","id":368151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367988#post367988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars are supposed to be the most adaptable of the Exalted though, right? Being able to shift around their abilities would fit with that theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if &quot;most adaptable&quot; can really be counted on as a theme. Some enhanced adaptability can probably come about as a result of themes, but it's probably not a thing that you can point to as a design goal. They're certainly more open to basic competency across a wider array of tasks than Solars, but that's a result of having Attribute-based Charms and Excellencies that number far fewer and cover more ground, which is space they share with other Attribute-based Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:22:41-08:00","id":368295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar adaptability is probably going to be more like &quot;I need to be faster, but I'm already at the peak of what I can do with my supernaturally enhanced speed. Good thing I ate that cheetah&quot;<br /> <br /> Or perhaps &quot;I need to be more beautiful. Good thing I had sex with that goddess of beauty and lust&quot;<br /> <br /> Or even &quot;I need to be stronger. Good thing I defeated that blood ape in a duel*&quot;<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\">This one's a maybe</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Blood apes are indeed mighty, but elephants, tyrant lizards and siege lizards are more powerful by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:43:58-08:00","id":368306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368295#post368295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood apes are indeed mighty, but elephants, tyrant lizards and siege lizards are more powerful by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, and all with different capacities to leverage that power, and plausibly different downsides between them. If manual dexterity and/or mobility (climb, Erymanthoi, climb!) are valued beyond the raw difference in power -- or enormous weight and/or size are notable downsides in that context -- going ape could be a winning move. If those aren't really concerns, then get to scaling up! Or knock something across your home plate! ... Or, uh... don't forget to pack ya derm,* I guess. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> * i dont know what that is or why it needed to get out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T05:38:05-08:00","id":368534,"title":"","content":"HT, if you refuse to unlearn all these preconceptions, you're gonna have a problem with Ex3's Lunars, no matter how good they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:40:00-08:00","id":368603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368534#post368534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HT, if you refuse to unlearn all these preconceptions, you're gonna have a problem with Ex3's Lunars, no matter how good they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's refusing? &gt;.&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:54:37-08:00","id":368743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=367686#post367686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...honestly? After quickly skimming the thread again for proper examples, roughly 2/3rds of the stuff you said you (and a lot of other people) wanted is in the territory of &quot;outrageous superpowers&quot;, rather than &quot;expressions of attributes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Lunars are limited solely to &quot;expression of Attributes&quot;, then they're Silver Solars and shouldn't have Spirit Shapes or Heart's Blood shapeshifting, neither of which map directly to &quot;expressions of any particular Attribute&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, for the most part I've deliberately avoided such concepts for this wishlist because I don't know how Lunar Charms are supposed to work, in general. I just know the outrageous things I think they should be able to do, <i>on top</i> of those &quot;Attribute +&quot; tricks.<br /> <br /> That's why the most anyone has said about Lunar Strength is SOS's comment on getting a proper &quot;hulking out&quot; Charm. Because we can at least be fairly sure that Lunars might have a Strength Increasing Exercise equivalent that justifies its effect through the Lunar experiencing a sudden and dramatic growth in muscle mass.<br /> <br /> Conversely, no one is really sure about Graceful Crane Stance, so no one has mentioned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:42:13-08:00","id":368912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368603#post368603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's refusing? &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>We've only had this discussion about the feasibility, relevance, practicality, logic, et cetera., of three hundred individuals &quot;holding back&quot; an effectively-infinite enemy across a border tens of thousands of miles long and hundreds or thousands of miles deep, what, a dozen times now? Yet still every time anyone mentions Lunars, you're there to ask for <i>exactly</i> that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-13-2015, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T13:54:35-08:00","id":368922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368912#post368912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've only had this discussion about the feasibility, practicality, logic, et cetera., of three hundred individuals &quot;holding back&quot; an effectively-infinite enemy across a border tens of thousands of miles long and hundreds or thousands of miles deep, what, a dozen times now? Yet still every time anyone mentions Lunars, you're there to ask for <i>exactly</i> that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alucard, there is a Creation-sized gap between 'this thing I like isn't in this' and 'this sucks harder than Cthulu having a lollipop'. I am perfectly willing to accept that the Lunars aren't the shield wall idea that i like. I'll lament that it's not there, sure, but so long as the Lunars are good it's not going to ruin their splat OR the game as a whole (hell, I prefer Solars, Alchemicals and Dragonblooded anyway if we're just going by fluff). I keep bringing it up because it was basically the ONLY thing in the entire 2e Lunar splatbook that DIDN'T suck.<br /> <br /> Also, of those dozens of discussions, I'm pretty sure this is the only one that specifically deals with 3e. MAYBE there's one other.<br /> <br /> (also also, you have yet to explain to me how and why the Fae simultaneously have this infinite army and yet are too small of a threat to require a shield wall against them after the Balorian Crusade. I don't care how many the Scarlet Empress killed, you can't even put a dent in 'infinity' by sheer definition of the word. It's either an infinite army that got pushed back a bit or a really really big one that got blown up, make up your mind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:09:15-08:00","id":368956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368922#post368922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(also also, you have yet to explain to me how and why the Fae simultaneously have this infinite army and yet are too small of a threat to require a shield wall against them after the Balorian Crusade. I don't care how many the Scarlet Empress killed, you can't even put a dent in 'infinity' by sheer definition of the word. It's either an infinite army that got pushed back a bit or a really really big one that got blown up, make up your mind)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://m.facebook.com/notes/exalted-second-edition/ink-monkeys-vol-43-chapter-seven-fair-folk/10150091728316654/\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> may make for some enlightening -- and fun -- reading, if you've not caught it before. Though, per the cliff's notes version, the latter of the two cases you outlined is likely more accurate. Unless the hannya get a taste for Creation, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:25:51-08:00","id":368967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368922#post368922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alucard, there is a Creation-sized gap between 'this thing I like isn't in this' and 'this sucks harder than Cthulu having a lollipop'. I am perfectly willing to accept that the Lunars aren't the shield wall idea that i like. I'll lament that it's not there, sure, but so long as the Lunars are good it's not going to ruin their splat OR the game as a whole (hell, I prefer Solars, Alchemicals and Dragonblooded anyway if we're just going by fluff). I keep bringing it up because it was basically the ONLY thing in the entire 2e Lunar splatbook that DIDN'T suck.<br /> <br /> Also, of those dozens of discussions, I'm pretty sure this is the only one that specifically deals with 3e. MAYBE there's one other.<br /> <br /> (also also, you have yet to explain to me how and why the Fae simultaneously have this infinite army and yet are too small of a threat to require a shield wall against them after the Balorian Crusade. I don't care how many the Scarlet Empress killed, you can't even put a dent in 'infinity' by sheer definition of the word. It's either an infinite army that got pushed back a bit or a really really big one that got blown up, make up your mind)</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about different points in time. As indicated in the link that Gaius provided, before hand, there was a vast throng (though not infinite) that would easily flow past the mere few Lunars that would have to police squares four hundred miles to a side, minimum, in order to catch interlopers. After? Don't bother guarding the borders, because you'll wait forever and not really come up with anything. Better to just go and bait the Realm so that you don't have to wait forever for that to fall down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:30:09-08:00","id":368973,"title":"","content":"You'll note I said <i>effectively</i> infinite. And do you not remember my beach analogy? From the perspective of me as an armed beach-comber, there might as well be an infinite number of jellyfish in the ocean; no matter how many I stab when they wash up on the beach, more will wash up tomorrow. I still have to tread carefully on the beach, because the things are still venomous, but they're the ones in a hostile environment that <i>will</i> eventually kill them, so the idea that <i>because I'm a human with a sword, I am obligated to patrol the entire coastline of California by myself and stab them</i> is a hard sell at best.<br /> <br /> If my wife died from a jellyfish sting or something, that's a different story. &quot;You have the power to stop it from happening to someone else&quot; and all. <br /> <br /> There's an (effectively-) infinite number of jellyfish in the ocean, but the tide can only bring in so many; one wave is not going to blanket the sands with a carpet of jellyfish five feet high. The Balorian Crusade was a massive hurricane, the like of which had never been seen before. And when the hurricane hits, you'll have far worse things than washed-up jellyfish to worry about.<br /> <br /> My fifteen-hundredth post here, and it's about jellyfish on a beach. This amuses me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-13-2015, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:41:55-08:00","id":368979,"title":"","content":"I'm with Alucard. Without massive armies, Lunars can not be stated to be an effective defense against the armies of the pre-Crusade or Crusade era Fair Folk. Post-Crusade, they are a broken, trapped people who are only a threat to local areas of Creation, not an existential threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:59:45-08:00","id":368995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368973#post368973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note I said <i>effectively</i> infinite. And do you not remember my beach analogy? From the perspective of me as an armed beach-comber, there might as well be an infinite number of jellyfish in the ocean; no matter how many I stab when they wash up on the beach, more will wash up tomorrow. I still have to tread carefully on the beach, because the things are still venomous, but they're the ones in a hostile environment that <i>will</i> eventually kill them, so the idea that <i>because I'm a human with a sword, I am obligated to patrol the entire coastline of California by myself and stab them</i> is a hard sell at best.<br /> <br /> If my wife died from a jellyfish sting or something, that's a different story. &quot;You have the power to stop it from happening to someone else&quot; and all.<br /> <br /> There's an (effectively-) infinite number of jellyfish in the ocean, but the tide can only bring in so many; one wave is not going to blanket the sands with a carpet of jellyfish five feet high. The Balorian Crusade was a massive hurricane, the like of which had never been seen before. And when the hurricane hits, you'll have far worse things than washed-up jellyfish to worry about.<br /> <br /> My fifteen-hundredth post here, and it's about jellyfish on a beach. This amuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to debate this with you, Count. I've already said I'm fine with it if it's not in the Lunar splat (something I only had to say because you assumed it was such in the first place). If all you're going to do is tell me the idea is stupid and I should shut up, don't bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:42:16-08:00","id":369073,"title":"","content":"It's all off topic anyway.<br /> <br /> Wishes, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:51:40-08:00","id":369087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369073#post369073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all off topic anyway.<br /> <br /> Wishes, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>This <i>is</i> a wish; I want Lunar players PCs to not be guilted for choosing &quot;not stabbing fae&quot; as his life's devotion, even in a Shogunate game. In part that means &quot;stabbing fae&quot; be outside the Lunar job descriptor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:45:29-08:00","id":369146,"title":"","content":"Come on guys, #notAllFae are reality-ravishing monsters that treat humans like puppets, there are <i>some</i> good ones.<br /> <br /> I kinda hope Lunars have an avenue for getting grace-related magic (not necessarily Grace Magic specifically mind you). I always liked the idea of Lunars having access to the fae's toys or playground in more ways than just &quot;familiars can be behemoths&quot;. <br /> <br /> Unless their depiction in 3e makes that irrelevant... which I'm kinda hoping it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:58:31-08:00","id":369165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=368743#post368743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are limited solely to &quot;expression of Attributes&quot;, then they're Silver Solars and shouldn't have Spirit Shapes or Heart's Blood shapeshifting, neither of which map directly to &quot;expressions of any particular Attribute&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, for the most part I've deliberately avoided such concepts for this wishlist because I don't know how Lunar Charms are supposed to work, in general. I just know the outrageous things I think they should be able to do, <i>on top</i> of those &quot;Attribute +&quot; tricks.<br /> <br /> That's why the most anyone has said about Lunar Strength is SOS's comment on getting a proper &quot;hulking out&quot; Charm. Because we can at least be fairly sure that Lunars might have a Strength Increasing Exercise equivalent that justifies its effect through the Lunar experiencing a sudden and dramatic growth in muscle mass.<br /> <br /> Conversely, no one is really sure about Graceful Crane Stance, so no one has mentioned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt very much that A: Lunars will only have attribute charms, and B: that they'll somehow be silver solar charms again. Solar, Sidereal or Dragon Blooded charms are all expressions of their abilities, yet they are very distinct because they are abilities filtered through the lens of the sun, stars or the five elements, respectively. I fully expect a similar situation with Lunars, their charms will be expressions of attributes, filtered through the lens of the moon. What we know so far about Lunar powers is that they are highly physical and focused inward. Those two things in and of themselves make it very hard for it to just make silver solars, but it also makes it hard to justify all the stage and esoteric powers that people seem to want lunars to have.<br /> <br /> So, while I will certainly encourage you and my own friends who are Lunar fans to be excited about their 3E version, I will caution that the enthusiasm I'm seeing be tempered, just a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:27:41-08:00","id":369308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369165#post369165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt very much that A: Lunars will only have attribute charms</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think Knacks might still have a place. Unless you meant something else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and B: that they'll somehow be silver solar charms again. </div> </div> </div>So do I. What's your point?<br /> <br /> Look, if people put together a wish list for Solars (and they probably did, a year ago) you would see just as much &quot;crazy shit&quot; on that list as this one. No one is going to ask specifically for all the little tricks like Dipping Swallow Defense or Bulwark Stance, or even waste time summing up such Charms with a wish like &quot;I want Solars to be Good At Swords&quot;. That tamer sort of shit is just <i>assumed</i>; taken for granted.<br /> <br /> People will instead ask for Wyld Shaping Technique, Eagle Wing Style, Blazing Solar Bolt, Perfected Celestial Array... Stuff like that. <br /> <br /> Why should you expect any different for a Lunar wish list?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fully expect a similar situation with Lunars, their charms will be expressions of attributes, filtered through the lens of the moon. </div> </div> </div>Hence the Charisma Charm that lets you scratch or piss on something to create a terror effect. Or the Appearance/Manipulation Charms that let you fake wounds or conceal them. Or the Intelligence Charm that represents a skill-independent talent for working with materials that used to be living plants or creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-13-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:39:36-08:00","id":369320,"title":"","content":"I think the territory marking and protection ideas serve better into some kind of geomantic practice that Lunars namely employ, rather than a charm set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:57:54-08:00","id":369335,"title":"","content":"Just like how some Solar charms are being rationalized as stuff the UCS can do, rather than just a feat of superhuman ability, I want Lunar charms have the same for what Luna can do. Cut the wyld with your blade, bear a cloak of night around you, things that add to the Lunarness, while helping develop Luna itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:04:15-08:00","id":369342,"title":"","content":"Also, I wish for the Lunar moonsilver tattoos to be reflexively hidden, but emerge glowing as the Lunar's anime gets stronger, starting from the castemark, and bleeding out, as if drawing itself on the skin. Moonsilver is a very protean material as far as we know, and so it should be able to shift within the body, emerging, hiding, moving, and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:05:22-08:00","id":369344,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the &quot;territory&quot; charms in Lunars and constructed a number of various other ones. Charms that would let you summon up landmarks or features or creatures from your territory, or that would let you travel back there quickly, or which would allow you to spy on anything and everything inside of it, etc.<br /> <br /> The base charms were, admittedly boring, but I think there's enough in the concept to be salvageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:08:27-08:00","id":369347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369308#post369308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think Knacks might still have a place. Unless you meant something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if knacks, as a thing in and of themselves, don't come back. With the Eclipse-alikes no longer being able grab any charm they want, the mechanical feature known as knacks may no longer needed. Shapeshifting will return, though, that's already been confirmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369308#post369308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do I. What's your point?<br /> <br /> Look, if people put together a wish list for Solars (and they probably did, a year ago) you would see just as much &quot;crazy shit&quot; on that list as this one. No one is going to ask specifically for all the little tricks like Dipping Swallow Defense or Bulwark Stance, or even waste time summing up such Charms with a wish like &quot;I want Solars to be Good At Swords&quot;. That tamer sort of shit is just <i>assumed</i>; taken for granted.<br /> <br /> People will instead ask for Wyld Shaping Technique, Eagle Wing Style, Blazing Solar Bolt, Perfected Celestial Array... Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Why should you expect any different for a Lunar wish list?<br /> <br /> Hence the Charisma Charm that lets you scratch or piss on something to create a terror effect. Or the Appearance/Manipulation Charms that let you fake wounds or conceal them. Or the Intelligence Charm that represents a skill-independent talent for working with materials that used to be living plants or creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that all those things is that, while they may require you to look at the a little sideways, they are still rooted in the themes of &quot;the sun&quot; &quot;human skill&quot; and &quot;perfection&quot;<br /> <br /> The only thing we know currently about Lunar thematics is that they are based on &quot;personal physicality&quot; &quot;being seen&quot; and presumably &quot;the moon&quot;. A piss based terror field, faking wounds and arbitrary skill at working with plant and animal bits does not fit within that design space.<br /> <br /> And frankly, on a personal note, I find piss based charms to be fucking stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T21:35:46-08:00","id":369415,"title":"","content":"Edit: never mind, i misinterpreted which charm you were talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-14-2015, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T00:05:19-08:00","id":369534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369347#post369347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing we know currently about Lunar thematics is that they are based on &quot;personal physicality&quot; &quot;being seen&quot; and presumably &quot;the moon&quot;. A piss based terror field, faking wounds and arbitrary skill at working with plant and animal bits does not fit within that design space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terror effect for the moon as a symbol of madness, and faking wounds for Luna as a trickster. We don't know how they're going to present the patroness of the Lunars in Ex3, but I can certainly how those things could, theoretically, make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T10:16:21-08:00","id":369833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369087#post369087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This <i>is</i> a wish; I want Lunar players PCs to not be guilted for choosing &quot;not stabbing fae&quot; as his life's devotion, even in a Shogunate game. In part that means &quot;stabbing fae&quot; be outside the Lunar job descriptor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... no it doesn't &gt;.&gt; No more than 'paragon of sun and virtue' guilts you away from being a hired assassin (you STed that one, if you'll recall) or 'killer of primordials' guilts the players into hunting the Yozis down.<br /> <br /> Lunar Wish: -Get rid of the Lunar inferiority complex that pervaded the entire 2e book.<br /> -... Okay, look, I just want Lunars to not suck. Give us a reason to play them over a Solar or a Dragonblood. That's not too much to ask, is it? I'll drop every other wish I have, just MAKE THEM GOOD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:16:23-08:00","id":369882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &amp;quot;Territory marking&amp;quot; charm might be a bit to much &amp;quot;Chosen of Zoo Tycoon&amp;quot; than &amp;quot;Chosen of Luna&amp;quot; and doens't really seem in theme with Lunar Charms being mostly internal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you own a thing, it is part of you. If it is part of you, it is internal. Lunars are big on making external things internal, if Heart's Blood is anything to go by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:24:58-08:00","id":369885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantises using Martial Arts ability mentioned, implying that Mantis forms or forms incorporating Mantis traits will be good for martial arts</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mostly on point with your other notes, but this one looks like a negatory: in the context of Lunars, animal forms, and martial arts, it was noted that <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)&amp;p=18622986#post18622986\" target=\"_blank\">animals can't perform Martial Arts Charms</a>. Animals having Brawl and Martial Arts seems to be <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)&amp;p=18641765#post18641765\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;just for fun.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of cool Beasties, an Apendix filled with animals and maybe a few minor spirits that Lunars can omnomnom would be nice. And mutations to build beastmen or, if Hybrid Body is stilll around, hybrid bodies with would be nice. </div> </div> </div>I recall some talk that they want to do a good old bestiary at some point, including a big section on animals. Mutations sound like they've been rolled into Merits this go-round, and I agree the Lunars book would be a pretty natural place for some of them to wind up. Ditto the bestiary, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:26:07-08:00","id":369886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369347#post369347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing we know currently about Lunar thematics is that they are based on &amp;quot;personal physicality&amp;quot; &amp;quot;being seen&amp;quot; and presumably &amp;quot;the moon&amp;quot;. A piss based terror field, faking wounds and arbitrary skill at working with plant and animal bits does not fit within that design space.<br /> <br /> And frankly, on a personal note, I find piss based charms to be fucking stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then put up a Keep Out sign.<br /> <br /> The concept isn't about urination, but supplementing ANY action that marks an object to warn people that it belongs to you. Pissing has the advantage of being real easy, but as the urine is washed or evaporated away, the Charm's effect dies with it. That's why a Lunar looking for a more permanent bordermarker will carve marks into large rocks or stone cliff faces.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to ignore the &quot;animal&quot; aesthetics and themes inherent in having Totems, Spirit Shapes, hybrid Warforms, and turning into animals without Charms. That is not going to be the end of &quot;animals&quot; in the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:41:43-08:00","id":370095,"title":"","content":"Having never really gotten into exalted before now, all I can really hope for is speed. Lunars came out right after DB's in 2e right? Here's hoping its after exigents in 3e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:44:10-08:00","id":370227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369885#post369885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall some talk that they want to do a good old bestiary at some point, including a big section on animals. Mutations sound like they've been rolled into Merits this go-round, and I agree the Lunars book would be a pretty natural place for some of them to wind up. Ditto the bestiary, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that at least a fair assortment of such things are in the core book, to help flesh out neat antagonists, familiars, beasts of burden, etc. that can be used for <b>any</b> kind of Exalt whether or not they can shapeshift into such creatures.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:51:19-08:00","id":370238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=369886#post369886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then put up a Keep Out sign.<br /> <br /> The concept isn't about urination, but supplementing ANY action that marks an object to warn people that it belongs to you. Pissing has the advantage of being real easy, but as the urine is washed or evaporated away, the Charm's effect dies with it. That's why a Lunar looking for a more permanent bordermarker will carve marks into large rocks or stone cliff faces.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to ignore the &quot;animal&quot; aesthetics and themes inherent in having Totems, Spirit Shapes, hybrid Warforms, and turning into animals without Charms. That is not going to be the end of &quot;animals&quot; in the Lunar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>...have you read the developer commentary about their plans for Lunars? At all? Both of those things have been directly contradicted by one dev or another saying &quot;this is/isn't how Lunars operate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted, they are several months / over a year old, so things might have changed, but I get the feeling that for the purpose of this wishlist, you're coming at this at an angle of &quot;this is what I want, regardless of any statements to the contrary&quot;, rather than &quot;this is what I want, that is within the bounds of what I already know.&quot; Which is why I keep saying you might want to temper your expectations just a bit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:31:25-08:00","id":370281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Gaius: No, but not every martial arts thingy is a Charm this go around-Mortals get techniques, Exalts get the charms derieved from them-I expect that Mantises will be able to use techniques, or that a mantis totem might have a Keyword that makes martial arts abillties easier, or maybe even have a few martial arts techniues of it's own that a Lunar can learn to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't really my expectation. Given that &quot;just for fun&quot; quote, I'd be wary of reading too much into some animals having Brawl while others have Martial Arts. Likewise, while the first answer specified, &quot;Martial Arts Charms,&quot; it led with a &quot;no,&quot; to a couple of much more general questions about Lunars benefiting from an animal form, re: Martial Arts. This isn't to say you're wrong, mind -- the data we have isn't exactly complete and crystal clear one way or the other. Simply that this isn't something I feel much confidence in seeing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/338242-lunar-wishlist?p=370227#post370227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that at least a fair assortment of such things are in the core book, to help flesh out neat antagonists, familiars, beasts of burden, etc. that can be used for <b>any</b> kind of Exalt whether or not they can shapeshift into such creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a given that there will be. They've spoiled some of the Merits that can function as mutations and indicated that a number of animals and other creatures will show up in the core book (we got a Hungry Ghost spoiled in a KS Update, for instance). There's just only so much room in the core book, given all the other stuff competing for wordcount.<br /> <br /> Also, as Rater reminded me of that &quot;spirit shape system of keywords for Charm tree reordering, etc.&quot; idea John mentioned forever ago, my wishlist includes a hope that mythic and metaphorical aspects will be valid associations in such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:10:09-08:00","id":371046,"title":"","content":"So, we've wandered away from Wishes again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, there's a new video/PC game coming out called &quot;Evolve&quot;, which is the only game in my life I've rushed to pre-order. It's a brand-new step forward into the realm of &quot;asymmetric gameplay&quot; design, where four players control First Person Shooter &quot;hunters&quot; against a single player controlling a Third Person Smasher &quot;monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> While the hunters have limited-battery-life jetpacks to help them navigate the mountains and valleys of the map, the monster can quickly climb over obstacles, leap down cliffs, and race across flat surfaces faster than the hunters can run. The Trapper hunter class is vital for its movement-restricting and monster-tracking abilities, because otherwise there would never be any catching the monster, which can easily break away and escape from a fight that goes bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heart's Blood shapeshifting already makes it easy for Lunars to turn a single battle into a series of battles interspersed by contested Survival rolls, after the Lunar has run away and covered his tracks while the Wyld Hunt tried desperately to find his hiding place before he recovers or disappears entirely. But I'd never the less like to see Lunar Charms emphasize and encourage this sort of hit-and-run, guerrilla warfare strategy.<br /> <br /> Charms that reward you or enhance your success at setting up ambush after ambush after ambush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:38:37-08:00","id":371137,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I certainly would like for the territory charms to return, mostly because being able to say &quot;This is mine, fuck off&quot; and have the world itself acknowledge it as fact was pretty cool and thematic, and also useful for making the Realm suffer for trying to pull their usual brand of military adventurism on your turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T10:48:33-08:00","id":371230,"title":"","content":"Back for another wish.<br /> <br /> I watched Ninja Scroll again today, a classic Exalted inspiration, and I'd like many of the abilities depicted available in Exalted. For Lunars particular, I want to be able to integrate creatures into my tattoos that emerge and attack for me, maybe a cool familiar charm? Also I want to be able to create decoys of myself or my shapes from cast off &quot;skin&quot; and essence, and fill them with my vermin or creature of choice, like snakes in Ninja Scroll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T21:57:44-08:00","id":380735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Intelligence charms that let you absorb the memories of heartsblood prey are a thing, then &quot;Lunar omnomnomed on a sorcerer/thaumaturgist/spirit/other relevant occultist and absorbed relevant knowledge from them&quot; should totally be a valid path of Sorcerous initiation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In addition to this, charms that let you supplement your abilities a shape's or adding them onto your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T09:31:11-08:00","id":381065,"title":"","content":"Lunars should not have anything comparable to Wyld Shaping Technique. But I feel there's a middle-ground between Wyld-Shaping Technique and Ritual of Lunar Stability that hasn't been sufficiently explored.<br /> <br /> Lunars can't create permanent, ordered lands out of the Wyld? Fine. But could Lunars at least have the power to reshape the local Wyld into a particular brand of wonderland more favorable to them than to their enemies?<br /> <br /> Preferably with the ability to use Ritual of Lunar Stability not only to protect Creation from the Wyld, but to prevent raksha from trying to change altered stretches of Wyld into something unfavorable to the Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I said earlier, Creation's history is being rewritten such that the Lunars actually fit within it, and so they do not need to be swept under the Wyld rug until the setting is ready for them to sudden start existing. Previously, Lunar history was written so that the Wyld pretty much stomped all over them, and Lunar Charms had to be written such that this made sense. Previously, Chimerism was made worse and more important than the Lunar Great Curse.<br /> <br /> That's not the case anymore. Now the Wyld Hunt and Sidereals are the chief historical dangers to the Lunar Exalted. Now the Lunars broke their own Castes themselves as a deliberate action to reinvent themselves for their new circumstances. Now Chimerism is similarly deliberate, and the Great Curse is the proper source of horror. Now the Lunars can be allowed to resist the Wyld more completely than before.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certainly not asking for the return of the Wyld keyword, but the Solar Exalted never needed that keyword to have good reasons for seeking out the Wyld, nor to have the power to make it their bitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-25-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}